er motor has reached. A fault disables 4WD shifting until the switch or wiring is repaired.",[["h","Encoder position switch contacts worn"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"],["l","Internal control module fault"]],["ABS warning light on","ESC/stability control deactivated","Possible reduced brake assist"],["medium",[150,900]],"l"],"C0551":["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit/Open","Open circuit on the longitudinal acceleration sensor (used by ESP/ESC for braking-direction stability).",[["h","Wiring open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["ABS warning light on","ESC/stability control deactivated","Possible reduced brake assist"],["medium",[150,1200]],"l"],"C0552":["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Range/Performance","Longitudinal acceleration sensor reading implausible.",[["h","Sensor reading drifted"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["ABS warning light on","ESC/stability control deactivated","Possible reduced brake assist"],["medium",[150,1200]],"l"],"C0553":["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit Low","Longitudinal accel sensor signal voltage below expected range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["ABS warning light on","ESC/stability control deactivated","Possible reduced brake assist"],["medium",[150,1200]],"l"],"C0554":["Longitudinal Acceleration Sensor Circuit High","Longitudinal accel sensor signal voltage above expected range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",