mbalance.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 11 dripping or leaking"],["m","Injector with excessive flow (worn seat or needle)"],["l","Wrong injector correction code after replacement"],["l","Injector circuit short (extended activation)"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Higher consumption, smoke or fuel smell"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02C4":["Cylinder 11 - Injector Restricted","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Deposits or coking at the nozzle of cylinder 11"],["m","Nozzle needle sticking"],["m","Contaminated fuel or water"],["m","Injector circuit high-resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Lack of power, higher consumption or smoke"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02C5":["Cylinder 11 - Injector Leaking","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Nozzle seat or needle of the cylinder 11 injector leaking"],["m","Deposits keeping the needle from closing fully"],["l","Rail pressure too high"],["l","Wrong or wrongly coded injector"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Smoke, fuel smell, knocking"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02C6":["Cylinder 12 - Fuel Trim at Max Limit","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 12 coked or partly clogged"],["m","Compression loss in this cylinder (valve, rings, leak at injector or glow plug)"],["m","Injector circuit high-resistance or connector"],["m","Petrol: false air at this cylinder's intake (manifold gasket)"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Lack of power, possibly misfire"],["medium",[100,900]],"c"],"P02C7":["Cylinder 12 - Fuel Trim at Min Limit","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 12 dripping or leaking"],["m","Injector with excessive flow (worn seat or needle)"],["l","Wrong injector correction code after replacement"],["l","Injector circuit short (extended activation)"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Higher consumption, smoke or fuel smell"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02C8":["Cylinder 12 - Injector Restricted","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Deposits or coking at the nozzle of cylinder 12"],["m","Nozzle needle sticking"],["m","Contaminated fuel or water"],["m","Injector circuit high-resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Lack of power, higher consumption or smoke"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02C9":["Cylinder 12 - Injector Leaking","These codes belong to an individual-cylinder fuel correction: a diesel's cylinder balance control measures each cylinder's crankshaft acceleration and adjusts its injection quantity; on petrol engines a cylinder-selective mixture control does the same. CARB requires the system to report when such a correction has used up its range or one cylinder causes an imbalance.",[["h","Nozzle seat or needle of the cylinder 12 injector leaking"],["m","Deposits keeping the needle from closing fully"],["l","Rail pressure too high"],["l","Wrong or wrongly coded injector"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, vibration","Smoke, fuel smell, knocking"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P02CA":["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Overboost Condition","Turbocharger B is a second, separately controlled turbo – on twin-turbo or two-stage systems, or one per bank. No manufacturer using the turbo B codes was found; twin-turbo engines such as GM's 3.0 V6 and Ford's 3.5 EcoBoost report boost faults under P0234/P0299 with a shared boost sensor, so the description follows CARB and the turbo A codes.",[["h","Wastegate B stuck closed, linkage seized"],["m","Boost control valve or actuator B faulty, vacuum line swapped or leaking"],["m","Boost sensor reading wrong"],["m","Turbo B vanes sooted (diesel)"]],["Check engine light, reduced power, limp mode","Power cut under load","Possibly knocking (petrol)"],["hard",[150,1800]],"c"],"P02CB":["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Underboost Condition","Turbocharger B is a second, separately controlled turbo – on twin-turbo or two-stage systems, or one per bank. No manufacturer using the turbo B codes was found; twin-turbo engines such as GM's 3.0 V6 and Ford's 3.5 EcoBoost report boost faults under P0234/P0299 with a shared boost sensor, so the description follows CARB and the turbo A codes.",[["h","Charge air leak (hose, cooler, clamp) on side B"],["m","Wastegate B stuck open or control valve faulty"],["m","Turbo B worn (bearing play, compressor wheel)"],["l","Exhaust leak ahead of turbine B"]],["Check engine light on","Clear lack of power","Whistling with a leak, limp mode"],["hard",[50,2000]],"c"],"P02CC":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02CC means the learned correction for cylinder 1 has reached its lower limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much less activation time than nominal – it delivers too much at small quantities or opens early.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 1 leaking or over-delivering at small quantities"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Disturbed crankshaft signal (worn drive belt, tone wheel, dual-mass flywheel)"]],["Check engine light on","Often nothing noticeable; possibly rough idle or knocking","Possibly smoke or higher consumption"],["hard",[0,1200]],"c"],"P02CD":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02CD means the learned correction for cylinder 1 has reached its upper limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much more activation time than nominal – it delivers too little or opens late, for example from coking.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 1 coked or worn (delivers too little)"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Disturbed crankshaft signal (worn drive belt, tone wheel, dual-mass flywheel)"]],["Check engine light on","Often nothing noticeable; possibly rough idle or knocking","Possibly smoke or loss of power"],["hard",[0,1200]],"c"],"P02CE":["Cylinder 2 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02CE means the learned correction for cylinder 2 has reached its lower limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much less activation time than nominal – it delivers too much at small quantities or opens early.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 2 leaking or over-delivering at small quantities"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Disturbed crankshaft signal (worn drive belt, tone wheel, dual-mass flywheel)"]],["Check engine light on","Often nothing noticeable; possibly rough idle or knocking","Possibly smoke or higher consumption"],["hard",[0,1200]],"c"],"P02CF":["Cylinder 2 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02CF means the learned correction for cylinder 2 has reached its upper limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much more activation time than nominal – it delivers too little or opens late, for example from coking.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 2 coked or worn (delivers too little)"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Disturbed crankshaft signal (worn drive belt, tone wheel, dual-mass flywheel)"]],["Check engine light on","Often nothing noticeable; possibly rough idle or knocking","Possibly smoke or loss of power"],["hard",[0,1200]],"c"],"P02D0":["Cylinder 3 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02D0 means the learned correction for cylinder 3 has reached its lower limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much less activation time than nominal – it delivers too much at small quantities or opens early.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 3 leaking or over-delivering at small quantities"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Disturbed crankshaft signal (worn drive belt, tone wheel, dual-mass flywheel)"]],["Check engine light on","Often nothing noticeable; possibly rough idle or knocking","Possibly smoke or higher consumption"],["hard",[0,1200]],"c"],"P02D1":["Cylinder 3 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","The engine module learns a small-quantity correction for each injector: on overrun it gives one injector a tiny test injection (GM about 1.5 mm³), measures the resulting crankshaft acceleration and corrects the injector's activation time per rail pressure step. P02D1 means the learned correction for cylinder 3 has reached its upper limit at at least one pressure step: the injector needs much more activation time than nominal – it delivers too little or opens late, for example from coking.",[["h","Injector of cylinder 3 coked or worn (delivers too little)"],["m","Engine software (update available for some models)"],["m","Injector correction code not or wrongly programmed after replacement"],["l","Distu