ly also U0284"],["easy",[10,300]],"u"],"P05A7":["Active Grille Air Shutter A Supply Voltage Circuit Low","An active grille shutter closes louvres in the grille to cut drag and speed warm-up and opens them for cooling; CARB names it as an off-cycle CO2 technology and treats the actuator as an output component. Smart actuators (Ford 3.0 L diesel, Toyota) check their own coil and supply and report over LIN; simpler ones (VW 1.8 T) have their own supply and a control line from the engine module.",[["h","Contact resistance in connector, wire or ground (corrosion)"],["m","Actuator faulty internally (measuring wrong)"],["l","Weak battery or charging system"]],["Check engine light on","Shutter inoperative at times","Possibly further voltage codes"],["easy",[20,400]],"u"],"P05A8":["Active Grille Air Shutter A Supply Voltage Circuit High","An active grille shutter closes louvres in the grille to cut drag and speed warm-up and opens them for cooling; CARB names it as an off-cycle CO2 technology and treats the actuator as an output component. Smart actuators (Ford 3.0 L diesel, Toyota) check their own coil and supply and report over LIN; simpler ones (VW 1.8 T) have their own supply and a control line from the engine module.",[["m","System overvoltage (regulator, jump start)"],["m","Actuator faulty internally (measuring wrong)"],["l","Supply shorted to another circuit"]],["Check engine light on","Shutter inoperative","Possibly P0563 or further voltage codes"],["medium",[20,450]],"u"],"P05A9":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Position Sensor Circuit","The active grille shutter (A = upper or only shutter, B = second) closes louvres to cut drag and speed warm-up and opens them for cooling; CARB names it as an off-cycle CO2 technology and requires its components to be monitored. A separately evaluated position sensor, as these titles assume, is described in Ford patents (Hall sensor on the motor or sensor on the linkage).",[["h","Position sensor in the actuator faulty (replaced as a unit)"],["h","Actuator connector corroded or with water ingress"],["m","Wire open in the front bumper harness (accident, rodents)"],["l","Engine module or reference voltage"]],["Check engine light on","Shutter stays in one position (usually open) or does not react","Slightly higher consumption, longer warm-up in winter"],["medium",[30,600]],"u"],"P05AA":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The active grille shutter (A = upper or only shutter, B = second) closes louvres to cut drag and speed warm-up and opens them for cooling; CARB names it as an off-cycle CO2 technology and requires its components to be monitored. A separately evaluated position sensor, as these titles assume, is described in Ford patents (Hall sensor on the motor or sensor on the linkage).",[["h","Louvres blocked (ice, snow, debris, bent bracket) – sensor correct, position wrong"],["m","Position sensor in the actuator drifting or worn"],["m","Basic setting not learned after replacement"],["m","Shaft or linkage between motor and louvres broken"]],["Check engine light on","Shutter stays in one position (usually open) or does not react","Slightly higher consumption, longer warm-up in winter"],["medium",[50,600]],"u"],"P05AB":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Position Sensor Circuit High","The active grille shutter (A = upper or only shutter, B = second) closes louvres to cut drag and speed warm-up and opens them for cooling; CARB names it as an off-cycle CO2 technology and requires its components to be monitored. A separately evaluated position sensor, as these titles assume, is described in Ford patents (Hall sensor on the motor or sensor on the linkage).",[["h","Signal shorted to supply or ground line open"],["h","Connector corroded or with water ingress"],["m","Position sensor in the actuator faulty internally"],["l","Engine module"]],["Check engine light on","Shutter stays in one position (usually open) or does not react","Slightly higher consumption, longer warm-up 