e actuator as an output component.",[["h","Debris, stones, ice or snow in the lower shutter"],["h","Louvres unhooked or broken, rubbing on bracket or horn, impact damage"],["m","Water or corrosion in connector or harness"],["m","Actuator B faulty"]],["Check engine light on (GM after two trips)","Lower shutter not moving or incompletely, possibly U0285 or P059F","Higher coolant temperature under load or slightly higher consumption"],["medium",[0,500]],"u"],"P05AF":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Stuck On","Shutter B is the second active grille shutter – at GM, Ford and Stellantis the lower one in the bumper. Shutters cut drag and speed warm-up when closed and open for cooling; CARB names them as an off-cycle CO2 technology and treats the actuator as an output component.",[["h","Engine module software (sporadic false message)"],["m","Louvres blocked open (ice, dirt, debris, accident damage)"],["m","Actuator or shutter unit B faulty"],["l","Poor supply or ground at the actuator"]],["Check engine light on","Grille shutter warning, top speed limited (Audi)","Longer warm-up, slightly higher consumption"],["medium",[0,500]],"u"],"P05B0":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Position Sensor Minimum/Maximum Stop Performance","Shutter B is the second active grille shutter – at GM, Ford and Stellantis the lower one in the bumper. Shutters cut drag and speed warm-up when closed and open for cooling; CARB names them as an off-cycle CO2 technology and treats the actuator as an output component.",[["h","Lower shutter or actuator faulty"],["m","Louvres blocked or bent (ice, stone chips, impact)"],["m","Shutter misassembled or connector off after repair"],["l","Connector or harness corroded"]],["Check engine light on","Lower shutter not moving fully","Possibly also P05AE"],["medium",[100,500]],"u"],"P05B1":["Active Grille Air Shutter B Control Circuit/Open","Shutter B is the second active grille shutter – at GM, Ford and Stellantis the lower one in the bumper. Shutters cut drag and speed warm