ark position sensor/switch reports the park request or position. On GM's shift-by-wire selectors (2017 LaCrosse, XT4/XT5, Bolt EV, later SUVs and pickups) it is the P button, read by two redundant analog sensors A and B with separate 'released' and 'pressed' voltage zones.",[["h","P button sensor faulty or worn"],["m","Knob not seated, button sticking"],["m","Contact resistance in the connector"],["l","Module software"]],["Check engine light, 'service transmission' or 'unable to shift' message","Park cannot be selected by button, or the car will not shift out of P","P button illumination off"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P07BD":["Transmission Park Position Sensor/Switch B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","With electronic gear selection the park position sensor/switch reports the park request or position. On GM's shift-by-wire selectors (2017 LaCrosse, XT4/XT5, Bolt EV, later SUVs and pickups) it is the P button, read by two redundant analog sensors A and B with separate 'released' and 'pressed' voltage zones.",[["h","Loose contact in the selector connector or harness"],["m","Sensor with intermittent fault"],["l","Off-centre pressing or a hand resting on the button"]],["Check engine light, 'service transmission' or 'unable to shift' message","Park cannot be selected by button, or the car will not shift out of P","P button illumination off"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P07BE":["Transmission Park Position Sensor/Switch A/B Correlation","With electronic gear selection the park position sensor/switch reports the park request or position. On GM's shift-by-wire selectors (2017 LaCrosse, XT4/XT5, Bolt EV, later SUVs and pickups) it is the P button, read by two redundant analog sensors A and B with separate 'released' and 'pressed' voltage zones.",[["h","Off-centre pressing or a hand resting on the P button"],["m","Control module software"],["m","One of the two sensors faulty or sticking"],["l","Shift knob worn or not seated"]],["Check engine light, 'service transmission' or 'unable to shift' message","Park cannot be selected by button, or the car will not shift out of P","P button illumination off"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P07BF":["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","These low/high codes are a purely electrical check of the sensor's signal voltage at the module and run even with the vehicle at rest – unlike the circuit, range, no-signal and intermittent codes, which evaluate speed while driving. Low means a short to ground, high a short to supply or, depending on the circuit, an open.",[["h","Signal or supply wire shorted to ground (chafing at the case)"],["m","Sensor shorted internally"],["m","Oil or moisture in the connector"],["l","Module input faulty"]],["Check engine light (GM after one trip)","Limp mode, harsh shifts, no converter lock-up","Adaption frozen"],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P07C0":["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor A Circuit High","These low/high codes are a purely electrical check of the sensor's signal voltage at the module and run even with the vehicle at rest – unlike the circuit, range, no-signal and intermittent codes, which evaluate speed while driving. Low means a short to ground, high a short to supply or, depending on the circuit, an open.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Open circuit or broken wire inside the sensor"],["m","Corroded connector"],["l","Module input faulty"]],["Check engine light (GM after one trip)","Limp mode, harsh shifts, no converter lock-up","Adaption frozen"],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P07C1":["Input/Turbine Shaft Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","These low/high codes are a purely electrical check of the sensor's signal voltage at the module and run even with the vehicle at rest – unlike the circuit, range, no-signal and intermittent codes, which evaluate speed while driving. Low means a short to ground, high a short to supply or, depending on the circuit, an open.",[["h","Signal or supply wire shorted to ground (chafing at the case)"],["m","Sensor shorted internally"],[