 shutdown"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF3":["Drive Motor C Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The ECM detects a range/performance fault on the drive motor c temperature sensor circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor characteristic drifted"],["m","Sensor mounting displaced"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["EV/hybrid system warning light on","Reduced motor power or torque","Possible limp mode or vehicle shutdown"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF4":["Drive Motor C Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","The ECM detects a low fault on the drive motor c temperature sensor circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal sensor short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["EV/hybrid system warning light on","Reduced motor power or torque","Possible limp mode or vehicle shutdown"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF5":["Drive Motor C Temperature Sensor Circuit High","The ECM detects a high fault on the drive motor c temperature sensor circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["EV/hybrid system warning light on","Reduced motor power or torque","Possible limp mode or vehicle shutdown"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF6":["Drive Motor C Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The ECM detects a intermittent/erratic fault on the drive motor c temperature sensor circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor connector not seated"],["m","Noisy ground reference"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["EV/hybrid system warning light on","Reduced motor power or torque","Possible limp mode or vehicle shutdown"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF7":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor B Circuit","The ECM detects a circuit fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor b circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF8":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","The ECM detects a range/performance fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor b circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor characteristic drifted"],["m","Sensor mounting displaced"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EF9":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor B Circuit Low","The ECM detects a low fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor b circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal sensor short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EFA":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor B Circuit High","The ECM detects a high fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor b circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EFB":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The ECM detects a intermittent/erratic fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor b circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor connector not seated"],["m","Noisy ground reference"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EFC":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor C Circuit","The ECM detects a circuit fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor c circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EFD":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","The ECM detects a range/performance fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor c circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Sensor characteristic drifted"],["m","Sensor mounting displaced"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0EFE":["Battery Charger A Input Voltage Sensor C Circuit Low","The ECM detects a low fault on the battery charger a input voltage sensor c circuit. Reading cannot be used reliably for control.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal sensor short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P0FFF":["Reserved Powertrain Fault","Manufacturer-specific reserved code in the SAE generic range used as catch-all for hybrid system faults that do not map to a more specific defined code. Should be diagnosed using the freeze frame data and any additional manufacturer codes.",[["m","Unspecified hybrid system fault"]],[],["shop_only",[200,5000]],"u"],"P2000":["NOx Adsorber Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","The lean NOx trap (LNT) on bank 1 is no longer storing or releasing NOx within the required efficiency window. Detected by the downstream NOx sensor or model-based monitor — typically caused by sulphur poisoning, thermal aging, or a failed regeneration strategy.",[["h","Sulphur poisoning from high-sulphur fuel — desulphation regeneration not running"],["m","Thermal aging of washcoat after high-temperature exposure"],["m","Downstream NOx sensor reading drifts"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,3500]],"c"],"P2001":["NOx Adsorber Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","The lean NOx trap (LNT) on bank 2 is no longer storing or releasing NOx within the required efficiency window. Detected by the downstream NOx sensor or model-based monitor — typically caused by sulphur poisoning, thermal aging, or a failed regeneration strategy.",[["h","Sulphur poisoning"],["m","Thermal aging of washcoat"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,3500]],"c"],"P2002":["Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","DPF heavily loaded — repeated short trips prevent regeneration"],["m","Filter substrate cracked or melted from runaway regeneration"],["m","Differential pressure sensor drift"],["l","Leak around DPF housing"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2003":["Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","Diesel Particulate Filter Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","DPF heavily loaded — repeated short trips prevent regeneration"],["m","Filter substrate cracked or melted"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2004":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open (Bank 1)","The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flap on bank 1 is stuck in the open position. The IMRC swirls or tumbles intake charge at low rpm by closing one runner per cylinder; when stuck open, low-end torque drops and the engine may misfire on cold starts.",[["h","Carbon buildup blocks flap travel"],["m","IMRC actuator or vacuum motor failed"],["m","Linkage rod broken or disconnected"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2005":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open (Bank 2)","The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flap on bank 2 is stuck in the open position. The IMRC swirls or tumbles intake charge at low rpm by closing one runner per cylinder; when stuck open, low-end torque drops and the engine may misfire on cold starts.",[["h","Carbon buildup blocks flap travel"],["m","IMRC actuator failed on bank 2"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2006":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","The IMRC flap on bank 1 is stuck in the closed position and cannot open at higher rpm. Top-end power suffers because the runner is restricted, and the engine may breathe poorly above mid-range.",[["h","Carbon deposits seize flap closed"],["m","Actuator stuck or vacuum line collapsed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2007":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2006. The IMRC flap on bank 2 cannot return to the open position and chokes intake flow at higher rpm.",[["h","Carbon deposits seize flap closed on bank 2"],["m","Bank 2 actuator stuck"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2008":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Solenoid Circuit Open (Bank 1)","The ECU detects an open circuit on the IMRC solenoid for bank 1. No control current flows when the runner is commanded to switch, leaving the flap in its default position.",[["h","Solenoid coil open"],["m","Connector unplugged or corroded"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["easy",[30,250]],"c"],"P2009":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Solenoid Circuit Low (Bank 1)","The IMRC solenoid drive line for bank 1 reads below the lower threshold — short to ground or a failed driver stage. The runner cannot be switched on demand.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Solenoid internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[30,250]],"c"],"P200A":["Intake Manifold Runner Performance (Bank 1)","The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) on bank 1 reports that flap movement does not match the commanded position within the allowed time window — either too slow, too short a stroke, or position feedback off-target.",[["h","Carbon buildup restricts flap travel"],["m","Actuator weak or vacuum supply low"],["l","Linkage worn — play between actuator and flap"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P200B":["Intake Manifold Runner Performance (Bank 2)","The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) on bank 2 reports that flap movement does not match the commanded position within the allowed time window — either too slow, too short a stroke, or position feedback off-target.",[["h","Carbon buildup"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P200C":["Particulate Filter Over Temperature (Bank 1)","A temperature sensor at the diesel particulate filter (DPF) on bank 1 has exceeded the safe limit — typically during a runaway regeneration. Continued operation can melt or crack the substrate.",[["h","Excessive soot load triggers runaway regeneration"],["m","Post-injection over-fueling during regeneration"],["l","DPF temperature sensor reading drifts high"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"c"],"P200D":["Particulate Filter Over Temperature (Bank 2)","A temperature sensor at the diesel particulate filter (DPF) on bank 2 has exceeded the safe limit — typically during a runaway regeneration. Continued operation can melt or crack the substrate.",[["h","Runaway regeneration"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"c"],"P200E":["Catalyst System Over Temperature (Bank 1)","A temperature sensor in the exhaust catalyst on bank 1 reports a value above the safe operating limit. Sustained over-temperature can sinter the precious-metal washcoat and destroy conversion efficiency.",[["h","Persistent misfire dumps unburned fuel into the cat"],["m","Sustained rich mixture from leaking injector or fuel pressure regulator"],["l","Catalyst temperature sensor drifts high"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3000]],"c"],"P200F":["Catalyst System Over Temperature (Bank 2)","A temperature sensor in the exhaust catalyst on bank 2 reports a value above the safe operating limit. Sustained over-temperature can sinter the precious-metal washcoat and destroy conversion efficiency.",[["h","Misfire dumps fuel into cat"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3000]],"c"],"P2010":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Solenoid Circuit High (Bank 1)","Drive voltage at the IMRC solenoid on bank 1 is above the upper limit — short to supply or an open ground side. The solenoid is energised constantly or the driver protection trips.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["l","ECU driver stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[30,250]],"c"],"P2011":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","The IMRC actuator drive circuit on bank 2 is open or has lost continuity — control module no longer detects a closing path through the actuator winding.",[["h","Open wiring or chafed conductor in IMRC harness"],["m","Connector corroded — high resistance contact"],["m","Actuator solenoid winding open"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2012":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","The IMRC actuator drive line on bank 2 reads below the expected voltage threshold — typically a short to ground or a stuck-low driver inside the control module.",[["h","Short to ground in driver line"],["m","Actuator winding shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2013":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","The IMRC actuator drive line on bank 2 reads above the expected voltage threshold — typically a short to battery voltage or an open ground side.",[["h","Short to B+ in driver line"],["m","Open ground return on actuator"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2014":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 1)","The position feedback signal of the IMRC flap on bank 1 is missing or implausible. Without feedback, the ECU cannot verify that the commanded runner position has been reached.",[["h","Position sensor failed"],["m","Signal wire broken"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2015":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Range/Performance (Bank 1)","The IMRC position sensor on bank 1 reports a value, but it does not match the commanded flap state — for example, the flap is commanded closed yet the sensor still reads open. Common on engines where the connector pin clip wears out and the sensor reads erratic positions.",[["h","Connector clip worn — intermittent contact"],["m","Flap sticking due to carbon"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2016":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 1)","The IMRC position sensor signal on bank 1 reads below the lower limit. Usually a short to ground on the signal wire or a failed sensor.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Position sensor failed low"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2017":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 1)","The IMRC position sensor signal on bank 1 reads above the upper limit. Typically a short to supply, an open ground reference, or a sensor that failed high.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2019":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Range/Performance (Bank 2)","The IMRC position sensor on bank 2 produces an electrically valid signal that does not match the commanded runner state — typically a sensor drift or sticking flap.",[["h","Position sensor drift"],["m","Carbon buildup blocks flap travel"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P201A":["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Unit 1)","Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Unit 1): the signal is implausible or outside the valid range. This valve doses reductant (DEF/AdBlue) into the exhaust for SCR NOx reduction.",[["h","DEF crystallisation clogs the dosing nozzle"],["m","DEF supply pressure below target"],["m","Valve coil ageing — slow response"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P201B":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Supply Voltage Low (Bank 1)","The supply voltage feeding the IMRC actuator on bank 1 is below the lower limit — typically a fuse, relay, or harness fault on the supply rail.",[["h","Supply fuse blown"],["m","Open supply wire"],["m","Supply relay contacts pitted"]],[],["medium",[20,250]],"u"],"P201C":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Supply Voltage Low (Bank 2)","The supply voltage feeding the IMRC actuator on bank 2 is below the lower limit — typically a fuse, relay, or harness fault on the supply rail.",[["h","Supply fuse blown"]],[],["medium",[20,250]],"u"],"P201D":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Internal Performance (Bank 1)","Internal self-diagnostics of the IMRC actuator on bank 1 report an off-spec condition — driver stage, position-feedback or thermal limit no longer matches the calibrated profile.",[["h","Actuator internal driver or sensor fault"],["l","Actuator overheated and derated"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P201E":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Actuator Internal Performance (Bank 2)","Internal self-diagnostics of the IMRC actuator on bank 2 report an off-spec condition — driver stage, position-feedback or thermal limit no longer matches the calibrated profile.",[["h","Internal actuator fault"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P201F":["Reductant Pump A Stuck On","Reductant Pump A Stuck On: the actuator is stuck in the on position.",[["h","Pump relay contacts welded"],["m","Pump driver line shorted to B+"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P2020":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 2)","The IMRC position sensor on bank 2 reports a voltage below the lower threshold — typically a short to ground or a sensor with very low resistance.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor element shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2021":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 2)","The IMRC position sensor on bank 2 reports a voltage above the upper threshold — usually a short to positive or an open ground.",[["h","Signal shorted to positive"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2022":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 2)","The IMRC position sensor on bank 2 reports a signal above the upper plausibility limit — typically an open signal line, broken sensor, or short to B+.",[["h","Open signal line at IMRC position sensor"],["m","Signal shorted to B+"],["m","Sensor element failed"]],[],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2023":["Intake Manifold Runner Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","The IMRC position sensor signal on bank 2 jumps or drops out intermittently — usually a loose pin, partially-broken conductor, or moisture in the connector.",[["h","Loose terminal in connector"],["m","Water ingress into connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[30,250]],"c"],"P2024":["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit","A general fault is reported on the EVAP fuel-vapor temperature sensor circuit — open, shorted, or out of plausible range. The sensor is part of the evaporative-emission system used to monitor canister loading.",[["h","Vapor temperature sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault between sensor and PCM"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2025":["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Performance","The EVAP fuel-vapor temperature sensor reading is plausible but does not match expected behaviour over time or temperature — slow response, incorrect offset, or stuck reading.",[["h","Sensor drift over service life"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2026":["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Voltage","The EVAP fuel-vapor temperature sensor signal sits below the lower plausibility limit — short to ground or short between signal and ground inside the sensor.",[["h","Short to ground on signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[40,300]],"c"],"P2027":["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit High Voltage","The EVAP fuel-vapor temperature sensor signal sits above the upper plausibility limit — open signal line, broken sensor, or short to B+.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[40,300]],"c"],"P2028":["EVAP Fuel Vapor Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent","The EVAP fuel-vapor temperature sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — usually a connector or chafed wire.",[["h","Intermittent connector or chafed wire"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[30,300]],"c"],"P2029":["Fuel Fired Heater Disabled","The fuel-fired auxiliary heater (used to warm coolant or DEF on cold start) has been disabled by the control module — typically because of repeated start failures, low-voltage supply, or a self-protection condition.",[["h","Heater glow plug failed"],["m","Low battery voltage triggered lockout"],["m","Fuel supply starved — empty tank or pump weak"]],[],["medium",[80,1200]],"c"],"P202A":["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit/Open","The DEF tank heater control circuit is open or has lost continuity — the PCM cannot drive the resistive heater that prevents the DEF (urea) tank from freezing in winter.",[["h","Heater element winding open"],["m","Open wire between PCM and heater"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P202B":["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit Low","The DEF tank heater control line reads below the expected voltage — short to ground or stuck-low driver.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P202C":["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit High","The DEF tank heater control line reads above the expected voltage — short to B+ or open ground. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P202D":["Reductant Leakage","A leak has been detected in the DEF (urea) supply system — usually by a pressure-decay test after pump shutdown, or by visible crystallisation around fittings.",[["h","Cracked DEF line or fitting"],["m","Pump seal leaking"],["m","Injector mounting seal leaking"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,1500]],"u"],"P202E":["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Unit 1)","Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Unit 1): the signal is implausible or outside the valid range. This valve doses reductant (DEF/AdBlue) into the exhaust for SCR NOx reduction.",[["h","DEF crystallisation in nozzle"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P202F":["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit Range/Performance","The control line that gates the DEF supply pump or the regeneration heating circuit does not respond as commanded — duty cycle, current draw, or response time off-spec.",[["h","Supply relay aged or pitted contacts"],["m","Supply pump motor brushes worn"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2030":["Fuel Fired Heater Performance","The fuel-fired auxiliary heater is operating but not delivering the expected heat output within the calibrated time — flame sensor reports weak combustion, exhaust temperature does not rise, or coolant heating rate is below threshold.",[["h","Combustion chamber sooted from short cycles"],["m","Flame sensor degraded"]],[],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P2031":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The exhaust gas temperature (EGT) sensor at position 2 on bank 1 — typically downstream of the catalyst or before the DPF — reports an implausible signal. EGT sensors protect the turbocharger and DPF from over-temperature and time the regeneration cycle.",[["h","EGT sensor failed"],["m","Wiring damaged by heat"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2032":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor at bank 1 position 2 reads below the lower limit. Common when the signal is shorted to ground or the sensor element is open.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor element open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2033":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor at bank 1 position 2 reads above the upper limit. Usually a short to supply, an open ground or a sensor that drifted high — risk of false DPF over-temperature limp.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor drift to high reading"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2034":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","A general electrical fault is reported on the exhaust gas temperature (EGT) sensor at bank 2 sensor 2 — open, short, or out of plausibility. EGT sensors monitor catalyst, DPF, and turbocharger inlet/outlet temperatures.",[["h","EGT sensor element failed"],["m","Open wire in EGT harness"],["l","Connector corroded by exhaust heat"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2035":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor on bank 2 sensor 2 reads below the lower plausibility limit — short to ground or shorted sensor element.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2036":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor on bank 2 sensor 2 reads above the upper plausibility limit — open signal or short to B+.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2037":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on reductant injection air-pressure sensor A — used on air-assisted DEF dosing systems to monitor the atomisation air pressure delivered to the injector.",[["h","Air pressure sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault between sensor and PCM"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2038":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor A reads inside the electrical range but does not match expected behaviour over time or load — slow response or wrong offset.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2039":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor A reads below its lower plausibility limit — short to ground or sensor internal short.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P203A":["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on DEF level sensor A — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. Some tanks use multiple level senders to cover irregular tank shapes; this is the primary one.",[["h","Sender failed — float, swing arm, or rheostat"],["m","Harness or connector fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P203B":["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","DEF level sensor A reading is in electrical range but plausibility check fails — value sticks, jumps, or does not match consumption.",[["h","Float arm sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P203C":["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Low","DEF level sensor A reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P203D":["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit High","DEF level sensor A reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P203E":["Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Reductant Level Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic: the signal is intermittent or erratic. Often a loose connector or chafed wiring; a wiggle test often locates it.",[["h","Corroded sender contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P203F":["Reductant Level Too Low","The DEF tank level has dropped below the warning threshold — driver action required to refill before the inducement strategy escalates to limp mode or no-restart.",[["h","DEF tank simply empty — refill needed"],["l","Level sensor under-reading"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[10,60]],"c"],"P2040":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor A reads above its upper plausibility limit — open signal line or short to B+.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2041":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor A signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or harness issue.",[["h","Intermittent connector or chafed wire"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[60,450]],"c"],"P2042":["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on reductant (DEF) temperature sensor A — used to compensate dosing for fluid viscosity and to enable tank heating in winter.",[["h","Sensor element failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2043":["Reductant Temperature Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","Reductant temperature sensor A reading is within electrical range but plausibility check fails — slow response or sticks at one value through a tank-warming cycle.",[["h","Sensor drifts or sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start cou