der vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P205F":["Reductant System Performance (Bank 2)","The DEF system as a whole on bank 2 is not delivering the required NOx reduction — NOx-out remains too high relative to commanded dosing across a drive cycle. Causes range from poor DEF quality, restricted dosing line, weak pump, to a degraded SCR catalyst.",[["h","Poor DEF quality — diluted or contaminated"],["m","SCR catalyst thermally aged"],["m","Crystallisation restricts dosing line"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,4000]],"c"],"P2060":["Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit Low","Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit Low: the control-circuit voltage is below the expected range. This valve doses reductant (DEF/AdBlue) into the exhaust for SCR NOx reduction.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P2061":["Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit High","Reductant Injection Air Pump Control Circuit High: the control-circuit voltage is above the expected range. This valve doses reductant (DEF/AdBlue) into the exhaust for SCR NOx reduction.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P2062":["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit/Open","The control line that energises the DEF supply pump or regeneration heating circuit is open — no continuity through the load or harness.",[["h","Open winding"],["m","Open wire"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2063":["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit Low","Reductant/regeneration supply control line stuck low — short to ground or stuck-low driver. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2064":["Reductant/Regeneration Supply Control Circuit High","Reductant/regeneration supply control line stuck high — short to B+ or open ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2065":["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on the secondary fuel-level sensor (B) — vehicles with saddle tanks or auxiliary tanks use a second sender to cover the full tank volume.",[["h","Sender failed — float, swing arm, or rheostat"],["m","Harness or connector fault"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2066":["Fuel Level Sensor B Performance","Secondary fuel-level sensor B reads within range but plausibility check fails — value sticks, jumps, or does not match consumption.",[["h","Float arm sticks"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2067":["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit Low","Fuel-level sensor B reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2068":["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit High","Fuel-level sensor B reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2069":["Fuel Level Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","Fuel-level sensor B signal jumps or drops out intermittently — usually a corroded sender or wiring. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Corroded sender contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P206A":["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on the DEF (urea) quality sensor — measures urea concentration via ultrasonic or refractive method to detect water dilution or wrong fluid.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P206B":["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","DEF quality sensor reads in range but reports an off-spec urea concentration — typically diluted DEF or non-DEF fluid in the tank.",[["h","DEF diluted with water"],["m","Wrong fluid in DEF tank"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[80,1500]],"c"],"P206C":["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit Low","DEF quality sensor reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P206D":["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit High","DEF quality sensor reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P206E":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2)","Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Carbon buildup blocks flap travel"],["m","Actuator seized"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P206F":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Carbon buildup blocks flap travel"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2070":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1)","Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Carbon buildup"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2071":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Carbon buildup"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2072":["Throttle Actuator Control System - Ice Blockage (Bank 1)","The electronic throttle on bank 1 is jammed by ice — typical at very low ambient temperatures with high humidity, after a short trip that did not warm the throttle housing. The strategy attempts a self-clearing motion before setting the code.",[["h","Ice formed in throttle body"],["m","Throttle housing coolant warming circuit blocked"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[50,500]],"c"],"P2073":["Manifold Absolute Pressure / Mass Air Flow - Throttle Position Correlation at Idle","At idle, the relationship between MAP/MAF and throttle position does not match the calibrated map — typically a vacuum leak, dirty MAF, sticking throttle plate, or sensor drift.",[["h","Vacuum leak — cracked hose, gasket, or PCV"],["m","MAF sensor contaminated"],["m","Carbon buildup at throttle plate"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss, hesitation under acceleration","Rough or unstable idle"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2074":["Manifold Absolute Pressure / Mass Air Flow - Throttle Position Correlation at Higher Load","At higher load, the relationship between MAP/MAF and throttle position does not match the calibrated map — typically a charge-air leak, restricted intake, or wide-open MAF underread.",[["h","Charge-air pipe leak after turbo"],["m","MAF sensor contaminated"],["l","Air filter heavily restricted"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss, hesitation under acceleration","Rough or unstable idle"],["medium",[40,700]],"c"],"P2075":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 1)","A general electrical fault is reported on the IMT valve position sensor at bank 1 — open, short, or out of plausibility.",[["h","Position sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P2076":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1)","IMT valve position sensor at bank 1 reads in range but plausibility check fails — value sticks or does not match commanded position.",[["h","Position feedback sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P2077":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 1)","IMT position sensor at bank 1 reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P2078":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 1)","IMT position sensor at bank 1 reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P2079":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1)","IMT position sensor at bank 1 signal is unstable — connector or harness issue. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P207A":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit (Bank 2)","A general electrical fault is reported on the IMT valve position sensor at bank 2 — open, short, or out of plausibility.",[["h","Position sensor failed"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P207B":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","IMT valve position sensor at bank 2 reads in range but plausibility check fails — value sticks or does not match commanded position.",[["h","Position feedback sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P207C":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Low (Bank 2)","IMT position sensor at bank 2 reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P207D":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit High (Bank 2)","IMT position sensor at bank 2 reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P207E":["Intake Manifold Tuning (IMT) Valve Position Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","IMT position sensor at bank 2 signal is unstable — connector or harness issue. The intake manifold runner control (IMRC) flaps tune intake geometry for filling efficiency across the rpm range; stuck flaps cost part-load torque and can set lean codes.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P207F":["Reductant Quality Performance","The ECU has concluded that the AdBlue/DEF in the tank does not meet specification. Diagnosed by comparing expected NOx reduction against the dosed reductant volume — too much dosing for too little NOx drop indicates diluted or wrong fluid.",[["h","AdBlue diluted with water or wrong fluid filled"],["l","NOx sensor drift gives false reductant-quality verdict"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[50,800]],"c"],"P2080":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The pre-catalyst EGT sensor on bank 1 returns a value that does not match the expected temperature curve under load. Often slow response time after long service life or a contaminated tip.",[["h","Sensor aged — slow response"],["m","Sensor tip soot-fouled"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2081":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 1 signal jumps or drops out intermittently — typically a connector or chafed wire near the exhaust manifold heat zone.",[["h","Connector loose or oxidised"],["m","Wire chafed against exhaust shielding"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2082":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 1 reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response, stuck reading, or value does not track other EGT sensors during a regeneration.",[["h","Sensor drift over service life"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2083":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 1 signal jumps or drops out intermittently — typically a connector or chafed wire near the exhaust manifold heat zone.",[["h","Connector loose"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2084":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The bank 1 sensor 2 EGT reading deviates from the expected ratio against the upstream EGT sensor or modeled exhaust temperature. Confuses DPF regeneration control and may force a forced regen.",[["h","Sensor aged or drifting"],["m","DPF heavily loaded — non-physical temperature gradient"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2085":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 2 signal jumps or drops out intermittently — typically a connector or chafed wire near the exhaust manifold heat zone.",[["h","Connector loose"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2086":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 2 reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response, stuck reading, or value does not track other EGT sensors during a regeneration.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2087":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 2 signal jumps or drops out intermittently — typically a connector or chafed wire near the exhaust manifold heat zone.",[["h","Connector loose"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2088":["Camshaft Position A Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","Drive voltage to the intake VVT oil control valve on bank 1 reads below the lower limit. Usually a short to ground or a coil shorted internally.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Solenoid coil internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2089":["Camshaft Position A Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","Drive voltage to the intake VVT oil control valve on bank 1 is above the upper limit — short to supply or open ground side. The solenoid is energised constantly or the driver protection trips.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["l","ECU driver stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P208A":["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit/Open","The control line driving DEF pump A is open — no continuity through the motor or harness, dosing pressure cannot be built.",[["h","Pump motor winding open"],["m","Open wire to pump"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"c"],"P208B":["Reductant Pump A Control Performance/Stuck Off","DEF pump A receives a run command but does not start, or shuts off prematurely — pump performance is below threshold.",[["h","Pump motor seized — DEF crystallised inside pump head"],["m","Motor brushes worn"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"c"],"P208C":["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit Low","DEF pump A control line stuck low — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"c"],"P208D":["Reductant Pump A Control Circuit High","DEF pump A control line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"c"],"P208E":["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1 Unit 1)","The DEF injection valve at bank 1 unit 1 does not open when commanded — typically crystallised DEF blocks the nozzle, no flow into the SCR.",[["h","Nozzle crystallised"],["m","Valve seized"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P208F":["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2 Unit 1)","The DEF injection valve at bank 2 unit 1 does not open when commanded — typically crystallised DEF blocks the nozzle, no flow into the SCR.",[["h","Nozzle crystallised"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P2090":["Camshaft Position B Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 1)","Drive voltage to the exhaust VVT oil control valve on bank 1 is below the lower limit. Same failure pattern as P2088 but for the exhaust cam phaser.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Exhaust VVT solenoid internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2091":["Camshaft Position B Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 1)","Drive voltage to the exhaust VVT oil control valve on bank 1 is above the upper limit. Mirror image of P2089 on the exhaust cam side.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["l","ECU driver stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2092":["A Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","The intake (A) camshaft phaser solenoid drive line on bank 2 is stuck low — short to ground or stuck-low driver. Variable-valve timing on intake bank 2 cannot be modulated.",[["h","Short to ground in solenoid drive line"],["m","Solenoid winding shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2093":["A Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","The intake (A) camshaft phaser solenoid drive line on bank 2 is stuck high — short to B+ or open ground.",[["h","Short to B+"],["m","Open ground return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2094":["B Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","The exhaust (B) camshaft phaser solenoid drive line on bank 2 is stuck low — short to ground or stuck-low driver.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2095":["B Camshaft Position Actuator Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","The exhaust (B) camshaft phaser solenoid drive line on bank 2 is stuck high — short to B+ or open ground.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2096":["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Lean (Bank 1)","Long-term fuel trim derived from the downstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 has reached the lean limit. The downstream-trim correction is a fine adjustment that runs after the main trim from the upstream sensor; persistent excursion suggests a degraded catalyst, an exhaust leak after the catalyst, or a drifting downstream sensor.",[["h","Exhaust leak after catalyst (post-cat sensor sees ambient air)"],["m","Downstream sensor drifting"],["l","Catalyst lightly degraded"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,700]],"c"],"P2097":["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Rich (Bank 1)","Long-term post-catalyst fuel trim on bank 1 has reached its rich limit. The downstream sensor sees more reductant than expected, often pointing to a degraded catalyst that no longer stores oxygen, or a failing downstream sensor biased rich.",[["h","Catalyst oxygen storage exhausted"],["m","Downstream sensor biased rich"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,1500]],"c"],"P2098":["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Lean (Bank 2)","Bank 2 counterpart of P2096. The post-catalyst fuel trim correction on bank 2 has reached its lean limit, suggesting an exhaust leak after the bank 2 catalyst, a drifting downstream sensor, or a degraded catalyst.",[["h","Exhaust leak after bank 2 catalyst"],["m","Bank 2 downstream sensor drifting"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,700]],"c"],"P2099":["Post Catalyst Fuel Trim System Too Rich (Bank 2)","Bank 2 counterpart of P2097. Post-catalyst trim on bank 2 has reached the rich limit — usually a depleted catalyst or a downstream sensor biased rich on the bank 2 side.",[["h","Bank 2 catalyst oxygen storage exhausted"],["m","Bank 2 downstream sensor biased rich"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,1500]],"c"],"P209A":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on reductant injection air-pressure sensor B — the second air-assist pressure sensor on dual-bank or dual-injector DEF systems.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P209B":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor B reads inside the electrical range but does not match expected behaviour over time or load — slow response or wrong offset.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P209C":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor B reads below its lower plausibility limit — short to ground or sensor internal short.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P209D":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","The reductant injection air-pressure sensor B reads above its upper plausibility limit — open signal line or short to B+.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P209E":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","The two reductant injection air-pressure sensors A and B disagree by more than the allowed tolerance — one is reading off, or there is a real pressure imbalance between the two air-assist branches.",[["h","One sensor drifts relative to the other"],["m","Real imbalance between air branches"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P209F":["Reductant Tank Heater Control Circuit Performance","DEF tank heater is electrically OK but does not warm the tank within the expected time — element is partially open, fluid level too low for proper heat transfer, or the heater is undersized for the ambient temperature.",[["h","Heater element partially open"],["m","DEF level too low for heat transfer"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P20A0":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit/Open","The reductant purge control valve A drive circuit is open — used to evacuate DEF lines back to the tank when the engine is shut down to prevent freezing damage.",[["h","Solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P20A1":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Performance","Reductant purge control valve A is electrically OK but does not vent the line within the expected time — partial blockage or weakened solenoid.",[["h","Partial blockage from crystallisation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P20A2":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit Low","Reductant purge control valve A drive line stuck low — short to ground. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P20A3":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Circuit High","Reductant purge control valve A drive line stuck high — short to B+. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P20A4":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Stuck Open","Reductant purge control valve A is mechanically stuck open — system cannot maintain dosing pressure because the line is constantly vented to the tank.",[["h","Valve stuck open mechanically"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P20A5":["Reductant Purge Control Valve A Stuck Closed","Reductant purge control valve A is mechanically stuck closed — DEF lines cannot be vented at shutdown, increasing risk of freeze damage in winter.",[["h","Valve stuck closed mechanically"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P20A6":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Control Valve Circuit/Open","The drive circuit for the air-