nto exhaust fails, regeneration cannot raise temperature.",[["h","Solenoid stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P20DD":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on the aftertreatment fuel-pressure sensor — used to verify the dedicated HC-dosing rail is primed.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[150,1000]],"c"],"P20DE":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Aftertreatment fuel-pressure sensor reads in range but plausibility fails — pressure does not rise during prime, drift across a regeneration.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[150,1000]],"c"],"P20DF":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Aftertreatment fuel-pressure sensor below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[150,1000]],"c"],"P20E3":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/3 Correlation (Bank 1)","Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/3 Correlation (Bank 1): the value does not correlate with the related sensor or expected pattern. The ECU uses this temperature to protect the catalyst and diesel particulate filter.",[["h","One EGT sensor drifts"],["m","Exhaust leak between the two sensor positions"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P20E4":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 2/3 Correlation (Bank 1)","Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 2/3 Correlation (Bank 1): the value does not correlate with the related sensor or expected pattern. The ECU uses this temperature to protect the catalyst and diesel particulate filter.",[["h","One EGT sensor drifts"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P20E5":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 2)","EGT sensors 1 and 3 on bank 2 disagree by more than the allowed tolerance — one is reading off, or there is a real temperature gradient that exceeds the calibrated map (e.g. from a leaking exhaust joint between the two locations).",[["h","One EGT sensor drifts"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P20E6":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Too Low","The DEF system air-assist pressure is below the required threshold — pump weak, line leak, or pressure-control valve stuck open.",[["h","Air pump weak"],["m","Leak in air line"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P20E7":["Reductant Injection Air Pressure Too High","The DEF system air-assist pressure exceeds the upper threshold — pressure-control valve stuck closed or air pump runaway.",[["h","Pressure control valve stuck closed"],["m","Air pump does not regulate"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P20E8":["Reductant Pressure Too Low","Pressure in the AdBlue/DEF supply line is below the target. Usually a failing reductant pump, a clogged filter, frozen lines, or a leak in the pressurised circuit.",[["h","Reductant pump weak or failed"],["m","Reductant filter clogged with crystals"],["m","Leak in pressurised reductant line"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1800]],"c"],"P20E9":["Reductant Pressure Too High","Manufacturer-specific variant of the reductant over-pressure condition. The pressure exceeds the upper threshold during a defined operating window; on some platforms used in addition to P20E2 to flag a different test path.",[["h","Return line blocked or frozen"],["m","Pressure sensor reads high"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[250,1500]],"c"],"P20EE":["NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)","The SCR catalyst on bank 1 is no longer reducing NOx to the level the ECU expects, even with proper reductant dosing and quality. Often the result of catalyst poisoning by sulphur or hydrocarbons, thermal aging, or a leak between the upstream and downstream NOx sensors.",[["h","SCR catalyst aged or poisoned"],["m","NOx sensor drift"],["l","Exhaust leak between upstream and downstream NOx sensors"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,3500]],"c"],"P20F0":["SCR NOx Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2)","SCR NOx Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2): the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","Runaway DPF regeneration upstream"],["l","Temperature sensor drift high"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"c"],"P20F1":["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2)","SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Over Temperature (Bank 2): the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","Runaway regeneration upstream"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"c"],"P20F2":["SCR NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","SCR NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","SCR catalyst thermally aged"],["m","Catalyst poisoning from sulphur or oil ash"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P20F3":["SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2)","SCR NOx Pre-Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 2): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Pre-catalyst thermally aged"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P20F4":["Reductant Consumption Too Low","The DEF consumption observed over the dosing window is below the model expectation — typically a clogged dosing nozzle, weak pump, or leak between pump and injector that recirculates DEF back to the tank.",[["h","Dosing nozzle clogged with crystallised DEF"],["m","Pump weak — flow under target"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P20F5":["Reductant Consumption Too High","The DEF consumption observed over the dosing window is above the model expectation — typically a leaking injector seat, leaking line fitting, or a pressure-control valve that vents constantly to the tank.",[["h","Injector seat leaks DEF into exhaust"],["m","Cracked line or fitting"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P20F6":["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1 Unit 1)","The DEF injection valve at bank 1 unit 1 does not close when commanded — DEF flows continuously into the SCR. Risk of crystallisation in the catalyst and over-dosing.",[["h","Valve seat eroded or contaminated"],["m","Valve plunger seized open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P20F7":["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2 Unit 1)","The DEF injection valve at bank 2 unit 1 does not close when commanded — DEF flows continuously into the SCR. Risk of crystallisation in the catalyst and over-dosing.",[["h","Valve seat eroded or contaminated"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P20F8":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Performance (Bank 1)","The IMRC actuator drive circuit on bank 1 is electrically OK but its current draw or duty-cycle response is outside the calibrated profile — typically a high-resistance solenoid winding or a partially shorted driver.",[["h","Solenoid winding ageing — resistance climbing"]],[],["medium",[50,500]],"u"],"P20F9":["Intake Manifold Runner Control Circuit Performance (Bank 2)","The IMRC actuator drive circuit on bank 2 is electrically OK but its current draw or duty-cycle response is outside the calibrated profile — typically a high-resistance solenoid winding or a partially shorted driver.",[["h","Solenoid winding ageing"]],[],["medium",[50,500]],"u"],"P20FA":["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit/Open","The control line driving DEF pump B is open. On large engines or dual-tank systems a second pump (B) supplements pump A; with B offline the system loses redundancy.",[["h","Pump motor winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"u"],"P20FB":["Reductant Pump B Control Performance/Stuck Off","DEF pump B receives a run command but does not start, or shuts off prematurely.",[["h","Pump head crystallised — motor seized"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"u"],"P20FC":["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit Low","DEF pump B control line stuck low — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"u"],"P20FD":["Reductant Pump B Control Circuit High","DEF pump B control line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1100]],"u"],"P20FE":["Reductant Metering Unit 1 Performance","The first DEF metering unit (the integrated module that combines pump, filter, level sensor, and dosing valve) is electrically OK but does not deliver the expected pressure or flow during operation.",[["h","Metering unit aged or partially clogged"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,3000]],"u"],"P20FF":["Reductant Control Module Performance","The dedicated SCR/reductant control module reports an internal performance fault — failed self-tests, watchdog resets, or calibration mismatch. Frequently a forerunner of total module failure.",[["h","Internal module fault"],["m","Calibration mismatch after software update"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[600,3500]],"u"],"P2100":["Throttle Actuator Control Motor Circuit Open","The drive-by-wire throttle motor circuit is open — no current flow detected. The ECU loses authority over the throttle plate and forces a limp-home with reduced power.",[["h","Throttle motor failed"],["m","Connector loose or corroded"],["m","Wiring break to throttle body"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2101":["Throttle Actuator Control Motor Circuit Range/Performance","The throttle motor responds, but its actual position does not track the commanded position within tolerance. Often a dirty throttle bore where the plate sticks, or a worn motor.",[["h","Throttle bore coked, plate sticks"],["m","Throttle motor worn"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2102":["Throttle Actuator Control Motor Circuit Low","Drive voltage to the throttle motor is below the lower limit. Typically a short to ground or a failed driver stage in the ECU.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Throttle motor internal short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2103":["Throttle Actuator Control Motor Circuit High","Drive voltage to the throttle motor is above the upper limit. Usually a short to supply or an open ground.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["m","Throttle motor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2104":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Forced Idle","The ECU has detected a fault severe enough that it forces the throttle actuator to the idle stop. The driver loses pedal authority — only idle is available until the underlying TAC fault clears.",[["h","Severe upstream TAC fault"],["m","Throttle position signal invalid"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[120,900]],"c"],"P2105":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Forced Engine Shutdown","The TAC monitor commanded an engine shutdown because throttle authority can no longer be guaranteed safely. The most aggressive TAC limp mode — used when both throttle position sensors disagree or the motor is uncontrollable.",[["h","TPS1 and TPS2 disagree beyond limit"],["m","Throttle motor not controllable"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2106":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Forced Limited Power","The TAC monitor restricts maximum throttle opening as a safety response to a TAC fault. The vehicle can still be driven, but accelerator pedal travel is capped.",[["h","Underlying TAC fault triggers limit"],["m","Pedal position sensor signal implausible"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[120,900]],"c"],"P2107":["Throttle Actuator Control Module Internal Processor","The internal processor or watchdog of the throttle actuator control module reports an internal fault. Communication between the TAC monitor core and the main ECU core has failed plausibility — typical for a defective ECU.",[["h","ECU internal processor fault"],["l","ECU software flash corrupted"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[400,2000]],"c"],"P2108":["Throttle Actuator Control Module Performance","Self-tests within the TAC module fail their performance criteria — for example RAM/ROM checks or analog reference voltages drift. Indicates an aging ECU rather than a wiring fault.",[["h","ECU internal performance fault"],["l","ECU connector pins corroded"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[400,2000]],"c"],"P2109":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor A Minimum Stop Performance","The ECU detects that the throttle position sensor A signal at the closed-throttle stop does not match the learned minimum value. The mechanical or electrical zero reference of the throttle has drifted out of the expected range, often after cleaning, replacement or wear.",[["h","Carbon deposits on throttle plate"],["h","Throttle position sensor drift"],["m","Idle/throttle relearn not performed"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P210A":["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit/Open","The drive circuit of throttle actuator motor B is open. Throttle B is the secondary throttle on engines with two throttle bodies — typically used for tumble flap or charge-motion control.",[["h","Motor winding open"],["m","Open wire to motor"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P210B":["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit Range/Performance","Throttle actuator B motor responds electrically but does not move the throttle plate as commanded — typically high-resistance brushes, partial winding fault, or a sticky throttle bore.",[["h","Motor brushes worn"],["m","Carbon buildup at throttle plate"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P210C":["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit Low","Throttle actuator B motor drive line stuck low — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P210D":["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Circuit High","Throttle actuator B motor drive line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P210E":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch C/F Voltage Correlation","The redundant throttle or accelerator pedal position channels C and F disagree by more than the allowed tolerance. Drive-by-wire systems compare two or three independent channels to detect a faulty potentiometer track.",[["h","One potentiometer track worn — voltage drift"],["m","Water in pedal connector"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P210F":["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Forced Limited RPM","Throttle B control has detected an unsafe condition and forced an RPM limit. Common protective response when motor current, throttle position feedback, or supply voltage on the B path is out of spec.",[["h","Protection mode triggered by paired throttle-B fault"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[100,800]],"u"],"P2110":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Forced Limited RPM","The TAC monitor caps engine speed at a fixed limp-home rpm because it can no longer trust the throttle response. Driver may notice a hard rev limit well below redline.",[["h","Underlying TAC fault triggers rpm cap"],["m","Throttle response time out of spec"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[120,900]],"c"],"P2111":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Stuck Open","The throttle plate cannot be commanded back to the closed/idle position. Idle speed runs high or the engine cannot decelerate properly — safety-critical fault that usually triggers immediate limp mode.",[["h","Throttle plate seized open"],["m","Return spring broken"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2112":["Throttle Actuator Control System — Stuck Closed","The throttle plate cannot be commanded open. The engine stays at idle or stalls under load.",[["h","Throttle plate seized closed"],["m","Throttle motor seized or gear broken"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2118":["Throttle Actuator Control Motor Current Range/Performance","The current draw of the throttle motor lies outside the expected range — either much higher (binding plate) or much lower (worn brushes, open winding) than calibrated.",[["h","Plate binding from carbon"],["m","Motor windings aged or open"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2119":["Throttle Closed Position Performance","When commanded to idle, the throttle plate does not reach the calibrated closed position. Often a coked throttle bore preventing the plate from seating fully.",[["h","Throttle bore coked at closed-position stop"],["m","Plate or stop misadjusted after service"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,500]],"c"],"P211A":["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Stuck Open","Throttle B is mechanically stuck open — typically carbon buildup or a broken return spring on the secondary throttle plate.",[["h","Carbon buildup holds plate open"],["m","Return spring broken"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"u"],"P211B":["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Stuck Closed","Throttle B is mechanically stuck closed — carbon buildup or a seized bearing on the secondary throttle.",[["h","Carbon buildup holds plate closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"u"],"P211C":["Throttle Actuator B Control Motor Current Range/Performance","Throttle B motor current draw does not match the calibrated map for the commanded position — high friction, partial short, or stiction.",[["h","High friction in throttle bore"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"u"],"P211D":["Throttle Actuator B Control Throttle Body Range/Performance","The throttle B body itself does not respond as commanded — position feedback is plausible but does not track the setpoint within the calibrated time window.",[["h","Throttle body aged or contaminated"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[80,700]],"u"],"P211E":["Throttle Actuator B Control Module Processor","The processor monitoring throttle B inside the throttle/PCM has reported a self-test failure — RAM check, ROM check, or watchdog timeout.",[["h","Internal processor fault"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"],["l","Supply voltage outside specification"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P211F":["Throttle Actuator B Control Module Performance","The throttle control module on the B path reports general performance issues — internal fault, communication mismatch, or calibration drift.",[["h","Internal module fault"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"],["l","Supply voltage outside specification"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2122":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"D\" Circuit Low","Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"D\" Circuit Low: the signal voltage is below the expected range. Often a short to ground or high resistance in the wiring.",[["h","Pedal sensor track worn"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,350]],"c"],"P2123":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"D\" Circuit High","Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"D\" Circuit High: the signal voltage is above the expected range. Often an open circuit or a short to supply voltage.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,350]],"c"],"P2127":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"E\" Circuit Low","Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"E\" Circuit Low: the signal voltage is below the expected range. Often a short to ground or high resistance in the wiring.",[["h","Pedal sensor track worn"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,350]],"c"],"P2128":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"E\" Circuit High","Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"E\" Circuit High: the signal voltage is above the expected range. Often an open circuit or a short to supply voltage.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,350]],"c"],"P212A":["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on throttle position sensor G — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. Sensor G is part of a multi-channel redundancy on dual-throttle systems.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P212B":["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Range/Performance","TPS G reads in range but plausibility check fails — value sticks, lags, or does not match the commanded throttle position.",[["h","Sensor wiper sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P212C":["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Low","TPS G below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P212D":["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit High","TPS G above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P212E":["Throttle Position Sensor/Switch G Circuit Intermittent","TPS G signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or harness issue. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,500]],"c"],"P212F":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F/G Voltage Correlation","Channels F and G of the throttle/pedal position sensor disagree by more than the allowed tolerance. Drive-by-wire system has lost redundancy and may force limp mode.",[["h","One potentiometer track worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,600]],"u"],"P2130":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on throttle/pedal position sensor F — open, shorted, or out of plausibility.",[["h","Sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2134":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch F Circuit Intermittent","TPS/APP sensor F signal jumps or drops out intermittently. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,500]],"c"],"P2135":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"A\"/\"B\" Voltage Correlation","The two redundant throttle position sensors on the throttle body disagree by more than allowed. Distinct from P2138 which monitors the pedal pair — P2135 monitors the throttle-body pair on drive-by-wire systems.",[["h","Throttle position sensor track worn"],["m","Corrosion on throttle body connector"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2136":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor A/C Voltage Correlation","The \"A\" and \"C\" channels of the throttle or pedal sensor disagree by more than the allowed tolerance. The ECU cannot trust either reading and forces limp-home with reduced torque.",[["h","One sensor track worn"],["m","Connector corroded with leakage"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,400]],"c"],"P2137":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor B/C Voltage Correlation","The \"B\" and \"C\" channels of the throttle or pedal sensor disagree beyond tolerance — the ECU cannot trust either signal and reverts to limp-home.",[["h","Track B or C worn"],["m","Connector corroded with leakage"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,400]],"c"],"P2138":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor \"D\"/\"E\" Voltage Correlation","The two redundant accelerator pedal position sensors disagree by more than the allowed tolerance. The ECU cannot trust either signal and switches to limp-home with very limited torque.",[["h","Pedal position sensor worn or contaminated"],["m","Corroded pedal connector"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[80,400]],"c"],"P2139":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch D/F Voltage Correlation","Channels D and F of the throttle/pedal position sensor disagree by more than the allowed tolerance.",[["h","One potentiometer track worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P213A":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B/Open","The drive circuit of EGR throttle B is open. EGR throttles partially close intake to increase exhaust gas recirculation flow at low loads.",[["h","Actuator winding open"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P213B":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B Range/Performance","EGR throttle B is electrically OK but does not move as commanded — typically carbon buildup or a sticking actuator.",[["h","Carbon buildup restricts movement"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P213C":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B Low","EGR throttle B drive line stuck low — short to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to ground"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P213D":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit B High","EGR throttle B drive line stuck high — short to B+. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to B+"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P213E":["Fuel Injection System Fault - Forced Engine Shutdown","A safety-critical fuel-injection fault has been detected and the PCM has shut down the engine to prevent damage. Examples are common-rail pressure runaway, multiple stuck-open injectors, or HPFP failure.",[["h","Common-rail pressure runaway"],["m","Injector stuck open"]],[],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P213F":["Fuel Pump System Fault - Forced Engine Shutdown","A safety-critical fuel-pump fault has been detected and the engine has been shut down. Typical for HPFP runaway or low-pressure pump that loses control authority.",[["h","HPFP runaway"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2140":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch E/F Voltage Correlation","Channels E and F of the throttle/pedal position sensor disagree by more than the allowed tolerance.",[["h","One potentiometer track worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P2141":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit A Low","EGR throttle A drive line stuck low — short to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to ground"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P2142":["EGR Throttle Control Circuit A High","EGR throttle A drive line stuck high — short to B+. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to B+"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,900]],"c"],"P2143":["EGR Vent Control Circuit/Open","The drive circuit of the EGR vent solenoid is open — the solenoid releases vacuum from the EGR actuator. Open circuit means the EGR cannot reset its position.",[["h","Solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2144":["EGR Vent Control Circuit Low","EGR vent solenoid drive line stuck low — short to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2145":["EGR Vent Control Circuit High","EGR vent solenoid drive line stuck high — short to B+. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2146":["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The ECU detects an open or missing supply voltage on injector group A. The injectors of this bank cannot be energized; the affected cylinders may not fire and the engine runs rough or stalls.",[["h","Blown injector fuse"],["m","Faulty injector supply relay"],["m","Open in supply wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2147":["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage measured at injector group A is below the calibrated threshold. Either the supply is shorted to ground or the source voltage has collapsed during cranking or load.",[["h","Supply wire shorted to ground"],["m","Weak battery, low cranking voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2148":["Fuel Injector Group A Supply Voltage Circuit High","The injector group A supply voltage exceeds the calibrated upper limit. Often a sign of a short to battery voltage on the supply line, an over-charging alternator or an internal driver failure.",[["h","Wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2149":["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The ECU detects an open or missing supply voltage on injector group B. The injectors on this bank cannot be energized, leading to misfire on the affected cylinders.",[["h","Blown injector group B fuse"],["m","Faulty injector supply relay"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P214A":["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High","SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High: the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","Upstream regeneration overshoot"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"u"],"P214B":["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration","SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration: the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","HC dosing overshot during regeneration"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"u"],"P214C":["SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High","SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High: the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","Sustained over-temperature event"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"u"],"P214D":["SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration","SCR NOx Catalyst Outlet Temperature Too High During Particulate Filter Regeneration: the component is overheating, typically from extended load or slip.",[["h","HC dosing overshot"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,4000]],"u"],"P214E":["Reductant Pump A Current Too High","DEF pump A current draw exceeds the upper threshold — typically a seized pump head or partial winding short.",[["h","Pump head seized"],["m","Winding partially shorted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P214F":["Reductant Heater A Current Too High","DEF heater A current draw exceeds the upper threshold — typically a partial short in the heating element.",[["h","Element partially shorted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P2150":["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group B has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2151":["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group B is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-B supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2152":["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group C is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2153":["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group C has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2154":["Fuel Injector Group C Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group C is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-C supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2155":["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group D is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2156":["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group D has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2157":["Fuel Injector Group D Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group D is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-D supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2158":["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on vehicle speed sensor B — second VSS used either at the transmission output or as redundancy. Open, short, or implausible signal.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2159":["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Range/Performance","The signal of the secondary vehicle speed sensor is implausible compared to other sensors. The ECU cannot use the value for fuel and ignition control or transmission shifting.",[["h","Faulty vehicle speed sensor B"],["m","Damaged wiring or connector"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P215A":["Vehicle Speed - Wheel Speed Correlation","The vehicle speed signal computed from VSS does not match the wheel-speed signal from ABS within tolerance. One of the two sources is wrong, or there is a tyre-size mismatch.",[["h","Tyre size mismatch versus calibration"],["m","One sensor drifts or fails"]],[],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P215B":["Vehicle Speed - Output Shaft Speed Correlation","VSS does not match transmission output-shaft speed within tolerance. Possible transmission slip, sensor fault, or harness issue.",[["h","Transmission slip"]],[],["hard",[100,3000]],"c"],"P215C":["Output Shaft Speed - Wheel Speed Correlation","Transmission output-shaft speed does not match ABS wheel speed within tolerance — typically transmission slip, driveline fault, or one sensor drift.",[["h","Transmission or driveline slip"]],[],["hard",[100,3000]],"c"],"P215D":["Reductant Pump B Stuck On","Reductant Pump B Stuck On: the actuator is stuck in the on position.",[["h","Pump relay contacts welded"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P215E":["Reductant Heater D Current Too Low","DEF heater D current draw is below threshold — typically a partially-open winding.",[["h","Element partially open"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P215F":["Reductant Heater D Current Too High","DEF heater D current draw exceeds threshold — element partially shorted.",[["h","Element partially shorted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P2160":["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","VSS B reads below lower plausibility — short to ground or sensor not signalling. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2161":["Vehicle Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic/High","VSS B signal jumps, drops out, or reads above plausibility — connector or harness issue, or magnetic ring damaged.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["m","Tone ring chipped"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P2162":["Vehicle Speed Sensor A/B Correlation","VSS A and VSS B disagree by more than the allowed tolerance.",[["h","One sensor drifts"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P2163":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor A Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor A does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2164":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor B Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor B does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2165":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor C Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor C does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2166":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor D Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor D does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2167":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor E Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor E does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2168":["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor F Maximum Stop Performance","Throttle/pedal position sensor F does not reach the calibrated maximum-stop value during the wide-open self-test. Sensor wear, mechanical stop misalignment, or a stuck pedal.",[["h","Sensor or mechanical stop worn"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2169":["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit/Open","The drive circuit of the exhaust pressure regulator vent solenoid is open. The solenoid releases pressure from the exhaust backpressure regulator, which is part of the exhaust brake system on diesel trucks.",[["h","Solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P216A":["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group E is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P216B":["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group E has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P216C":["Fuel Injector Group E Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group E is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-E supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P216D":["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group F is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P216E":["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group F has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P216F":["Fuel Injector Group F Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group F is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-F supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2170":["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit Low","EPR vent solenoid drive line stuck low — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P2171":["Exhaust Pressure Regulator Vent Solenoid Control Circuit High","EPR vent solenoid drive line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P2172":["Throttle Actuator Control System - Sudden High Air Flow Detected","A sudden, large jump in MAF/MAP signal not matched by a corresponding pedal change has been detected — typically a torn intake boot, dropped MAF sensor, or actively-stuck-open throttle plate.",[["h","Torn intake boot"],["m","MAF sensor connection lost"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2174":["Throttle Actuator Control System - Sudden Low Air Flow Detected","A sudden, large drop in MAF/MAP signal not matched by a pedal change — typically intake restriction, MAF failure, or actively-stuck-closed throttle plate.",[["h","Intake severely restricted"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2175":["Throttle Actuator Control System - Low Air Flow Detected","Sustained low air-flow condition detected — slower than P2174 but persistent. Restricted air filter, dirty MAF, or partially-stuck throttle.",[["h","Air filter heavily restricted"],["m","MAF sensor contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[20,300]],"c"],"P2176":["Throttle Actuator A Control System - Idle Position Not Learned","Throttle Actuator A Control System - Idle Position Not Learned: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Idle relearn procedure not completed"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[10,100]],"c"],"P2177":["System Too Lean Off Idle Bank 1","Fuel trim values on bank 1 indicate a lean condition during off-idle operation. The ECU has to add significant fuel correction to maintain stoichiometric mixture above idle.",[["h","Vacuum leak under load"],["m","Low fuel pressure / weak pump"],["m","Contaminated MAF sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2178":["System Too Rich Off Idle Bank 1","Bank 1 fuel trim shows a strong rich correction during off-idle operation. The ECU is forced to subtract fuel to keep the mixture near stoichiometric.",[["h","Leaking fuel injector"],["m","Excessive fuel pressure"],["m","Stuck-open purge valve"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2179":["System Too Lean Off Idle Bank 2","Fuel trims on bank 2 show a lean deviation during off-idle operating conditions. Causes are similar to bank 1 but isolated to the second cylinder bank.",[["h","Vacuum leak on bank 2"],["m","Low fuel pressure"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P217A":["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group G is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P217B":["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group G has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P217C":["Fuel Injector Group G Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group G is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-G supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P217D":["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit/Open","The supply rail to injector group H is open, so none of the injectors in this group can fire. The affected cylinders produce no power and the engine runs rough or on reduced cylinders.",[["h","Open supply wire or blown fuse"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P217E":["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The supply voltage feeding injector group H has dropped below the lower limit. The injectors in this group lose drive voltage and may stop firing, so the cylinders they serve run lean or cut out.",[["h","Fuse, relay, or wiring fault on supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P217F":["Fuel Injector Group H Supply Voltage Circuit High","The supply voltage on injector group H is above the upper limit. Overvoltage on the group-H supply can mis-time or damage the injectors.",[["h","Charging system overvoltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2180":["System Too Rich Off Idle Bank 2","Bank 2 fuel trim shows a rich shift during off-idle conditions. The ECU subtracts fuel to maintain proper combustion.",[["h","Leaking injector on bank 2"],["m","Excessive fuel pressure"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2181":["Cooling System Performance","The engine cooling system does not reach or maintain the expected temperature within the diagnostic window — usually a stuck-open thermostat, but also a low coolant level or a stuck cooling fan that overcools the engine.",[["h","Thermostat stuck open"],["m","Coolant level low"],["l","Cooling fan stuck on"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2182":["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on engine coolant temperature sensor 2 — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. Sensor 2 is typically at the radiator outlet or as redundancy on the second cylinder bank.",[["h","Sensor failed"],["m","Harness fault"]],["Check engine light on","Cooling fan runs constantly or not at all","Cabin heater weak or excessively hot"],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2183":["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Range/Performance","ECT sensor 2 reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response, stuck reading, or value does not track ECT 1 across a warm-up.",[["h","Sensor drifts over service life"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Cooling fan runs constantly or not at all","Cabin heater weak or excessively hot"],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2184":["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Low","ECT sensor 2 reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. The engine coolant temperature sensor feeds warm-up enrichment, fan control and closed-loop entry — a stuck-cold reading keeps the engine in open loop and rich forever.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Cooling fan runs constantly or not at all","Cabin heater weak or excessively hot"],["medium",[40,350]],"c"],"P2185":["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit High","The second coolant temperature sensor (often radiator-outlet or cylinder-head bank) reports a voltage above the upper threshold — typically an open signal wire or a sensor with infinite resistance.",[["h","Sensor element open"],["m","Signal wire open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Cooling fan runs constantly or not at all","Cabin heater weak or excessively hot"],["easy",[40,200]],"c"],"P2186":["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 2 Circuit Low","The second coolant temperature sensor reports a voltage below the lower threshold — typically a short to ground or a sensor with very low resistance.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor element shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Cooling fan runs constantly or not at all","Cabin heater weak or excessively hot"],["easy",[40,200]],"c"],"P2187":["System Too Lean at Idle (Bank 1)","Fuel trim on bank 1 hits the lean limit only at idle, while trim returns to normal at higher load. This pattern strongly indicates a vacuum leak — leaks become a larger fraction of total airflow at idle and so dominate the trim, but disappear into background noise above idle.",[["h","Vacuum leak (intake gasket, brake booster, hoses)"],["m","PCV valve stuck open"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[20,600]],"c"],"P2188":["System Too Rich at Idle (Bank 1)","Fuel trim on bank 1 hits the rich limit only at idle. Often a leaking injector dribbling fuel at low load, a sticky purge valve dumping fuel vapour, or fuel pressure regulator that fails to relieve pressure when intake vacuum is high.",[["h","Leaking injector at idle"],["m","Purge valve stuck open"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[40,500]],"c"],"P2189":["System Too Lean at Idle (Bank 2)","Fuel trim on bank 2 hits the lean limit only at idle, while trim returns to normal at higher load. This pattern strongly indicates a vacuum leak — leaks become a larger fraction of total airflow at idle and so dominate the trim, but disappear into background noise above idle.",[["h","Vacuum leak on bank 2"],["m","PCV valve stuck open"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[20,600]],"c"],"P218A":["Throttle Actuator B Control System - Idle Position Not Learned","Throttle Actuator B Control System - Idle Position Not Learned: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Idle relearn procedure not completed"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[10,100]],"u"],"P218B":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit","A general electrical fault on the throttle/fuel inhibit signal B — used by anti-theft, immobiliser, or transmission to forbid throttle/fuel until released.",[["h","Inhibit signal lost"]],[],["hard",[80,1000]],"u"],"P218C":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit Range/Performance","Throttle/fuel inhibit B signal reads in range but plausibility fails — does not assert/release as expected.",[["h","Inhibit logic mismatch"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[80,1000]],"u"],"P218D":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit Low","Throttle/fuel inhibit B line stuck low. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[80,800]],"u"],"P218E":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit B Circuit High","Throttle/fuel inhibit B line stuck high. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[80,800]],"u"],"P218F":["Reductant No Flow Detected","The DEF dosing system commands flow but the pressure or flow sensor reports no actual delivery — typically a fully blocked dosing nozzle, a frozen line, or a dead pump.",[["h","Dosing line or nozzle fully blocked"],["m","Pump dead"],["l","Line frozen at very low ambient temperature"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[200,2000]],"u"],"P2190":["System Too Rich at Idle (Bank 2)","Fuel trim on bank 2 hits the rich limit only at idle. Often a leaking injector dribbling fuel at low load, a sticky purge valve dumping fuel vapour, or fuel pressure regulator that fails to relieve pressure when intake vacuum is high.",[["h","Leaking injector at idle on bank 2"],["m","Purge valve stuck open"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[40,500]],"c"],"P2191":["System Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 1)","Bank 1 fuel trim hits the lean limit only at higher engine load. Pattern points to a fuel-supply restriction — failing fuel pump, blocked filter, or weak injectors — rather than a vacuum leak (which would dominate at idle).",[["h","Fuel pump weak under load"],["m","Fuel filter clogged"],["m","MAF reads low at high airflow"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[50,800]],"c"],"P2192":["System Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 1)","Bank 1 fuel trim hits the rich limit only at higher load. Often excessive fuel pressure, a stuck-closed MAF reading low, or coolant temperature signal stuck cold causing over-fuelling.",[["h","Fuel pressure too high"],["m","MAF reads low under load"],["m","Coolant temperature sensor stuck cold"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2193":["System Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 2)","Bank 2 fuel trim hits the lean limit only at higher engine load. Pattern points to a fuel-supply restriction — failing fuel pump, blocked filter, or weak injectors — rather than a vacuum leak (which would dominate at idle).",[["h","Fuel pump weak under load"],["m","Fuel filter clogged"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[50,800]],"c"],"P2194":["System Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 2)","Bank 2 fuel trim hits the rich limit only at higher load. Often excessive fuel pressure, a stuck-closed MAF reading low, or coolant temperature signal stuck cold causing over-fuelling.",[["h","Fuel pressure too high"],["m","MAF reads low under load"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[40,600]],"c"],"P2195":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Lean (Bank 1, Sensor 1)","The upstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 returns a constant lean signal during conditions where rich content is expected (for example after a deceleration fuel cut-off recovery). Usually a sensor that has lost its rich-side response or a slow heater warm-up.",[["h","Upstream sensor failed stuck lean"],["m","Sensor heater slow to warm up"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2196":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Rich (Bank 1, Sensor 1)","The upstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 returns a constant rich signal under deceleration fuel cut-off where lean is expected. Often a contaminated sensor (silicone, oil, coolant) or short to ground that pulls the signal high in some sensor types.",[["h","Upstream sensor contaminated"],["m","Upstream sensor failed stuck rich"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2197":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Lean (Bank 2, Sensor 1)","The upstream oxygen sensor on bank 2 returns a constant lean signal during conditions where rich content is expected (for example after a deceleration fuel cut-off recovery). Usually a sensor that has lost its rich-side response or a slow heater warm-up.",[["h","Upstream sensor failed stuck lean"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2198":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Rich (Bank 2, Sensor 1)","The upstream oxygen sensor on bank 2 returns a constant rich signal under deceleration fuel cut-off where lean is expected. Often a contaminated sensor (silicone, oil, coolant) or short to ground that pulls the signal high in some sensor types.",[["h","Upstream sensor contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2199":["Intake Air Temperature Sensor 1/2 Correlation","The two intake air temperature sensors disagree by more than the calibrated correlation threshold during stable conditions. The ECU cannot determine which value is correct.",[["h","One IAT sensor drifting"],["m","Wiring issue on one sensor"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P219A":["Bank 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","The fuel-trim values across cylinders on bank 1 differ enough that the bank-average air-fuel ratio is biased — a single cylinder is significantly leaner or richer than the rest. Detected by short-term-fuel-trim variance or by the wide-band O2 sensor harmonic monitor.",[["h","One injector clogged or leaking"],["m","Vacuum leak at one intake runner"],["l","Low compression on one cylinder"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P219B":["Bank 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","The fuel-trim values across cylinders on bank 2 differ enough that the bank-average air-fuel ratio is biased — a single cylinder is significantly leaner or richer than the rest. Detected by short-term-fuel-trim variance or by the wide-band O2 sensor harmonic monitor.",[["h","One injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P219C":["Cylinder 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 1 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P219D":["Cylinder 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 2 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P219E":["Cylinder 3 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 3 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P219F":["Cylinder 4 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 4 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A0":["Cylinder 5 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 5 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A1":["Cylinder 6 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 6 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A2":["Cylinder 7 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 7 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A3":["Cylinder 8 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 8 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A4":["Cylinder 9 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 9 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A5":["Cylinder 10 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 10 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A6":["Cylinder 11 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 11 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A7":["Cylinder 12 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","Cylinder 12 fuel trim deviates significantly from the bank average — a single-cylinder injector or intake fault.",[["h","Injector clogged or leaking"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P21A8":["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on DEF level sensor B — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. Some tanks use multiple level senders to cover irregular tank shapes; this is the primary one.",[["h","Sender failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"u"],"P21A9":["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","DEF level sensor B reading is in electrical range but plausibility check fails — value sticks, jumps, or does not match consumption.",[["h","Float arm sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"u"],"P21AA":["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Low","DEF level sensor B reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P21AB":["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit High","DEF level sensor B reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P21AC":["Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Reductant Level Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic: the signal is intermittent or erratic. Often a loose connector or chafed wiring; a wiggle test often locates it.",[["h","Corroded sender contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[60,600]],"u"],"P21AD":["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit","A general electrical fault is reported on DEF level sensor C — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. Some tanks use multiple level senders to cover irregular tank shapes; this is the primary one.",[["h","Sender failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"u"],"P21AE":["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","DEF level sensor C reading is in electrical range but plausibility check fails — value sticks, jumps, or does not match consumption.",[["h","Float arm sticks"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[120,800]],"u"],"P21AF":["Reductant Level Sensor C Circuit Low","DEF level sensor C reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulat