cher to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21EE":["Cylinder 10 Injector B Circuit Low","Cylinder 10 second-injector (B) drive line stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21EF":["Cylinder 10 Injector B Circuit High","Cylinder 10 second-injector (B) drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21F0":["Cylinder 11 Injector B Circuit Low","Cylinder 11 second-injector (B) drive line stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21F1":["Cylinder 11 Injector B Circuit High","Cylinder 11 second-injector (B) drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21F2":["Cylinder 12 Injector B Circuit Low","Cylinder 12 second-injector (B) drive line stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21F3":["Cylinder 12 Injector B Circuit High","Cylinder 12 second-injector (B) drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P21F4":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 1)","The secondary fuel control loop B on bank 1 reports a lean condition outside idle. On dual-injection systems (port + direct) the secondary loop trims port injection independently from the main loop.",[["h","Vacuum leak"],["m","Port injectors clogged"],["m","Fuel pressure low"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21F5":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 1)","Fuel Control System B Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 1): the fuel-trim control is correcting for an over-rich mixture in this operating range.",[["h","Port injectors leaking"],["m","Fuel pressure high"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21F6":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Off Idle (Bank 2)","The secondary fuel control loop B on bank 2 reports a lean condition outside idle. On dual-injection systems (port + direct) the secondary loop trims port injection independently from the main loop.",[["h","Vacuum leak or injector clog"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21F7":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Off Idle (Bank 2)","The secondary fuel control loop B on bank 2 reports a rich condition outside idle.",[["h","Injectors leaking"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21F8":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Idle (Bank 1)","Secondary fuel control loop B reports a lean condition at idle on bank 1. Idle is sensitive to vacuum leaks since manifold flow is low.",[["h","Vacuum leak — most visible at idle"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P21F9":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Idle (Bank 1)","Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Idle (Bank 1): the fuel-trim control is correcting for an over-rich mixture in this operating range.",[["h","Injectors leak at low duty cycle"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21FA":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Idle (Bank 2)","Secondary fuel control loop B reports a lean condition at idle on bank 2. Idle is sensitive to vacuum leaks since manifold flow is low.",[["h","Vacuum leak on bank 2 intake"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P21FB":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Idle (Bank 2)","The secondary fuel control loop B reports a rich condition at idle on bank 2. Idle rich often means injectors that leak at low duty cycle.",[["h","Injectors leak on bank 2"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1000]],"u"],"P21FC":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 1)","Secondary fuel control loop B on bank 1 reports a lean condition at higher load. Lean at high load typically points at fuel pressure shortfall, restricted injectors, or charge-air leak.",[["h","Fuel pressure drops under load"],["m","Charge-air leak after turbo"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,1500]],"u"],"P21FD":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 1)","Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 1): the fuel-trim control is correcting for an over-rich mixture in this operating range.",[["h","Fuel pressure regulator stuck high"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1500]],"u"],"P21FE":["Fuel Control System B Too Lean at Higher Load (Bank 2)","Secondary fuel control loop B on bank 2 reports a lean condition at higher load. Lean at high load typically points at fuel pressure shortfall, restricted injectors, or charge-air leak.",[["h","Fuel or charge-air problem on bank 2"]],["Check engine light on","Rough idle, possible stalling","Hesitation or hard cold start"],["medium",[80,1500]],"u"],"P21FF":["Fuel Control System B Too Rich at Higher Load (Bank 2)","The secondary fuel control loop B reports a rich condition at higher load on bank 2. Rich at high load typically points to a stuck-closed return on the fuel pressure regulator or over-delivering injectors.",[["h","Injectors over-deliver on bank 2"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Black smoke from exhaust on acceleration"],["medium",[80,1500]],"u"],"P2200":["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1)","The NOx sensor on bank 1 — typically upstream of the SCR catalyst — does not communicate or sends an invalid signal. NOx sensors are smart sensors with their own controller on the CAN bus; faults often involve heater failure or bus dropout.",[["h","NOx sensor failed"],["m","Sensor wiring or CAN harness open"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2201":["NOx Sensor Range/Performance (Bank 1)","The bank 1 NOx sensor reports values outside the plausibility window against modeled NOx and the downstream sensor. Often slow response from contamination by oil ash or coolant.",[["h","NOx sensor aged — slow response"],["m","Sensor element contaminated"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2202":["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1)","The NOx sensor signal on bank 1 is below the lower limit. Either short to ground on the analog return, sensor failed at low end, or pump cell stuck.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor failed low"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2203":["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1)","The NOx sensor signal on bank 1 is above the upper limit — short to supply, open ground, or a sensor that failed high. SCR control runs in default mode.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor failed high"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2204":["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1)","The bank 1 NOx sensor signal drops out intermittently. Typical cause is a marginal connector, harness chafing near hot exhaust components, or thermal-cycling solder joints inside the smart sensor.",[["h","Connector intermittent contact"],["m","Harness chafed near exhaust"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2205":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit (Bank 1)","The heater inside the bank 1 NOx sensor cannot be controlled — open, short, or failed driver. Without proper heater operation the sensor never reaches its operating temperature and reports invalid data.",[["h","Heater element open"],["m","Heater short to supply or ground"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P220A":["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The supply voltage rail to the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 is faulty — typically a fuse, harness break, or short. NOx sensors need a clean stable supply for the heater and the wide-band measurement cell.",[["h","Fuse, harness break, or short"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P220B":["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The supply voltage rail to the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 is faulty — typically a fuse, harness break, or short. NOx sensors need a clean stable supply for the heater and the wide-band measurement cell.",[["h","Supply rail fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P220C":["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The supply voltage rail to the NOx sensor on bank 2 sensor 1 is faulty — typically a fuse, harness break, or short. NOx sensors need a clean stable supply for the heater and the wide-band measurement cell.",[["h","Supply rail fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P220D":["NOx Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The supply voltage rail to the NOx sensor on bank 2 sensor 2 is faulty — typically a fuse, harness break, or short. NOx sensors need a clean stable supply for the heater and the wide-band measurement cell.",[["h","Supply rail fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P220E":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The heater control loop for the NOx sensor at bank 1 sensor 1 reports off-spec behaviour — heater current draw or response time outside the calibrated range. NOx sensors only operate above ~600 °C, so heater control is critical.",[["h","Heater element ageing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P220F":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The heater control loop for the NOx sensor at bank 1 sensor 2 reports off-spec behaviour — heater current draw or response time outside the calibrated range. NOx sensors only operate above ~600 °C, so heater control is critical.",[["h","Heater element ageing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2212":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The feedback line that monitors the NOx sensor heater current draw on bank 1 sensor 1 jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or harness issue.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2213":["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 2): an electrical fault is present in the circuit.",[["h","Sensor element failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,1500]],"c"],"P2214":["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","NOx sensor on bank 2 reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response, drift, or value does not match the model expectation.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,1500]],"c"],"P2215":["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 2): the signal voltage is below the expected range. Often a short to ground or high resistance in the wiring.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2216":["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 2): the signal voltage is above the expected range. Often an open circuit or a short to supply voltage.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2217":["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2): the signal is intermittent or erratic. Often a loose connector or chafed wiring; a wiggle test often locates it.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P2218":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 2): the control circuit is open. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Heater winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2219":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 2): the control-circuit voltage is below the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P221A":["NOx Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 1)","NOx sensors 1 and 2 on bank 1 disagree by more than the allowed tolerance over a drive cycle. One sensor drifts, or there is a real NOx gradient that exceeds the calibrated map.",[["h","One sensor drifts"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,2000]],"u"],"P221B":["NOx Sensor 1/2 Correlation (Bank 2)","NOx sensors 1 and 2 on bank 2 disagree by more than the allowed tolerance over a drive cycle. One sensor drifts, or there is a real NOx gradient that exceeds the calibrated map.",[["h","One sensor drifts"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,2000]],"u"],"P221C":["Reductant Heater B Current Too Low","Reductant Heater B Current Too Low: the control module has detected this fault condition. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Element partially open"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P221D":["Reductant Heater B Current Too High","Reductant Heater B Current Too High: the control module has detected this fault condition. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Element partially shorted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P221E":["Reductant Heater C Current Too Low","Reductant Heater C Current Too Low: the control module has detected this fault condition. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Element partially open"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P221F":["Reductant Heater C Current Too High","Reductant Heater C Current Too High: the control module has detected this fault condition. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Element partially shorted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P2220":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 2): the control-circuit voltage is above the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2221":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 2): an electrical fault is present in the circuit. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Sense circuit failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2222":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2): the signal is implausible or outside the valid range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Sense circuit drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2223":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 2): the signal voltage is below the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2224":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 2): the signal voltage is above the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2225":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 2)","The feedback line that monitors the NOx sensor heater current draw on bank 2 sensor 1 jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or harness issue.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,700]],"c"],"P2226":["Barometric Pressure Circuit","The ECU detects a general fault in the barometric pressure sensor circuit. The atmospheric pressure value used for altitude compensation and fuel/air calculation is not available or implausible.",[["h","Defective barometric pressure sensor"],["m","Wiring fault to BPS"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2227":["Barometric Pressure Circuit Range/Performance","The barometric pressure sensor delivers an electrically valid signal that does not match the operating point — for example pressure jumps that do not match altitude changes, or values stuck near full scale.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["m","Connector corroded"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2228":["Barometric Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","The barometric (ambient) pressure sensor reports a voltage below the valid window. The ECU uses this signal to compensate fuel and boost calculations for altitude — a stuck-low value tricks the ECU into thinking the car is at high altitude.",[["h","Barometric pressure sensor failed"],["m","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2229":["Barometric Pressure Sensor Circuit High","The barometric pressure sensor reports a voltage above the valid window. Usually a short to supply or an open ground.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P222A":["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit","A general electrical fault on barometric pressure sensor B — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. The sensor measures atmospheric pressure for altitude compensation; sensor B is a redundant or secondary unit.",[["h","Sensor failed"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P222B":["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Barometric sensor B reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response or stuck reading. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P222C":["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","Barometric sensor B below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P222D":["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","Barometric sensor B above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P222E":["Barometric Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Barometric sensor B signal jumps or drops out intermittently. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P222F":["Barometric Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","Barometric pressure sensors A and B disagree by more than the allowed tolerance. Used for redundancy on hybrid and emission-critical systems.",[["h","One sensor drifts"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2230":["Barometric Pressure Circuit Low","Voltage from the barometric pressure sensor is below the calibrated minimum. The signal is too low for any plausible atmospheric pressure, suggesting a short to ground or sensor fault.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal sensor fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2232":["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The O2 sensor signal wire on bank 1 sensor 2 has shorted to the heater wire. This pulls the signal away from a measurement of exhaust composition and produces erratic fuel-trim behaviour.",[["h","Short between signal and heater wires"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2233":["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","The O2 sensor signal wire on bank 1 sensor 3 has shorted to the heater wire. This pulls the signal away from a measurement of exhaust composition and produces erratic fuel-trim behaviour.",[["h","Short between signal and heater wires"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2234":["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The O2 sensor signal wire on bank 2 sensor 1 has shorted to the heater wire. This pulls the signal away from a measurement of exhaust composition and produces erratic fuel-trim behaviour.",[["h","Short between signal and heater wires"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2235":["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 2)","The O2 sensor signal wire on bank 2 sensor 2 has shorted to the heater wire. This pulls the signal away from a measurement of exhaust composition and produces erratic fuel-trim behaviour.",[["h","Short between signal and heater wires"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2236":["O2 Sensor Signal Circuit Shorted to Heater Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","The O2 sensor signal wire on bank 2 sensor 3 has shorted to the heater wire. This pulls the signal away from a measurement of exhaust composition and produces erratic fuel-trim behaviour.",[["h","Short between signal and heater wires"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2237":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The pumping current line of the wide-band lambda sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 is unable to operate. Wide-band sensors regulate exhaust oxygen to a reference cell via this pumping current — without it, AFR cannot be measured.",[["h","Pumping current line open"],["m","Wide-band sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2238":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Pumping current at the bank 1 sensor 1 wide-band lambda probe is below the lower limit — short to ground or sensor at end of life.",[["h","Pump line shorted to ground"],["m","Wide-band sensor aged"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2239":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","Pumping current at the bank 1 sensor 1 wide-band lambda probe is above the upper limit — short to supply or open return path.",[["h","Pump line shorted to supply"],["m","Return path to ECU open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P223A":["Reductant Heater E Control Circuit","Reductant Heater E Control Circuit: the control circuit has an electrical fault. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Heater winding or wiring fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P223B":["Reductant Heater F Control Circuit","Reductant Heater F Control Circuit: the control circuit has an electrical fault. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Heater winding or wiring fault"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P223C":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Range/Performance (Bank 1)","The pumping current of the wide-band O2 sensor on bank 1 is in electrical range but plausibility check fails. Wide-band sensors use a pumping cell that adjusts oxygen concentration in a reference chamber; the current required is proportional to lambda.",[["h","Pumping cell aged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P223D":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Range/Performance (Bank 2)","The pumping current of the wide-band O2 sensor on bank 2 is in electrical range but plausibility check fails. Wide-band sensors use a pumping cell that adjusts oxygen concentration in a reference chamber; the current required is proportional to lambda.",[["h","Pumping cell aged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P223E":["O2 Sensor Reference Resistance Out Of Range (Bank 1)","The reference resistance of the wide-band O2 sensor on bank 1 is outside the calibrated range — used by the controller to set the operating point of the pumping cell. Drift here indicates sensor element ageing or contamination.",[["h","Sensor element aged or contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P223F":["O2 Sensor Reference Resistance Out Of Range (Bank 2)","The reference resistance of the wide-band O2 sensor on bank 2 is outside the calibrated range — used by the controller to set the operating point of the pumping cell. Drift here indicates sensor element ageing or contamination.",[["h","Sensor element aged or contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P2240":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart of P2237. The wide-band lambda sensor on bank 2 sensor 1 cannot operate its pumping current circuit.",[["h","Pumping current line open on bank 2"],["m","Bank 2 wide-band sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2241":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The pumping-current line of the wide-band oxygen sensor on bank 2, sensor 1 is below the lower threshold. Wide-band sensors use a small pumping current to keep their measuring cell at lambda 1; a low value usually means an open or shorted pump cell.",[["h","Pump cell open or sensor failed"],["m","Pumping current line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2242":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","The pumping-current line of the bank 2, sensor 1 wide-band oxygen sensor reads above the upper threshold. Common with a short to a positive supply or a damaged sensor amplifier in the ECU.",[["h","Pumping current line shorted to positive"],["m","Sensor internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2243":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The reference voltage line that powers the wide-band sensor cell on bank 1 sensor 1 is missing or out of tolerance. Without correct reference, the AFR calculation is invalid.",[["h","Reference voltage line open"],["m","Wide-band sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2244":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The reference voltage that the ECU supplies to the wide-band oxygen sensor on bank 1, sensor 1 drifts outside the expected range. The reference is the baseline against which the cell voltages are measured; a drift falsifies every lambda calculation.",[["h","Reference circuit drift in ECU"],["m","High resistance in reference wiring"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2245":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The reference voltage feeding the bank 1, sensor 1 wide-band oxygen sensor is below the lower threshold. Often a short to ground in the wiring or a failed reference output stage.",[["h","Reference line shorted to ground"],["l","ECU reference output failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2246":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The reference voltage on the bank 1, sensor 1 wide-band oxygen sensor reads above the upper threshold. Common with a short to a positive supply or a corroded connector with leakage current.",[["h","Reference line shorted to positive"],["m","Connector corroded with leakage"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2247":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart of P2243. Reference voltage on the bank 2 sensor 1 wide-band probe is missing or out of tolerance.",[["h","Reference voltage line open on bank 2"],["m","Bank 2 wide-band sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2248":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2244. The reference voltage at the wide-band oxygen sensor on bank 2, sensor 1 is outside its expected range and falsifies the lambda calculation.",[["h","Reference circuit drift in ECU"],["m","High resistance in reference wiring"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2249":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2245. The reference voltage on bank 2, sensor 1 is below the lower threshold — typically a short to ground or failed ECU output.",[["h","Reference line shorted to ground"],["l","ECU reference output failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P224A":["NOx Sensor Heater Resistance (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The measured heater element resistance of the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 is outside the calibrated range. Used as a sensor-element health check.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P224B":["NOx Sensor Heater Resistance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The measured heater element resistance of the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 is outside the calibrated range. Used as a sensor-element health check.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P224C":["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit/Open","The drive circuit for the shutoff valve at the alternative-fuel tank A is open. Bi-fuel vehicles (CNG, LPG, hydrogen) use a high-pressure shutoff valve at the tank for safety; with this fault the alternative fuel cannot be drawn from the tank.",[["h","Solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P224D":["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","Alternative-fuel shutoff valve A is electrically OK but does not open when commanded. Vehicle remains on petrol/diesel only.",[["h","Valve seized closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P224E":["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit Low","Shutoff valve A drive line stuck low — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P224F":["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve A Control Circuit High","Shutoff valve A drive line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P2250":["O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2246. The reference voltage at bank 2, sensor 1 is above the upper threshold, usually due to a short to positive or connector leakage.",[["h","Reference line shorted to positive"],["m","Connector corroded with leakage"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2251":["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The negative current control line (Vs−) of the wide-band lambda sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 is open or out of range. Used as the virtual ground reference for the Nernst cell.",[["h","Vs− line open"],["m","Wide-band sensor failed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2252":["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The negative-current (Vs negative) line on the bank 1, sensor 1 wide-band oxygen sensor is below the lower threshold. This line is the return path for the Nernst cell; loss of the signal blocks the lambda calculation.",[["h","Vs negative line shorted to ground"],["m","Nernst cell return open inside sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2253":["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The Vs negative line on bank 1, sensor 1 reads above the upper threshold. Often a short to positive or a damaged ECU sensor amplifier.",[["h","Vs negative line shorted to positive"],["m","Internal short in sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2254":["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2252. The Vs negative line on the wide-band oxygen sensor at bank 2, sensor 1 is below the lower threshold.",[["h","Vs negative line shorted to ground"],["m","Nernst cell return open inside sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2255":["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","Bank 2 counterpart to P2253. The Vs negative line on bank 2, sensor 1 reads above the upper threshold.",[["h","Vs negative line shorted to positive"],["m","Internal short in sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"c"],"P2256":["O2 Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 2","The ECU detects a low-side voltage below threshold on the heater control of the rear oxygen sensor on bank 1. The heater driver may be stuck on or shorted to ground.",[["h","Heater wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal heater short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on after several drive cycles","Slightly increased fuel consumption during cold start","Delayed entry into closed-loop fuel control"],["medium",[100,400]],"c"],"P2257":["Secondary Air Injection System Control A Circuit Low","The control circuit of the secondary air injection system A reads a voltage below specification. Either the relay output is shorted to ground or the wiring/load is faulty.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Faulty SAI relay"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2258":["Secondary Air Injection System Control A Circuit High","The control circuit A of the secondary air injection system shows a voltage above the calibrated upper threshold. Likely a short to battery voltage or an open in the relay coil/output.",[["h","Control wire shorted to battery"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2259":["Secondary Air Injection System Control B Circuit Low","The drive line for secondary air injection (AIR) control circuit B is stuck low. Secondary air is pumped into the exhaust manifold during cold start to speed up catalyst light-off.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P225A":["NOx Sensor Calibration Memory (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The factory calibration memory of the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 cannot be read or contains a checksum error. Each NOx sensor ships with a unique calibration table programmed at the factory.",[["h","Sensor calibration memory corrupt"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"],["l","Supply voltage outside specification"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P225B":["NOx Sensor Calibration Memory (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The factory calibration memory of the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 cannot be read or contains a checksum error. Each NOx sensor ships with a unique calibration table programmed at the factory.",[["h","Sensor calibration memory corrupt"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"],["l","Supply voltage outside specification"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P225C":["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 1): the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Sensor poisoned by silicon, sulphur, or oil ash"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P225D":["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1): the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Sensor aged or condensate damaged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P225E":["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 reads suspiciously high for too long — biased upward or stuck. Common after sensor poisoning by silicon, sulphur, or oil ash.",[["h","Sensor poisoned"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P225F":["NOx Sensor Performance - Signal Biased/Stuck Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 reads suspiciously low for too long — biased downward or stuck. Common after sensor element ageing, condensate damage from cold start, or wiring fault that pulls the signal down.",[["h","Sensor aged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P2260":["Secondary Air Injection System Control B Circuit High","AIR system control B drive line stuck high — short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2261":["Turbo/Super Charger Bypass Valve Mechanical","The ECU detects a mechanical fault in the turbocharger or supercharger bypass valve. The valve does not open or close as commanded, causing boost-pressure errors and reduced engine response.",[["h","Stuck bypass valve"],["m","Leak in vacuum/pressure actuator"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[150,700]],"c"],"P2262":["Turbo Boost Pressure Not Detected - Mechanical","The ECU does not detect any meaningful boost pressure increase under load even though the turbocharger is commanded. Likely a mechanical defect in the turbo, charge-air piping or wastegate.",[["h","Charge pipe loose or split"],["m","Turbocharger mechanical damage"],["m","Wastegate stuck open"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P2263":["Turbo/Super Charger Boost System Performance","Boost pressure does not match the requested target during normal operation. The deviation between commanded and measured boost exceeds the calibrated tolerance, often due to leaks, sticking actuators or sensor errors.",[["h","Charge-air leak"],["h","VNT vanes sticking with soot"],["m","Boost pressure sensor drift"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2264":["Water in Fuel Sensor Circuit","The ECU detects an electrical fault in the diesel water-in-fuel sensor circuit. Until repaired, water contamination in the fuel filter cannot be detected, risking damage to the high-pressure pump and injectors.",[["h","Defective water-in-fuel sensor"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2265":["Water in Fuel Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The ECU detects that the water-in-fuel sensor signal is implausible compared to operating conditions. The reading does not change as expected during fuel filter purge or warm-up.",[["h","Sensor drift or contamination"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2266":["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit Low","The water-in-fuel sensor at the diesel fuel filter reads below lower plausibility — short to ground. The sensor warns the driver to drain the filter when condensate accumulates.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2267":["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit High","Water-in-fuel sensor reads above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2268":["Water in Fuel Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","Water-in-fuel sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["easy",[40,300]],"c"],"P2269":["Water in Fuel Condition - Sensor A","The water-in-fuel sensor at fuel filter A has detected water above the warning threshold. The fuel filter must be drained; running the engine on water-contaminated diesel can damage the high-pressure pump and injectors.",[["h","Condensate accumulated in filter — drain required"]],[],["easy",[10,100]],"c"],"P226A":["Water in Fuel Lamp Control Circuit","A general electrical fault on the drive line for the dashboard water-in-fuel warning lamp.",[["h","Lamp drive failed"]],[],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P226B":["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Boost Pressure Too High - Mechanical","Boost pressure on turbo A exceeds the upper threshold and the cause is mechanical (wastegate stuck closed, VGT vanes stuck closed) rather than electrical drive fault.",[["h","Wastegate or VGT stuck closed"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,3000]],"c"],"P226C":["Turbocharger Boost Control A Slow Response","Turbocharger Boost Control A Slow Response: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects turbo/supercharger boost-pressure control.",[["h","VGT vanes stiff or worn"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,3000]],"u"],"P226D":["Particulate Filter Deteriorated/Missing Substrate (Bank 1)","The DPF substrate on bank 1 has been detected as cracked, melted, or removed. Differential pressure across the filter is too low for the measured exhaust flow — the soot trap no longer works.",[["h","Substrate cracked or melted from runaway regen"],["m","Substrate removed by tampering"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[800,4000]],"u"],"P226E":["Particulate Filter Deteriorated/Missing Substrate (Bank 2)","The DPF substrate on bank 2 has been detected as cracked, melted, or removed. Differential pressure across the filter is too low for the measured exhaust flow — the soot trap no longer works.",[["h","Substrate cracked, melted, or removed"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[800,4000]],"u"],"P226F":["Turbocharger Boost Control B Slow Response","Turbocharger Boost Control B Slow Response: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects turbo/supercharger boost-pressure control.",[["h","VGT vanes stiff or worn"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,3000]],"u"],"P2270":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Lean (Bank 1, Sensor 2)","The downstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 reports a constant lean signal during a forced-rich command from the ECU. Suggests either a sensor that has lost its rich-side response, or a catalyst that is so degraded that no rich exhaust reaches the downstream sensor (cross-check P0420).",[["h","Downstream sensor failed stuck lean"],["m","Exhaust leak after catalyst"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[60,800]],"c"],"P2271":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Rich (Bank 1, Sensor 2)","The downstream oxygen sensor on bank 1 reports a constant rich signal during a forced-lean command. Suggests a failed downstream sensor or a sensor contaminated by oil/coolant from upstream engine wear.",[["h","Downstream sensor failed stuck rich"],["m","Downstream sensor contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2272":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Lean (Bank 2, Sensor 2)","The downstream oxygen sensor on bank 2 reports a constant lean signal during a forced-rich command from the ECU. Suggests either a sensor that has lost its rich-side response, or a catalyst that is so degraded that no rich exhaust reaches the downstream sensor (cross-check P0420).",[["h","Downstream sensor failed stuck lean"],["m","Exhaust leak after catalyst"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[60,800]],"c"],"P2273":["O2 Sensor Signal Stuck Rich (Bank 2, Sensor 2)","The downstream oxygen sensor on bank 2 reports a constant rich signal during a forced-lean command. Suggests a failed downstream sensor or a sensor contaminated by oil/coolant from upstream engine wear.",[["h","Downstream sensor failed stuck rich"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2274":["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 1 Sensor 3): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Sensor aged or contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2275":["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 1 Sensor 3)","O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 1 Sensor 3): the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Sensor coated with carbon or fuel residue"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2276":["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Lean (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","O2 sensor at bank 2 sensor 3 reports a lean reading suspiciously stable for too long. Sensor 3 is typically downstream of the second catalyst on systems with three-stage aftertreatment.",[["h","Sensor aged"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2277":["O2 Sensor Signal Biased/Stuck Rich (Bank 2 Sensor 3)","O2 sensor at bank 2 sensor 3 reports a rich reading suspiciously stable for too long. Sensor 3 is typically downstream of the second catalyst on systems with three-stage aftertreatment; sensor coated with carbon or fuel residue is the typical cause.",[["h","Sensor coated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2278":["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped Bank 1 Sensor 3 / Bank 2 Sensor 3","The PCM detects that the O2 sensor signals from bank 1 sensor 3 and bank 2 sensor 3 are swapped — typically a wiring crossover after sensor replacement.",[["h","Wiring crossover after sensor replacement"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["easy",[10,100]],"c"],"P2279":["Intake Air System Leak","The ECU has detected a discrepancy between commanded throttle/intake conditions and the resulting MAP/MAF that points to unmetered air entering after the throttle body. On turbocharged engines this often means a cracked or disconnected boost pipe between turbo and intake; on naturally aspirated engines, a hole in the intake manifold or hose.",[["h","Boost pipe disconnected or cracked"],["h","Intake hose split"]],[],["easy",[20,400]],"c"],"P227A":["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit","A general electrical fault on barometric pressure sensor C — open, shorted, or out of plausibility. The sensor measures atmospheric pressure for altitude compensation; sensor C is a redundant or secondary unit.",[["h","Sensor failed"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P227B":["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","Barometric sensor C reads in range but plausibility check fails — slow response or stuck reading. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P227C":["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Low","Barometric sensor C below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P227D":["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit High","Barometric sensor C above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P227E":["Barometric Pressure Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Barometric sensor C signal jumps or drops out intermittently. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P227F":["Air Flow Restriction/Air Leak Between Air Filter and MAF (Bank 2)","Restriction or leak detected in the intake plumbing between the air filter and the mass-air-flow sensor on bank 2 — typically a cracked intake boot or torn filter element.",[["h","Cracked intake boot"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss, hesitation under acceleration","Rough or unstable idle"],["easy",[20,300]],"u"],"P2280":["Air Flow Restriction / Air Filter Restriction","The ECU detects an excessive intake restriction. Either the air filter is heavily clogged or an obstruction in the intake duct is reducing airflow below the expected level.",[["h","Clogged air filter element"],["m","Foreign object in intake"]],[],["easy",[20,150]],"c"],"P2281":["Air Leak Between MAF and Throttle Body","The ECU detects unmetered air entering between the mass airflow sensor and the throttle body. The actual airflow into the engine is greater than what the MAF measures, leading to lean conditions.",[["h","Cracked or torn intake hose"],["m","Loose hose clamp"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss, hesitation under acceleration","Rough or unstable idle"],["easy",[30,250]],"c"],"P2282":["Air Leak Between Throttle Body and Intake Valves","The ECU detects unmetered air entering downstream of the throttle body. Typical sources are leaking intake-manifold gaskets, vacuum hoses or PCV components.",[["h","Leaking intake manifold gasket"],["m","Cracked vacuum hose"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2283":["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the injector control pressure (ICP) sensor — used on HEUI (Hydraulically actuated Electronically controlled Unit Injector) systems on heavy-duty diesel engines such as the Ford Powerstroke 6.0/7.3 and Caterpillar engines. ICP measures the high-pressure oil that actuates the injectors.",[["h","Sensor failed"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2284":["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The injector control pressure (ICP) sensor on HEUI diesel systems reports a value that does not match expected operating range or commanded pressure. Affects fuel injection timing and quantity.",[["h","ICP sensor drift"],["m","Leak in high-pressure oil system"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2285":["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","The voltage of the injector control pressure sensor is below the calibrated minimum. The signal indicates either a short to ground or a sensor that has lost its supply.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["m","Open 5 V supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2286":["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Circuit High","The voltage of the injector control pressure sensor is above the calibrated maximum. Likely a short to supply voltage or an open ground in the sensor circuit.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["m","Open ground wire"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2287":["Injector Control Pressure Sensor Intermittent","The injector control pressure sensor signal is intermittently lost or out of range. Often caused by intermittent wiring faults or a failing sensor that drops out under vibration or temperature.",[["h","Intermittent connector contact"],["m","Sensor failing under load"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2288":["Injector Control Pressure Too High","ICP is above the upper threshold during operation. Typically the injection pressure regulator (IPR) is stuck closed or the high-pressure oil pump runs above target.",[["h","IPR stuck closed"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"c"],"P2289":["Injector Control Pressure Too High - Engine Off","ICP remains above threshold after engine shutdown — pressure does not bleed off as expected, indicating a stuck check valve or sensor offset error.",[["h","Check valve stuck"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"c"],"P228A":["Fuel Pressure Regulator A - Forced Engine Shutdown","Fuel Pressure Regulator A - Forced Engine Shutdown: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Pressure runaway"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P228B":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B - Forced Engine Shutdown","Fuel Pressure Regulator B - Forced Engine Shutdown: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Pressure runaway"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P228C":["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Regulator leaks or pump weak"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P228D":["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Return path blocked or pump runaway"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P228E":["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low","Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low: the adaptive learning value has reached its lower limit, so the ECU can no longer compensate. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Long-term wear of regulator"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P228F":["Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too High","Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Learning Limits - Too High: the adaptive learning value has reached its upper limit, so the ECU can no longer compensate. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Long-term drift upward"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2290":["Injector Control Pressure Too Low","ICP is below the lower threshold — typically IPR stuck open, leaking high-pressure oil rail, or weak HP oil pump.",[["h","IPR stuck open"],["m","HP oil pump weak"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"c"],"P2291":["Injector Control Pressure Too Low - Engine Cranking","During cranking, ICP does not build up enough to fire injectors. Typical no-start condition on HEUI engines from a stuck-open IPR or weak HP oil pump.",[["h","HP oil rail does not pressurise"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"c"],"P2292":["Injector Control Pressure Erratic","ICP signal is unstable or jumps — connector or sensor issue, or air in the high-pressure oil rail. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Air in HP oil rail"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"c"],"P2293":["Fuel Pressure Regulator 2 Performance","The high-pressure fuel pressure regulator (volume control or pressure control valve on a direct-injection rail) is not maintaining commanded pressure. Often the rail-pressure sensor reading drifts away from the setpoint under load.",[["h","Pressure regulator worn or sticking"],["m","High-pressure pump weak"],["l","Rail pressure sensor drift"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2294":["Fuel Pressure Regulator 2 Control Circuit","Electrical fault on the control line to the high-pressure fuel pressure regulator solenoid. Without a working drive signal the rail cannot maintain pressure and the engine may not start or runs in limp-home.",[["h","Regulator solenoid open or shorted"],["m","Wiring break to regulator"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2295":["Fuel Pressure Regulator 2 Control Circuit Low","Drive voltage to the second fuel pressure regulator solenoid is below the lower limit. On common-rail diesels and direct-injection petrol engines this affects high-pressure fuel control directly.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Solenoid coil internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2296":["Fuel Pressure Regulator 2 Control Circuit High","Drive voltage to the second fuel pressure regulator solenoid is above the upper limit — short to supply or open ground side. The driver protection trips, regulator falls back to default.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["l","ECU driver stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2297":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","During engine deceleration with closed throttle (DFCO), the O2 sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 should swing fully lean as the manifold fills with fresh air. Code is set when the swing does not happen — usually a slow or coated sensor.",[["h","Sensor slow or coated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2298":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration (Bank 2 Sensor 1)","During engine deceleration with closed throttle (DFCO), the O2 sensor on bank 2 sensor 1 should swing fully lean as the manifold fills with fresh air. Code is set when the swing does not happen — usually a slow or coated sensor.",[["h","Sensor slow or coated"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2299":["Brake Pedal Position / Accelerator Pedal Position Correlation","The ECU detects simultaneous brake and accelerator activation beyond a permitted threshold. Modern brake-throttle override safety logic forces idle in this state — usually triggered by a stuck brake light switch or a faulty pedal sensor.",[["h","Brake light switch stuck on"],["m","Accelerator pedal sensor drift"]],[],["easy",[20,250]],"c"],"P229A":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Regulator leaks or pump weak"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P229B":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High: the control module has detected this fault condition. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Return path blocked or pump runaway"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P229C":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low","Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Learning Limits - Too Low: the adaptive learning value has reached its lower limit, so the ECU can no longer compensate. This controls fuel-rail pressure.",[["h","Long-term wear of regulator"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P229D":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Exceeded Learning Limits - Too High","The adaptive learning offset for fuel pressure regulator B has reached the upper limit. Long-term drift upward indicates progressive wear of the regulator or a return path that is becoming restricted.",[["h","Long-term drift upward"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P229E":["NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2): an electrical fault is present in the circuit.",[["h","Sensor element failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,1500]],"u"],"P229F":["NOx Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 2","The downstream NOx sensor on bank 1 (after the SCR catalyst) returns implausible NOx readings during operation. Either the sensor is degraded or upstream chemistry is abnormal.",[["h","NOx sensor aging"],["m","Low SCR efficiency"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22A0":["NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal voltage is below the expected range. Often a short to ground or high resistance in the wiring.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P22A1":["NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal voltage is above the expected range. Often an open circuit or a short to supply voltage.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P22A2":["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal is intermittent or erratic. Often a loose connector or chafed wiring; a wiggle test often locates it.",[["h","Intermittent connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P22A3":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the control circuit is open. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Heater winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P22A4":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the control-circuit voltage is below the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P22A5":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the control-circuit voltage is above the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P22A6":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit (Bank 1 Sensor 2): an electrical fault is present in the circuit. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Sense circuit failed"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P22A7":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Range/Performance (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal is implausible or outside the valid range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Sense circuit drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P22A8":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Low (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal voltage is below the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P22A9":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit High (Bank 1 Sensor 2): the signal voltage is above the expected range. The NOx sensor heater brings the sensor to operating temperature; a fault delays accurate NOx readings used for SCR control.",[["h","Open signal line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[80,800]],"u"],"P22AA":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Intermittent (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","The feedback line that monitors the NOx sensor heater current draw on bank 1 sensor 2 jumps or drops out intermittently — connector lo