ne stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22EF":["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","Cylinder 6 alternative-fuel injector drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F0":["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 6 alternative-fuel injector is electrically OK but its response (current ramp, dwell, peak voltage) is off-spec — typically winding ageing.",[["h","Winding ageing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F1":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Performance","The particulate matter (PM) sensor heater on diesel after-DPF systems does not reach or hold the calibrated operating temperature within the expected time. Without proper heating the PM sensor cannot be regenerated and read correctly.",[["h","PM sensor aging"],["m","Increased heater resistance"]],[],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22F2":["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","Cylinder 7 alternative-fuel injector drive line stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F3":["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","Cylinder 7 alternative-fuel injector drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F4":["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 7 alternative-fuel injector is electrically OK but its response (current ramp, dwell, peak voltage) is off-spec — typically winding ageing.",[["h","Winding ageing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F5":["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit/Open","The drive circuit for the cylinder 8 alternative-fuel injector is open. Bi-fuel vehicles have a second set of injectors for CNG, LPG, or hydrogen — separate from the petrol/diesel injectors.",[["h","Injector winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F6":["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Low","Cylinder 8 alternative-fuel injector drive line stuck low — short to ground. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F7":["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit High","Cylinder 8 alternative-fuel injector drive line stuck high — short to B+. A flow-deviating injector throws off cylinder balance — adjacent cylinders run leaner/richer to compensate, often masking the root cause until the trim limit is hit.",[["h","Short to B+"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F8":["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Injector Control Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 8 alternative-fuel injector is electrically OK but its response (current ramp, dwell, peak voltage) is off-spec — typically winding ageing.",[["h","Winding ageing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P22F9":["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response Low to High (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 responds too slowly when NOx concentration rises (typically observed when SCR dosing is reduced or stopped). The sensor has aged or its protection cap is clogged.",[["h","Sensor aged or protection cap clogged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22FA":["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response High to Low (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 responds too slowly when NOx concentration falls (typically observed when SCR dosing increases). The sensor has aged or its protection cap is clogged.",[["h","Sensor aged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22FB":["NOx Sensor Performance - Sensing Element (Bank 1 Sensor 1)","The wide-band sensing element of the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 1 reports an internal performance fault — typically poisoning, condensate damage, or end of service life.",[["h","Element poisoned or end of life"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22FC":["NOx Sensor Performance - Slow Response Low to High (Bank 1 Sensor 2)","NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 2 responds too slowly when NOx concentration rises (typically observed when SCR dosing is reduced or stopped). The sensor has aged or its protection cap is clogged.",[["h","Sensor aged"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P22FD":["NOx Sensor Performance Slow Response High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 2","The downstream NOx sensor on bank 1 (post-SCR) responds too slowly when NOx levels fall after a reductant injection event. The control unit measures the time between commanded reductant dose and the resulting NOx drop and finds it exceeds the diagnostic threshold, indicating an aged sensor element.",[["h","NOx sensor element aged or thermally damaged"],["m","SCR efficiency reduced (catalyst aged or contaminated)"],["l","Reductant injector dosing drift"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,900]],"u"],"P22FE":["NOx Sensor Sensing Element Bank 1 Sensor 2","NOx Sensor Sensing Element Bank 1 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Sensor element poisoned by silicone, sulphur or oil ash"],["m","Thermal shock from condensate (cold start with wet exhaust)"],["m","Sensor at end of service life"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P22FF":["SCR NOx Catalyst Inlet Temperature Too Low","The temperature sensor at the SCR catalyst inlet reports a value below the threshold needed for efficient ammonia conversion. Below roughly 180-200 °C the SCR cannot reduce NOx and reductant injection is suspended; if this is detected continuously the ECU sets the fault.",[["h","Temperature sensor drifts low or has shifted resistance"],["m","Short-trip operation - exhaust never reaches operating temperature"],["l","Exhaust heater or heat-management strategy not active"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,600]],"u"],"P2300":["Ignition Coil A Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil A reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil A cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Internal coil short"],["m","Primary wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2301":["Ignition Coil A Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil A reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil A does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Primary wire shorted to battery"],["m","Open primary winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2302":["Ignition Coil A Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil A. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil A.",[["h","Worn or fouled spark plug"],["m","Coil secondary winding failure"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2303":["Ignition Coil B Primary Control Circuit Low","The ECU reads a low primary control voltage on ignition coil B. Misfire is typically observed on the cylinder this coil serves.",[["h","Internal coil short"],["m","Primary wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2304":["Ignition Coil B Primary Control Circuit High","Voltage on the primary control of ignition coil B exceeds the calibrated upper limit, indicating an electrical fault that prevents proper coil charging.",[["h","Primary wire shorted to battery"],["m","Open primary winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2305":["Ignition Coil B Secondary Circuit","The secondary side of ignition coil B is faulty. Spark energy at the corresponding spark plug is insufficient, producing misfires.",[["h","Worn spark plug"],["m","Coil secondary failure"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2306":["Ignition Coil C Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control of ignition coil C reads below the calibrated minimum. The cylinder served by this coil will misfire.",[["h","Internal coil short"],["m","Wiring fault on coil C"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2307":["Ignition Coil C Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control voltage at ignition coil C exceeds the upper limit, suggesting a short to battery or an open primary winding.",[["h","Primary shorted to battery"],["m","Open primary winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2308":["Ignition Coil C Secondary Circuit","The secondary side of ignition coil C does not produce sufficient spark energy. Misfire is observed on the corresponding cylinder.",[["h","Worn spark plug"],["m","Coil secondary failure"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2309":["Ignition Coil D Primary Control Circuit Low","Low primary control voltage on ignition coil D. The cylinder served by this coil will misfire if not corrected quickly.",[["h","Internal coil short"],["m","Primary shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P230A":["Cylinder 1 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 1 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 1 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Local intake or vacuum leak at cylinder 1"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 1 (valves, rings)"],["l","Partial misfire from ignition or fuel-side defect"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P230B":["Cylinder 2 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 2 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 2 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Local intake or vacuum leak at cylinder 2"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 2"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P230C":["Cylinder 3 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 3 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 3 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Local intake or vacuum leak at cylinder 3"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 3"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P230D":["Cylinder 4 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 4 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 4 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Local intake or vacuum leak at cylinder 4"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 4"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P230E":["Cylinder 5 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 5 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 5 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 5"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P230F":["Cylinder 6 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 6 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 6 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 6"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P2310":["Ignition Coil D Primary Control Circuit High","The ECU detects an excessive voltage on the primary control of ignition coil D, normally caused by a short to battery or an open primary winding.",[["h","Primary shorted to battery"],["m","Open primary winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2311":["Ignition Coil D Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected in the secondary side of ignition coil D. Insufficient spark energy results in cylinder misfire.",[["h","Worn spark plug"],["m","Secondary winding failure"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2312":["Ignition Coil E Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil E reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil E cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil E internal driver fault"],["l","Connector oxidised or loose at coil E"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2313":["Ignition Coil E Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil E reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil E does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil E"],["m","Control line shorted to battery or supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2314":["Ignition Coil E Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil E. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil E.",[["h","Spark plug worn, fouled or with excessive electrode gap"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil E"],["l","Spark lead or boot cracked"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2315":["Ignition Coil F Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil F reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil F cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil F internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2316":["Ignition Coil F Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil F reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil F does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil F"],["m","Control line shorted to battery or supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2317":["Ignition Coil F Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil F. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil F.",[["h","Spark plug worn, fouled or with excessive electrode gap"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil F"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2318":["Ignition Coil G Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil G reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil G cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil G internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2319":["Ignition Coil G Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil G reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil G does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil G"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P231A":["Cylinder 7 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 7 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 7 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 7"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P231B":["Cylinder 8 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 8 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 8 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 8"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P231C":["Cylinder 9 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 9 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 9 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 9"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P231D":["Cylinder 10 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambda feedback. For cylinder 10 the per-cylinder fuel correction has hit its software-side maximum or minimum without restoring balance, indicating the underlying mechanical or fuelling deviation is too large to compensate.",[["h","Fuel injector for cylinder 10 has drifted in flow rate"],["m","Reduced compression on cylinder 10"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P231E":["Cylinder 11 Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance Adjustment At Limit During Balance","The ECU continuously trims individual cylinders to equalise air-fuel ratio across the bank using ion-current or per-cylinder lambd