ary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil H does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil H"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2323":["Ignition Coil H Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil H. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil H.",[["h","Spark plug worn or fouled"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil H"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2324":["Ignition Coil I Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil I reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil I cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil I internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2325":["Ignition Coil I Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil I reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil I does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil I"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2326":["Ignition Coil I Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil I. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil I.",[["h","Spark plug worn or fouled"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil I"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2327":["Ignition Coil J Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil J reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil J cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil J internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2328":["Ignition Coil J Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil J reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil J does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil J"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2329":["Ignition Coil J Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil J. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil J.",[["h","Spark plug worn or fouled"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil J"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P232A":["TCM Request Forced Engine Shutdown","The transmission control module (TCM) has requested an emergency engine shutdown over the powertrain bus, typically because it has detected a condition that could damage the gearbox or driveline if engine torque were not removed (e.g. severe overheating, loss of pressure or hydraulic control).",[["h","TCM internal protection logic triggered by gearbox condition"],["l","Invalid or stuck shutdown message on powertrain bus"]],[],["hard",[200,3500]],"u"],"P232B":["Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects fueling of the associated cylinders.",[["h","Injector partially clogged or coked"],["m","Injector aged - flow rate has drifted low"],["l","Increased contact resistance in injector harness"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[180,700]],"u"],"P232C":["Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","Cylinder 11 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects fueling of the associated cylinders.",[["h","Injector leaks internally or seat leaking"],["m","Injector aged - flow rate has drifted high"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[180,700]],"u"],"P232D":["Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit","Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Min Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects fueling of the associated cylinders.",[["h","Injector partially clogged or coked"],["m","Injector aged - flow rate has drifted low"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[180,700]],"u"],"P232E":["Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit","Cylinder 12 Fuel Injector A Offset Learning At Max Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects fueling of the associated cylinders.",[["h","Injector leaks internally or seat leaking"],["m","Injector aged - flow rate has drifted high"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[180,700]],"u"],"P232F":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 1 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 1 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P232F)",[["h","Sensor element slow or aged"],["m","Exhaust leak between catalyst and sensor"],["l","Sensor wiring high resistance or chafed"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P2330":["Ignition Coil K Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil K reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil K cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil K internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2331":["Ignition Coil K Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil K reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil K does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil K"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2332":["Ignition Coil K Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil K. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil K.",[["h","Spark plug worn or fouled"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil K"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2333":["Ignition Coil L Primary Control Circuit Low","The primary control circuit of ignition coil L reads a voltage below the expected level — usually a short to ground on the primary driver wire or a low-resistance fault in the coil primary winding. Coil L cannot build a normal charge, so the cylinder it fires misfires, especially under load.",[["h","Primary winding shorted to ground or harness chafed"],["m","Coil L internal driver fault"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2334":["Ignition Coil L Primary Control Circuit High","The primary control circuit of ignition coil L reads a voltage above the expected level — typically an open primary circuit or a short to battery voltage on the primary control wire. The ECU sees no normal current flow, coil L does not fire, and the cylinder misfires.",[["h","Open circuit in primary winding or harness for coil L"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2335":["Ignition Coil L Secondary Circuit","A fault is detected on the secondary (high-voltage) side of ignition coil L. The spark delivered to the plug is missing or too weak, causing a misfire on the cylinder served by coil L.",[["h","Spark plug worn or fouled"],["m","Secondary breakdown inside coil L"]],[],["easy",[60,280]],"c"],"P2336":["Cylinder 1 Above Knock Threshold","The knock sensor channel for cylinder 1 has registered combustion noise above the calibrated knock threshold beyond what the spark retard map can correct. Often associated with low-octane fuel, EGR malfunction or carbon-induced hot spots.",[["h","Low octane fuel used"],["m","Carbon deposits causing pre-ignition"],["m","EGR not lowering combustion temperature"]],[],["medium",[40,800]],"c"],"P2337":["Cylinder 2 Above Knock Threshold","The knock sensor channel for cylinder 2 has registered combustion noise above the calibrated knock threshold beyond what the spark retard map can correct. Often associated with low-octane fuel, EGR malfunction or carbon-induced hot spots.",[["h","Low octane fuel used"],["m","Carbon deposits causing pre-ignition"]],[],["medium",[40,800]],"c"],"P2338":["Cylinder 3 Above Knock Threshold","The knock sensor channel for cylinder 3 has registered combustion noise above the calibrated knock threshold beyond what the spark retard map can correct. Often associated with low-octane fuel, EGR malfunction or carbon-induced hot spots.",[["h","Low octane fuel used"],["m","Carbon deposits causing pre-ignition"]],[],["medium",[40,800]],"c"],"P2339":["Cylinder 4 Above Knock Threshold","The knock sensor channel for cylinder 4 has registered combustion noise above the calibrated knock threshold beyond what the spark retard map can correct. Often associated with low-octane fuel, EGR malfunction or carbon-induced hot spots.",[["h","Low octane fuel used"],["m","Carbon deposits causing pre-ignition"]],[],["medium",[40,800]],"c"],"P233A":["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit Open","The ECU detects an open circuit on the control line for the third (C) fuel pressure regulator. Either the regulator solenoid coil is internally open, the harness is broken, or the connector has lost contact - the ECU cannot drive the regulator and rail pressure cannot be controlled by this stage.",[["h","Open circuit in harness or connector"],["m","Regulator solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[120,450]],"u"],"P233B":["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit Low","Same as P233A but with the control line shorted to ground - the ECU measures a low voltage that does not match the commanded duty cycle.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["m","Regulator solenoid shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[120,450]],"u"],"P233C":["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Control Circuit High","Same as P233A but with the control line shorted to supply - the ECU measures a high voltage that does not match the commanded duty cycle.",[["h","Control line shorted to battery or supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[120,450]],"u"],"P233D":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit Open","The supply line that powers the solenoid of fuel pressure regulator B is open. Without supply the regulator cannot operate and the ECU cannot maintain rail pressure on this stage; sets when the controller sees no current flow even with the solenoid commanded on.",[["h","Supply line open or relay defective"],["m","Fuse for regulator B supply blown"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P233E":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit Low","The supply line that powers the solenoid of fuel pressure regulator B is below the expected voltage with the regulator commanded active - typically a high-resistance feed, partial short to ground or weak relay contact.",[["h","Supply feed has high contact resistance"],["m","Partial short to ground on supply line"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P233F":["Fuel Pressure Regulator B Solenoid Supply Voltage Control Circuit High","Same as P233D but with the supply line shorted to a higher potential than expected, so the ECU measures more voltage on the regulator B feed than the commanded level allows.",[["h","Supply line shorted to a higher voltage rail"],["l","Supply relay contact welded closed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P2340":["Cylinder 5 Above Knock Threshold","The knock-sensor evaluation reports cylinder 5 above the knock threshold over a sustained window. The ECU retards ignition for that cylinder; persistent knock indicates poor fuel quality, carbon deposits or cooling issues.",[["h","Low octane or contaminated fuel"],["m","Carbon deposits raise compression locally"],["l","Local cooling issue at cylinder 5"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P2341":["Cylinder 6 Above Knock Threshold","Same condition as P2340 but on cylinder 6 — sustained knock above the threshold with retarded ignition correction.",[["h","Low octane or contaminated fuel"],["m","Carbon deposits raise compression locally"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P2342":["Cylinder 7 Above Knock Threshold","Sustained knock above the threshold on cylinder 7 — usual causes are fuel quality, carbon deposits, or cooling issues at this cylinder.",[["h","Low octane or contaminated fuel"],["m","Carbon deposits raise compression locally"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P2343":["Cylinder 8 Above Knock Threshold","Sustained knock above the threshold on cylinder 8 — typical on V8 engines under load with poor fuel.",[["h","Low octane or contaminated fuel"],["m","Carbon deposits raise compression locally"]],[],["medium",[50,600]],"c"],"P2344":["Cylinder 9 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","The knock or combustion-vibration sensor monitors the structure-borne noise of each cylinder. The signal level for cylinder 9 has stayed above the diagnostic threshold for an extended period, indicating either persistent knock or an electrical fault that biases the channel high.",[["h","Persistent knocking on cylinder 9 (low-octane fuel, carbon deposits, hot spot)"],["m","Sensor or wiring biased high by short or moisture"],["l","Mechanical knock from bearings, piston pin or wrong torque"]],[],["medium",[120,1500]],"c"],"P2345":["Cylinder 10 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","The knock or combustion-vibration sensor monitors the structure-borne noise of each cylinder. The signal level for cylinder 10 has stayed above the diagnostic threshold for an extended period, indicating either persistent knock or an electrical fault that biases the channel high.",[["h","Persistent knocking on cylinder 10"],["m","Sensor or wiring biased high"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"]],[],["medium",[120,1500]],"c"],"P2346":["Cylinder 11 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","The knock or combustion-vibration sensor monitors the structure-borne noise of each cylinder. The signal level for cylinder 11 has stayed above the diagnostic threshold for an extended period, indicating either persistent knock or an electrical fault that biases the channel high.",[["h","Persistent knocking on cylinder 11"],["m","Sensor or wiring biased high"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"]],[],["medium",[120,1500]],"c"],"P2347":["Cylinder 12 Above Knock/Combustion Vibration Sensor Threshold","The knock or combustion-vibration sensor monitors the structure-borne noise of each cylinder. The signal level for cylinder 12 has stayed above the diagnostic threshold for an extended period, indicating either persistent knock or an electrical fault that biases the channel high.",[["h","Persistent knocking on cylinder 12"],["m","Sensor or wiring biased high"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"]],[],["medium",[120,1500]],"c"],"P2348":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the cylinder 9 combustion pressure sensor — used on engines with closed-loop combustion control (e.g. some Volvo and BMW direct-injection diesels) to measure cylinder pressure directly via a sensor at the glow plug or injector position.",[["h","Open circuit in sensor or wiring"],["m","Connector loose or oxidised"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2349":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 9 pressure sensor reads in range but plausibility check fails. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal implausible against engine model"],["m","Sensor element drifted"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P234A":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Cylinder 9 pressure sensor below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor internal short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P234B":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Cylinder 9 pressure sensor above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P234C":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Cylinder 9 pressure sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or wiring issue. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector or terminal"],["m","Harness chafed - intermittent short"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P234D":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Too Low","Cylinder 9 measured peak combustion pressure is below the calibrated minimum — typically low compression, weak injection, or stuck-open exhaust valve.",[["h","Low compression on cylinder 9 (valves, rings, head gasket)"],["m","Injector flow too low"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P234E":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Too High","Cylinder 9 measured peak combustion pressure is above the calibrated maximum — typically pre-ignition, knock, over-fuelling, or runaway combustion.",[["h","Injector overdelivery on cylinder 9"],["m","Pre-ignition or knock"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P234F":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Variation Low","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 9 is below the calibrated minimum — pressure stays unusually constant cycle-to-cycle, often a sign that the closed-loop combustion controller has lost authority or the sensor signal is filtered.",[["h","Weak combustion - low cycle-to-cycle variation"],["m","Pressure sensor signal amplitude low"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2350":["Cylinder 9 Pressure Variation High","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 9 is above the calibrated maximum — combustion is unstable cycle-to-cycle, typical of partial misfire or injector seat erosion.",[["h","Rough combustion - excessive cycle-to-cycle variation"],["m","Injector intermittent on cylinder 9"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2351":["Cylinder 9 Combustion Performance","The closed-loop combustion controller reports that combustion performance on cylinder 9 is below the calibrated quality metric. Computed from the cylinder pressure trace — IMEP (indicated mean effective pressure), CA50 (50% mass burnt angle) or peak pressure deviates from the model.",[["h","Mean effective pressure outside model"],["m","Injector flow has drifted"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2352":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the cylinder 10 combustion pressure sensor — used on engines with closed-loop combustion control (e.g. some Volvo and BMW direct-injection diesels) to measure cylinder pressure directly via a sensor at the glow plug or injector position.",[["h","Open circuit in sensor or wiring"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2353":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 10 pressure sensor reads in range but plausibility check fails. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal implausible against engine model"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2354":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Cylinder 10 pressure sensor below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2355":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Cylinder 10 pressure sensor above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2356":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Cylinder 10 pressure sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or wiring issue. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2357":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Too Low","Cylinder 10 measured peak combustion pressure is below the calibrated minimum — typically low compression, weak injection, or stuck-open exhaust valve.",[["h","Low compression on cylinder 10"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P2358":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Too High","Cylinder 10 measured peak combustion pressure is above the calibrated maximum — typically pre-ignition, knock, over-fuelling, or runaway combustion.",[["h","Injector overdelivery on cylinder 10"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P2359":["Ignition Coil L Secondary Circuit","The ECU detects a secondary-circuit fault on ignition coil L (cylinder 12 on a V12 or another high-numbered cylinder). The cylinder will misfire if the spark output is insufficient.",[["h","Worn spark plug"],["m","Coil secondary failure"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"u"],"P235A":["Cylinder 10 Pressure Variation High","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 10 is above the calibrated maximum — combustion is unstable cycle-to-cycle, typical of partial misfire or injector seat erosion.",[["h","Rough combustion - excessive variation"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P235B":["Cylinder 10 Combustion Performance","The closed-loop combustion controller reports that combustion performance on cylinder 10 is below the calibrated quality metric. Computed from the cylinder pressure trace — IMEP (indicated mean effective pressure), CA50 (50% mass burnt angle) or peak pressure deviates from the model.",[["h","Mean effective pressure outside model"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"],["l","CAN terminating resistor (120 Ω) drifted out of spec"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P235C":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the cylinder 11 combustion pressure sensor — used on engines with closed-loop combustion control (e.g. some Volvo and BMW direct-injection diesels) to measure cylinder pressure directly via a sensor at the glow plug or injector position.",[["h","Open circuit in sensor or wiring"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P235D":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 11 pressure sensor reads in range but plausibility check fails. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal implausible against engine model"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P235E":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Cylinder 11 pressure sensor below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P235F":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Cylinder 11 pressure sensor above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2360":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Cylinder 11 pressure sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or wiring issue. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2361":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Too Low","Cylinder 11 measured peak combustion pressure is below the calibrated minimum — typically low compression, weak injection, or stuck-open exhaust valve.",[["h","Low compression on cylinder 11"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P2362":["Glow Plug Module Control Module Power Circuit Low","The diesel glow plug control module reports a power-supply voltage below the operating threshold. Glow plug heating may be partially or fully disabled, causing hard cold start.",[["h","Weak battery / poor charging"],["m","Voltage drop in module supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P2363":["Glow Plug Module Control Module Power Circuit High","The voltage at the glow plug control module supply line is above the upper threshold. Indicates wiring or charging-system overvoltage condition.",[["m","Charging system overvoltage"],["m","Wiring shorted to battery"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P2364":["Cylinder 11 Pressure Variation High","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 11 is above the calibrated maximum — combustion is unstable cycle-to-cycle, typical of partial misfire or injector seat erosion.",[["h","Rough combustion - excessive variation"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2365":["Cylinder 11 Combustion Performance","The closed-loop combustion controller reports that combustion performance on cylinder 11 is below the calibrated quality metric. Computed from the cylinder pressure trace — IMEP (indicated mean effective pressure), CA50 (50% mass burnt angle) or peak pressure deviates from the model.",[["h","Mean effective pressure outside model"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"],["l","CAN terminating resistor (120 Ω) drifted out of spec"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2366":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the cylinder 12 combustion pressure sensor — used on engines with closed-loop combustion control (e.g. some Volvo and BMW direct-injection diesels) to measure cylinder pressure directly via a sensor at the glow plug or injector position.",[["h","Open circuit in sensor or wiring"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2367":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Cylinder 12 pressure sensor reads in range but plausibility check fails. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal implausible against engine model"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2368":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Cylinder 12 pressure sensor below lower plausibility — short to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P2369":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Cylinder 12 pressure sensor above upper plausibility — open signal or short to B+. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P236A":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Cylinder 12 pressure sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — connector or wiring issue. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P236B":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Too Low","Cylinder 12 measured peak combustion pressure is below the calibrated minimum — typically low compression, weak injection, or stuck-open exhaust valve.",[["h","Low compression on cylinder 12"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P236C":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Too High","Cylinder 12 measured peak combustion pressure is above the calibrated maximum — typically pre-ignition, knock, over-fuelling, or runaway combustion.",[["h","Injector overdelivery on cylinder 12"]],[],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P236D":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Variation Low","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 12 is below the calibrated minimum — pressure stays unusually constant cycle-to-cycle, often a sign that the closed-loop combustion controller has lost authority or the sensor signal is filtered.",[["h","Weak combustion - low cycle-to-cycle variation"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P236E":["Cylinder 12 Pressure Variation High","Cylinder-to-cylinder pressure variation on cylinder 12 is above the calibrated maximum — combustion is unstable cycle-to-cycle, typical of partial misfire or injector seat erosion.",[["h","Rough combustion - excessive variation"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P236F":["Cylinder 12 Combustion Performance","The closed-loop combustion controller reports that combustion performance on cylinder 12 is below the calibrated quality metric. Computed from the cylinder pressure trace — IMEP (indicated mean effective pressure), CA50 (50% mass burnt angle) or peak pressure deviates from the model.",[["h","Mean effective pressure outside model"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"],["l","CAN terminating resistor (120 Ω) drifted out of spec"]],[],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2370":["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit Open","An open circuit is detected on the control line for the second fuel volume regulator (B) used on twin high-pressure-pump diesel systems. Without this regulator the high-pressure pump cannot meter fuel for its assigned cylinder bank, leading to rail-pressure faults and limp-home behaviour.",[["h","Open in harness or connector to regulator B"],["m","Regulator solenoid winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2371":["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit Performance","The ECU sees implausible feedback on the control loop for fuel volume regulator B - duty cycle does not match measured rail pressure response. The regulator either reacts too slowly, sticks, or has shifted from its calibration.",[["h","Regulator stem sticking due to debris or wear"],["m","High-pressure pump wear changes regulator response"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P2372":["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit Low","Same as P2370 with the control line shorted to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["m","Regulator solenoid shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2373":["Fuel Volume Regulator B Control Circuit High","Same as P2370 with the control line shorted to supply. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to battery or supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2374":["Turbocharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit","The pressure sensor at the inlet of the second turbocharger (B) - on twin-turbo or sequential-turbo systems - is reporting a circuit fault. The ECU cannot determine inlet pressure and falls back to a substitute value, which limits boost control accuracy on this stage.",[["h","Open in sensor signal, supply or ground"],["m","Connector corroded by underhood moisture"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P2375":["Turbocharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P2374 but with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model under boost. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"],["m","Reference hose blocked or kinked"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P2376":["Turbocharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","Same as P2374 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P2377":["Turbocharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","Same as P2374 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P2378":["Turbocharger Inlet Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Same as P2374 but the signal is intermittent or has spikes that the ECU cannot reconcile - typically a wiring or connector fault.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector or terminal"],["m","Harness chafed or pinched"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P2379":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 2 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 2 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P2379)",[["h","Sensor element slow or aged"],["m","Exhaust leak between catalyst and sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P237A":["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P237A)",[["h","Sensing element or protective tube fouled with soot, oil or coolant"],["m","Sensor seal or thread leaks - bypass air dilutes sample"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P237B":["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 2 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 2 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P237B)",[["h","Sensing element or protective tube fouled"],["m","Sensor seal leaks - bypass air dilutes sample"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P237C":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Open","Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Open: the control circuit is open. Likely a broken wire, disconnected connector, or failed actuator.",[["h","Open in harness or connector"],["m","Actuator solenoid or motor winding open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P237D":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Low","Same as P237C with the control line shorted to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P237E":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Circuit High","Same as P237C with the control line shorted to supply. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P237F":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Performance","Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve A Control Performance: the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Flap stuck due to soot or carbon deposits"],["m","Actuator gearing worn or slipping"],["l","Position sensor offset against actual flap angle"]],[],["medium",[250,1200]],"u"],"P2380":["Wait to Start Lamp Control Circuit","The ECU detects an electrical fault on the wait-to-start indicator output of the diesel preheat system. The driver may not get a correct preheat indication.",[["m","Indicator bulb / LED failure"],["m","Wiring fault to instrument cluster"]],[],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P2381":["EGR Sensor D Circuit High","EGR Sensor D Circuit High: the signal voltage is above the expected range. Without valid EGR feedback the ECU disables exhaust gas recirculation and may set further EGR codes.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2382":["EGR Sensor D Circuit Low","Same as P2381 but with the signal voltage below the plausible lower limit - typically the signal line shorted to ground or an internal sensor short.",[["h","Signal line shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor internal short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2383":["EGR Sensor D Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P2381 but with the signal in plausible voltage range yet not matching the engine model - drift, partial blockage of the reference port, or a slow sensor.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"],["m","Reference port partially blocked by soot"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2384":["EGR Sensor D Circuit Intermittent","Same as P2381 but the signal is intermittent - typically a connector or harness fault. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector or terminal"],["m","Harness chafed or pinched"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2385":["EGR Sensor E Circuit","A circuit fault is detected on the fifth exhaust-gas recirculation sensor (E). The ECU loses this EGR feedback channel and falls back to a substitute value; emissions and EGR rate accuracy on this stage are reduced until repair.",[["h","Open in sensor signal, supply or ground"],["m","Connector corroded or contaminated"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2386":["EGR Sensor E Circuit High","EGR Sensor E Circuit High: the signal voltage is above the expected range. Without valid EGR feedback the ECU disables exhaust gas recirculation and may set further EGR codes.",[["h","Signal line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2387":["EGR Sensor E Circuit Low","Same as P2382 on EGR sensor E. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Signal line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2388":["EGR Sensor E Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P2383 on EGR sensor E. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P2389":["EGR Sensor E Circuit Intermittent","Same as P2384 on EGR sensor E. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,450]],"u"],"P238A":["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit","A general circuit fault on the secondary water-in-fuel sensor B - typically used on diesel systems with two filter housings (pre-pump and post-pump). The ECU loses water-detection feedback on this stage; risk of water reaching the high-pressure pump and injectors.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P238B":["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P238A with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P238C":["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Low","Same as P238A with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P238D":["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit High","Same as P238A with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P238E":["Water in Fuel Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","Same as P238A with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P238F":["Water in Fuel Condition Sensor B","Sensor B reports water in the fuel filter housing - drain the water trap immediately. Continued operation may cause damage to the high-pressure pump and injectors.",[["h","Water has collected in the filter trap"]],[],["easy",[20,100]],"u"],"P2390":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit Open","Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit Open: the control circuit is open. Likely a broken wire, disconnected connector, or failed actuator.",[["h","Open in actuator or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2391":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Performance","Same as P2390 with the actuator electrically intact yet not delivering the commanded position - sticky valve, broken linkage, or position offset.",[["h","Valve stuck due to soot"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2392":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit Low","Same as P2390 with the control line shorted to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2393":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Circuit High","Same as P2390 with the control line shorted to supply. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2394":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Stuck Open","Diesel intake air flow valve B is mechanically stuck open - the ECU cannot close it for anti-shudder shutdown or EGR mixing assistance.",[["h","Valve stuck open due to soot or broken linkage"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2395":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Stuck Closed","Same as P2394 with the valve stuck closed - intake airflow blocked even when the engine should run with full air.",[["h","Valve stuck closed due to soot or broken linkage"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2396":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit","A general circuit fault on the position sensor of diesel intake air flow valve B.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2397":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Range or Performance","Same as P2396 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the actuator command.",[["h","Sensor signal offset"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2398":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit Low","Same as P2396 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2399":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit High","Same as P2396 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P239A":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Same as P2396 with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P239B":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control Motor Current Range or Performance","The motor current of the actuator on diesel intake air flow B is outside the calibrated window - typically excessive (sticky valve), or too low (worn brushes).",[["h","Motor overloaded by jammed valve"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P239C":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control System High Air Flow Detected","With diesel intake air flow valve B commanded closed the measured airflow is above the calibrated threshold - valve does not seat or position sensor offset.",[["h","Valve does not seat fully"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P239D":["Diesel Intake Air Flow B Control System Low Air Flow Detected","Same as P239C with the airflow below the threshold when the valve is commanded open - valve does not open fully or the path is restricted.",[["h","Valve does not open fully"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P239E":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 1 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 1 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P239E)",[["h","Sensor element slow or aged"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P239F":["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 2 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 2 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P239F)",[["h","Sensor element slow or aged"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P23A0":["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P23A0)",[["h","Sensing element or protective tube fouled"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P23A1":["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 2 Sensor 2","O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 2 Sensor 2: the control module has detected this fault condition. (Code P23A1)",[["h","Sensing element or protective tube fouled"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"u"],"P23A2":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Open","Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Open: the control circuit is open. Likely a broken wire, disconnected connector, or failed actuator.",[["h","Open in harness or actuator"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P23A3":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Low","Same as P237D on bypass valve B. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P23A4":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Circuit High","Same as P237E on bypass valve B. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P23A5":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Performance","Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Control Performance: the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Flap stuck due to soot or carbon"]],[],["medium",[250,1200]],"u"],"P23A6":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Stuck Open","Bypass valve B is stuck in the open position - exhaust bypasses the heat exchanger continuously, slowing engine warm-up.",[["h","Valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[250,1200]],"u"],"P23A7":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Stuck Closed","Same as P23A6 with bypass valve B stuck closed - exhaust always passes through the heat exchanger.",[["h","Valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[250,1200]],"u"],"P23A8":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Stop Performance","During calibration the position sensor of bypass valve B does not reach one of its mechanical end stops as expected.",[["h","Linkage worn or slipping"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P23A9":["Communication Fault Forced Engine Shutdown","A safety-critical communication loss between control modules has triggered a forced engine shutdown. The ECU could not validate signals it needs to operate safely (e.g.",[["h","Bus communication lost"],["l","Gateway module routing CAN messages incorrectly"],["l","CAN terminating resistor (120 Ω) drifted out of spec"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"u"],"P23AA":["Turbocharger Bypass Valve A Stuck","The turbocharger bypass valve A (compressor bypass for surge protection or wastegate-style boost relief) is mechanically stuck. Boost control is impaired - either no relief on overspeed or no boost build-up depending on which position the valve is stuck in.",[["h","Valve stuck due to debris or actuator failure"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P23AB":["NOx Sensor Processor Performance Bank 1 Sensor 3","An internal self-test in the control module reports a fault in its processing of the \"NOx sensor processing, bank 1 sensor 3\" value. The module computes and cross-checks this value redundantly inside its own processor; when the results disagree, the code sets.",[["h","Internal software anomaly"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"],["l","Supply voltage outside specification"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P23AC":["NOx Sensor Circuit Bank 1 Sensor 3","A general circuit fault on the third NOx sensor of bank 1.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23AD":["NOx Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23AC with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23AE":["NOx Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23AC with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23AF":["NOx Sensor Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23AC with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B0":["NOx Sensor Circuit Intermittent Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23AC with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B1":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Open Bank 1 Sensor 3","The heater control circuit for the NOx sensor on bank 1 sensor 3 is open. Without the heater the sensor cannot reach operating temperature; readings stay invalid.",[["h","Open in heater control wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B2":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23B1 with the heater control line shorted to ground. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Heater control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B3":["NOx Sensor Heater Control Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23B1 with the heater control line shorted to supply. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Heater control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B4":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Bank 1 Sensor 3","A general circuit fault on the heater sense feedback for the bank 1 sensor 3 NOx sensor - the line over which the ECU verifies that the heater is actually drawing current.",[["h","Open in heater sense line"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23B5":["NOx Sensor Heater Sense Circuit Ra