ent biased or stuck high.",[["h","Sensor element biased high"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23BE":["NOx Sensor Performance Signal Biased or Stuck Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23BD with the sensor stuck low.",[["h","Sensor element biased low"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23BF":["NOx Sensor Performance Slow Response Low to High Bank 1 Sensor 3","NOx Sensor Performance Slow Response Low to High Bank 1 Sensor 3: the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Sensor element aged"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"],["l","5V/reference voltage unstable under load"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23C0":["NOx Sensor Performance Slow Response High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","NOx Sensor Performance Slow Response High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 3: the component is electrically intact but its response does not match the command.",[["h","Sensor element aged"],["l","Sensor element contaminated by oil, soot or coolant"],["l","5V/reference voltage unstable under load"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23C1":["NOx Sensor Sensing Element Bank 1 Sensor 3","NOx Sensor Sensing Element Bank 1 Sensor 3: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Sensor element poisoned by silicone or sulphur"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23C2":["NOx Sensor Delayed Response High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P23C0 with a measurable delay before the sensor begins to track falling levels - the start of the response is delayed, not just the slope.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[400,850]],"u"],"P23C3":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit","A general circuit fault on the position sensor of the third engine coolant bypass valve C - typically used in advanced thermal management systems with multiple coolant loops.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P23C4":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit Low","Same as P23C3 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P23C5":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Position Sensor Circuit High","Same as P23C3 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P23C6":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Driver Current or Temperature Too High","The driver stage of the coolant bypass val