s kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Feedback line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"u"],"P23D1":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Open","Per-cylinder fuel heaters (used on some heavy-duty diesels for cold-start atomisation) on cylinder 1 have an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in heater or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23D2":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","Same as P23D1 with the control line shorted to supply. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23D3":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","Same as P23D1 with the control line shorted to ground. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23D4":["Cylinder 1 Fuel Heater Performance","Cylinder 1 fuel heater is electrically intact yet does not deliver the expected heat - aged element or contact resistance high.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23D5":["Cylinder 2 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Open","Per-cylinder fuel heaters (used on some heavy-duty diesels for cold-start atomisation) on cylinder 2 have an open 