ource"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23DB":["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","Same as P23D3 on cylinder 3. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23DC":["Cylinder 3 Fuel Heater Performance","Cylinder 3 fuel heater is electrically intact yet does not deliver the expected heat - aged element or contact resistance high.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23DD":["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Open","Per-cylinder fuel heaters (used on some heavy-duty diesels for cold-start atomisation) on cylinder 4 have an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in heater or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23DE":["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit High","Same as P23D2 on cylinder 4. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23DF":["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Control Circuit Low","Same as P23D3 on cylinder 4. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23E0":["Cylinder 4 Fuel Heater Performance","Cylinder 4 fuel heater is electrically intact yet does not deliver the expected heat - aged element or contact resistance high.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"u"],"P23E1":["EGR C Control Circuit Open","A general open-circuit fault on the third EGR valve C control - typically a third EGR loop in heavy-duty engines or specific Euro-7 systems.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P23E2":["EGR C Control Circuit Performance","Same as P23E1 with the actuator electrically intact but not delivering the commanded position. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","EGR valve C sticking due to soot"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P23E3":["EGR C Control Circuit Low","Same as P23E1 with the control line shorted to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P23E4":["EGR C Control Circuit High","Same as P23E1 with the control line shorted to supply. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P23E5":["EGR C Control Stuck Open","EGR valve C is stuck in the open position - exhaust gas continuously dilutes intake air, reducing power and risking misfires at idle.",[["h","Valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P23E6":["EGR C Control Stuck Closed","Same as P23E5 with valve C stuck closed - no EGR through this stage; NOx emissions rise. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P23E7":["EGR C Flow Insufficient Detected","Same as P049B on EGR loop C. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","EGR cooler C clogged with soot"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P23E8":["EGR C Flow Excessive Detected","Same as P049C on EGR loop C. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","EGR valve C sticking open"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P23E9":["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 2","Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 2: the circuit is open. This relates to engine timing; a fault can cause rough running, a no-start, or timing errors.",[["h","Open in output wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23EA":["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Low Bank 2","Same as P23E9 with the output shorted to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23EB":["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit High Bank 2","Same as P23E9 with the output shorted to supply. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23EC":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 1","Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 1: the circuit is open. This relates to engine timing; a fault can cause rough running, a no-start, or timing errors.",[["h","Open in output wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23ED":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Low Bank 1","Same as P23EA on cam B bank 1. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23EE":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit High Bank 1","Same as P23EB on cam B bank 1. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23EF":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 2","Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Open Bank 2: the circuit is open. This relates to engine timing; a fault can cause rough running, a no-start, or timing errors.",[["h","Open in output wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23F0":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit Low Bank 2","Same as P23EA on cam B bank 2. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23F1":["Camshaft B Position Signal Output Circuit High Bank 2","Same as P23EB on cam B bank 2. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Output line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["easy",[60,250]],"u"],"P23F2":["Cylinder 1 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 1 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 1 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F3":["Cylinder 2 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 2 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 2 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F4":["Cylinder 3 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 3 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 3 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F5":["Cylinder 4 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 4 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 4 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F6":["Cylinder 5 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 5 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 5 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F7":["Cylinder 6 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 6 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 6 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F8":["Cylinder 7 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 7 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 7 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23F9":["Cylinder 8 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 8 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 8 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FA":["Cylinder 9 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 9 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 9 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FB":["Cylinder 10 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 10 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 10 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FC":["Cylinder 11 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 11 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 11 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FD":["Cylinder 12 Injector B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","On dual-injector systems (typical for some heavy-duty diesels and some petrol/gas bi-fuel applications) the secondary injector B at cylinder 12 cannot keep its mixture in balance with the rest of the bank.",[["h","Injector B for cylinder 12 has drifted in flow rate"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FE":["Bank 1 System B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","The secondary fuel system B on bank 1 (e.g. port-injection rail in a dual-injection engine, or LPG/CNG rail in a bi-fuel system) does not maintain calibrated mixture - lambda response on bank 1 is biased by an offset on the B system.",[["h","Secondary fuel system has drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P23FF":["Bank 2 System B Air-Fuel Ratio Imbalance","The secondary fuel system B on bank 2 (e.g. port-injection rail in a dual-injection engine, or LPG/CNG rail in a bi-fuel system) does not maintain calibrated mixture - lambda response on bank 2 is biased by an offset on the B system.",[["h","Secondary fuel system has drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P2400":["EVAP Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit Open","The control circuit to the EVAP leak-detection pump is open. Without that pump the ECU cannot pressurise the fuel-vapour system to test for leaks.",[["h","Leak detection pump failed"],["m","Wiring open to pump"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2401":["EVAP Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit Low","Drive voltage on the leak-detection pump line is below the lower limit. Often a short to ground in the harness.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Pump internal short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2402":["EVAP Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit High","Drive voltage on the leak-detection pump line is above the upper limit. Usually a short to supply or open ground.",[["h","Drive line shorted to supply"],["m","Pump ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2403":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Open","The leak detection pump (LDP) - which actively pressurises the EVAP system to find leaks - has an open sense circuit. The ECU cannot read the pump status during the diagnostic cycle.",[["h","Open in pump or sense wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2404":["EVAP Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Range/Performance","The sense (reed-switch or current-feedback) signal from the leak-detection pump is electrically valid but does not match expectations during a leak test. Often a worn pump diaphragm or a sticking reed contact.",[["h","Pump diaphragm worn"],["m","Reed switch intermittent"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2405":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Low","Same as P2403 with the sense voltage below the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Sense line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2406":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit High","Same as P2403 with the sense voltage above the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Sense line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2407":["EVAP Leak Detection Pump Sense Circuit Range/Performance","The leak detection pump returns a sense signal that is electrically valid but does not match the expected response during the pump's self-test or pressure cycle.",[["h","Pump diaphragm worn"],["m","Sense wiring high resistance"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2408":["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","On vehicles with a sensed fuel cap, the cap-status signal is electrically valid but does not change as expected when the cap is opened or closed.",[["h","Cap switch worn"],["m","Cap seal aged, switch never seats"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["easy",[30,150]],"c"],"P2409":["Fuel Cap Sensor or Switch Circuit Range or Performance","The sensor or switch that detects whether the fuel cap is properly closed reports a value within plausible range yet not matching driver action.",[["h","Contact drifted or dirty"]],[],["easy",[40,200]],"c"],"P240A":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit Open","The leak detection pump heater - keeps the pump diaphragm warm in cold weather - has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in heater or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P240B":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit Low","Same as P240A with the control line shorted to ground. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P240C":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Heater Control Circuit High","Same as P240A with the control line shorted to supply. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P240D":["Alternative Fuel Low Pressure System Leak","Alternative Fuel Low Pressure System Leak: a leak has been detected in this brake-hydraulic circuit, which reduces braking pressure. Safety-critical.",[["h","Hose or fitting leak"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"u"],"P240E":["Alternative Fuel High Pressure System Leak","Alternative Fuel High Pressure System Leak: a leak has been detected in this brake-hydraulic circuit, which reduces braking pressure. Safety-critical.",[["h","Hose, fitting or cylinder valve leak"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"u"],"P240F":["EGR Slow Response","The EGR system reacts to commanded changes more slowly than calibrated - typically a partly clogged EGR cooler, sticky valve, or worn actuator.",[["h","EGR valve or cooler sticky"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P2410":["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Stuck","The fuel cap status switch is stuck in one position — the ECU never sees the expected transition between open and closed.",[["h","Cap switch stuck mechanically"],["m","Connector corroded"]],[],["easy",[30,150]],"c"],"P2411":["Fuel Cap Sensor/Switch Circuit","A general electrical fault on the fuel cap sensor/switch circuit — open or short.",[["h","Signal wire open"],["m","Cap switch failed"]],[],["easy",[30,150]],"c"],"P2412":["Fuel Cap Sensor or Switch Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Same as P2409 with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["easy",[40,200]],"c"],"P2413":["Exhaust Gas Recirculation System Performance","The ECU monitors EGR flow indirectly through MAF, MAP or differential-pressure feedback and finds that actual EGR flow does not match the commanded value over a sustained period.",[["h","Carbon buildup in EGR passages"],["h","Sticking EGR valve"],["m","EGR differential pressure sensor fault"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2414":["O2 Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1 Sensor 1","Same as P237A but on the upstream sensor B1S1 (pre-catalyst). A drifted or sluggish lambda sensor lets the mixture run lean or rich without correction — fuel economy and emissions suffer immediately.",[["h","Sensing element fouled"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,350]],"c"],"P2418":["EVAP Switching Valve Control Circuit Performance","The evaporative switching valve — used on multi-path EVAP systems to route purge or pressure-test flow — does not respond as expected. Self-test fails because tank pressure does not change in the calibrated direction.",[["h","Switching valve failed"],["m","EVAP line blocked or kinked"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2419":["EVAP Switching Valve Stuck Open","The EVAP switching valve cannot close. Tank pressure cannot be isolated for the leak detection test, and purge routing may bypass the canister.",[["h","Valve stuck open mechanically"],["m","Drive circuit always energised"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P241A":["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped Bank 1 Sensor 1 and Sensor 2","The pre- and post-catalyst lambda signals on bank 1 are swapped - the upstream sensor responds like a downstream sensor and vice versa. Typically the harness was reversed during a sensor change.",[["h","Harness swapped during repair"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["easy",[40,150]],"u"],"P241B":["O2 Sensor Signals Swapped Bank 2 Sensor 1 and Sensor 2","The pre- and post-catalyst lambda signals on bank 2 are swapped - the upstream sensor responds like a downstream sensor and vice versa. Typically the harness was reversed during a sensor change.",[["h","Harness swapped during repair"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["easy",[40,150]],"u"],"P241C":["Throttle Actuator Control System Ice Blockage Bank 2","The throttle actuator on bank 2 cannot move because of ice formation - typical for very cold ambient temperature with humid intake. Engine de-ices on warm-up.",[["h","Ice in throttle bore"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["easy",[10,100]],"u"],"P241D":["SCR Inducement Forced Engine Shutdown","The SCR inducement strategy (mandatory regulatory measure to enforce AdBlue refilling and emissions compliance) has reached the final stage and shut down the engine. Refill AdBlue and clear inducement fault to restart.",[["h","AdBlue tank empty or out of compliance"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[20,200]],"u"],"P241E":["Reductant Heater Coolant Control Valve Stuck Closed","The valve that routes engine coolant to heat the AdBlue lines is stuck closed - AdBlue lines do not warm up and may freeze in cold weather, blocking dosing.",[["h","Valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P241F":["EGR Cooler B Efficiency Below Threshold","The temperature drop across EGR cooler B is below the calibrated threshold - cooler is fouled with soot, has internal scaling, or coolant flow is restricted. Recirculated gas reaches the intake hotter than designed, increasing NOx and combustion temperatures.",[["h","Cooler fouled with soot or scaled"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[400,1500]],"u"],"P2420":["EVAP Switching Valve Stuck Closed","The EVAP switching valve cannot open when commanded. Purge or test flow cannot reach the appropriate path and the leak monitor aborts.",[["h","Valve stuck closed mechanically"],["m","Drive circuit open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2421":["EVAP Vent Valve Stuck Open","The evaporative emission system vent valve does not close on command. The ECU detects that the evap system cannot hold pressure or vacuum because the canister is permanently vented to atmosphere.",[["h","Vent valve mechanically stuck open"],["m","Dust/debris preventing valve seat"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[60,250]],"c"],"P2422":["EVAP Canister Vent Valve Stuck Closed","The vent valve at the canister end of the EVAP system cannot open. Without ambient air entering the canister, fresh fuel cannot purge the stored vapors and refueling may trigger ORVR issues.",[["h","Vent valve seized closed"],["m","Drive circuit open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[40,350]],"c"],"P2423":["HC Adsorption Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold Bank 1","The ECU determines that the hydrocarbon adsorption catalyst on bank 1 no longer holds enough HC during cold start to meet emission targets. Often due to ageing or thermal damage.",[["h","Catalyst aging / thermal damage"],["m","Oxygen sensor drift"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[800,3000]],"c"],"P2424":["HC Adsorption Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold Bank 2","The hydrocarbon adsorption catalyst on bank 2 - which traps HC during cold-start until the main catalyst lights off - is degraded; HC slip during cold start is above the calibrated threshold.",[["h","Catalyst adsorber aged"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,1800]],"c"],"P2425":["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit Open","The valve that admits coolant flow to the EGR cooler has an open control circuit - cooling cannot be enabled and EGR temperatures stay too high.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2426":["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit Low","Same as P2425 with the control line shorted to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2427":["EGR Cooling Valve Control Circuit High","Same as P2425 with the control line shorted to supply. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2428":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Too High Bank 1","An EGT sensor on bank 1 reports a temperature above the safety threshold for prolonged operation - typical for blocked DPF, restricted exhaust, or excessive fuelling. Risk of catalyst, DPF or turbo damage.",[["h","DPF blocked or active regeneration"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2429":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Too High Bank 2","An EGT sensor on bank 2 reports a temperature above the safety threshold for prolonged operation - typical for blocked DPF, restricted exhaust, or excessive fuelling. Risk of catalyst, DPF or turbo damage.",[["h","DPF blocked or active regeneration"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"c"],"P242A":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 1 Sensor 3","A general circuit fault is detected on the EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 3 (typically just downstream of the turbo or before the catalyst). The ECU loses thermal protection feedback for the catalyst and DPF.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P242B":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P242A with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P242C":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P242A with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P242D":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P242A with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P242E":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 1 Sensor 3","Same as P242A with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P242F":["Particulate Filter Restriction Ash Accumulation Bank 1","The diesel particulate filter on bank 1 reports backpressure attributable to ash (non-combustible residue from oil and fuel additives, not removable by regeneration). The filter has reached the end of its service life and needs cleaning or replacement.",[["h","DPF full of ash"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[800,3500]],"c"],"P2430":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Bank 1","A general circuit fault on the secondary air injection (AIR) system flow or pressure sensor on bank 1 - the sensor that verifies air pump flow during cold-start enrichment compensation.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2431":["Secondary Air Injection System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit","The ECU detects a general fault in the secondary air injection system air flow or pressure sensor circuit. The diagnostic cannot verify proper SAI operation.",[["h","Defective SAI sensor"],["m","SAI sensor wiring fault"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2432":["Secondary Air Injection System Air Flow/Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The signal of the SAI air flow or pressure sensor is implausible during operation. The reading does not change as expected when the air pump is commanded.",[["h","Clogged SAI passages"],["m","SAI sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2433":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","Same as P2430 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2434":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 1","Same as P2430 with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2435":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Bank 2","AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Bank 2: an electrical fault is present in the circuit.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2436":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 2","Same as P2430 on bank 2 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2437":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2","AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2: the signal voltage is below the expected range. Often a short to ground or high resistance in the wiring.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2438":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit High Bank 2","Same as P2433 on bank 2. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P2439":["AIR System Air Flow or Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 2","Same as P2434 on bank 2. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,450]],"c"],"P243A":["Particulate Filter Restriction Ash Accumulation Bank 2","The diesel particulate filter on bank 2 reports backpressure attributable to ash (non-combustible residue from oil and fuel additives, not removable by regeneration). The filter has reached the end of its service life and needs cleaning or replacement.",[["h","DPF full of ash"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[800,3500]],"u"],"P243B":["Particulate Filter Restriction Forced Limited Power Bank 2","Particulate Filter Restriction Forced Limited Power Bank 2: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","DPF heavily clogged"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3500]],"u"],"P243C":["Particulate Filter Regeneration Frequency Bank 2","The DPF on bank 2 needs regeneration more often than calibrated. Possible causes are an oil-burning engine, fuel-injector leak, short-trip operation, or a sensor offset.",[["h","Short-trip operation"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P243D":["Particulate Filter Regeneration Duration Bank 2","Regenerations on bank 2 take longer than calibrated to complete - typically a low EGT during the cycle (cold weather, short trips) or a partially aged catalyst before the DPF.",[["h","Regeneration too slow"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P243E":["Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete Bank 2","Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete Bank 2: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Regeneration aborted before completion"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[50,500]],"u"],"P243F":["Particulate Filter Restriction Soot Accumulation Too High Bank 2","Particulate Filter Restriction Soot Accumulation Too High Bank 2: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Soot loading critical"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P2440":["Secondary Air Injection System Switching Valve Stuck Open (Bank 1)","The switching/check valve in the secondary air injection plumbing on bank 1 is stuck in the open position. With the valve permanently open, exhaust gas can back-feed into the air pump and corrode it, while the downstream O2 sensor sees ambient air constantly.",[["h","Switching valve stuck open by carbon or corrosion"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2441":["Secondary Air Injection System Switching Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 1)","The switching valve on bank 1 will not open when commanded, so no secondary air reaches the exhaust during cold start. Catalyst light-off is delayed and emissions during the cold-start window rise.",[["h","Switching valve stuck closed by carbon"],["m","Vacuum control line leak"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2442":["Secondary Air Injection System Switching Valve Stuck Open (Bank 2)","The switching/check valve in the secondary air injection plumbing on bank 2 is stuck in the open position. With the valve permanently open, exhaust gas can back-feed into the air pump and corrode it, while the downstream O2 sensor sees ambient air constantly.",[["h","Switching valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2443":["Secondary Air Injection System Switching Valve Stuck Closed (Bank 2)","The switching valve on bank 2 will not open when commanded, so no secondary air reaches the exhaust during cold start. Catalyst light-off is delayed and emissions during the cold-start window rise.",[["h","Switching valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2444":["Secondary Air Injection System Pump Stuck Off (Bank 1)","The secondary-air pump does not run when commanded during cold start. Often a seized pump (after exhaust back-feed corroded the impeller), a blown fuse, or a failed relay.",[["h","Pump seized by corrosion"],["m","Pump relay failed"],["m","Pump fuse blown"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2445":["Secondary Air Injection System Pump Stuck On (Bank 1)","The secondary-air pump continues to run after the cold-start window, when the ECU has commanded it off. Usually a stuck-closed relay welding the pump permanently to battery voltage.",[["h","Pump relay stuck closed"],["m","Drive line shorted to supply"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2446":["Secondary Air Injection Pump Stuck Off (Bank 2)","Bank 2 secondary air pump does not deliver air when commanded. The catalyst light-off process is delayed and cold-start emissions rise.",[["h","Pump seized from condensate corrosion"],["m","Relay failed open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[200,900]],"c"],"P2447":["Secondary Air Injection Pump Stuck On (Bank 2)","Bank 2 secondary air pump runs continuously. Either a stuck-on relay or a shorted control output keeps the pump powered when it should be off.",[["h","Relay stuck closed"],["m","Driver stage shorted on"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2448":["AIR System High Air Flow Bank 1","The secondary air injection system on bank 1 delivers more flow than calibrated when the pump is commanded on - typically a stuck-open switching valve allowing free flow.",[["h","AIR switching valve stuck open"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P2449":["AIR System High Air Flow Bank 2","The secondary air injection system on bank 2 delivers more flow than calibrated when the pump is commanded on - typically a stuck-open switching valve allowing free flow.",[["h","AIR switching valve stuck open"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P244A":["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too Low","The differential pressure across the DPF is below the calibrated minimum even at higher loads. Often a sign of a damaged or missing filter substrate, or a leak in the sensing line.",[["h","Cracked or missing DPF substrate"],["m","Leak in pressure sensing line"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P244B":["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Sensor Offset","At engine off, the DPF differential pressure sensor does not return to zero within the allowed offset window. The static offset is too large to be ignored.",[["h","Sensor zero-point drift"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P244C":["Exhaust Temperature Too Low For Particulate Filter Regeneration Bank 1","During an attempted regeneration of the bank 1 DPF the EGT did not reach the temperature window needed for soot oxidation. Regeneration could not start or was held.",[["h","Engine load too low for regeneration"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P244D":["Exhaust Temperature Too High For Particulate Filter Regeneration Bank 1","Same as P244C with the EGT too high - regeneration paused to protect filter substrate from melt damage.",[["h","Engine load too high - filter overheating risk"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[50,500]],"c"],"P244E":["Exhaust Temperature Too Low For Particulate Filter Regeneration Bank 2","During an attempted regeneration of the bank 2 DPF the EGT did not reach the temperature window needed for soot oxidation. Regeneration could not start or was held.",[["h","Engine load too low for regeneration"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P244F":["Exhaust Temperature Too High For Particulate Filter Regeneration Bank 2","Same as P244D on bank 2.",[["h","Engine load too high - filter overheating risk"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[50,500]],"c"],"P2450":["EVAP System Switching Valve Performance/Stuck","The EVAP switching valve does not respond to commands as expected. The valve is mechanically stuck or unable to switch between purge and vent paths, blocking proper leak diagnosis.",[["h","Mechanical failure of valve"],["m","Contamination preventing motion"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2451":["EVAP System Switching Valve Stuck Closed","The EVAP switching valve - which directs vapor flow between purge and leak-detection paths - is stuck in the closed position. The diagnostic cycle cannot complete.",[["h","Valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2452":["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general electrical fault on the DPF differential-pressure sensor circuit. Without a valid pressure reading the ECU cannot estimate soot load and may inhibit regeneration.",[["h","DPF pressure sensor failed"],["m","Sensor sample hoses clogged with soot"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P2453":["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The DPF differential-pressure sensor produces a value that is electrically valid but does not match expectations — for example a non-zero reading with engine off or no change between idle and load.",[["h","Sample hoses clogged or kinked"],["m","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P2454":["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Voltage on the DPF differential-pressure sensor signal line is below the lower threshold. Typically a short to ground or an open in the supply line.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Reference voltage line open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,300]],"c"],"P2455":["Diesel Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Voltage on the DPF pressure sensor line exceeds the upper threshold. Usually a short to supply or an open ground on the sensor.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["m","Sensor ground open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,300]],"c"],"P2456":["DPF Differential Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","The DPF differential-pressure sensor delivers an intermittent signal — usually a marginal connector or a chafed wiring section that breaks contact during temperature or vibration.",[["h","Connector intermittent"],["m","Wiring chafed against bracket"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[50,250]],"c"],"P2457":["EGR Cooler Performance","The EGR cooler does not lower exhaust gas temperature as expected — typically internal coolant fouling, a partial blockage, or a cracked cooler that mixes coolant with exhaust gas.",[["h","Cooler internally clogged with soot"],["m","Cooler cracked, coolant entering exhaust"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["hard",[400,2500]],"c"],"P2458":["DPF Regeneration Duration","The DPF regeneration cycle takes longer than the calibrated maximum. The ECU sets this code when the soot load is not being burned off within the expected window — common after many short trips or with degraded post-injection.",[["h","Heavy soot load, short trips"],["m","Post-injection insufficient"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2459":["Diesel Particulate Filter Regeneration Frequency","Active DPF regenerations are being requested more often than the calibration window allows. Indicates that soot accumulates faster than the filter can burn it off — typically due to short-trip use, leaking injectors, or excessive engine oil consumption.",[["h","Predominantly short-trip operation"],["m","Leaking injector raises soot output"],["m","High engine oil consumption (turbo seals, valve stems)"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[100,1500]],"c"],"P245A":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Open Bank 1","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 1 - routes EGR around the cooler during cold-start to keep cabin and engine warm-up fast - has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P245B":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Range or Performance Bank 1","Same as P245A with the actuator electrically intact yet not delivering the commanded position. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Bypass valve sticking due to soot"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P245C":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Low Bank 1","Same as P245A with the control line shorted to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P245D":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit High Bank 1","Same as P245A with the control line shorted to supply. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"c"],"P245E":["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit","A general circuit fault on the secondary differential pressure sensor B across the DPF - measures backpressure for the regeneration strategy.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P245F":["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P245E with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2460":["DPF Restriction — Forced Limited Power","The DPF restriction has reached a level that forces the ECU to limit engine power. The driver must allow a forced regeneration or have the filter serviced before normal power is restored.",[["h","Heavy soot load, regenerations skipped"],["m","Ash loaded near service interval"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3500]],"c"],"P2461":["DPF Restriction — Forced Limited","The DPF restriction has reached the limit defined for forced limited operation. Vehicle behaviour depends on the manufacturer — usually a hard torque cap with a service warning.",[["h","Heavy soot load, regenerations skipped"],["m","Ash loaded near service interval"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3500]],"c"],"P2462":["Diesel Particulate Filter Restriction - Soot Accumulation","The DPF differential pressure sensor reports a backpressure rise consistent with excessive soot accumulation. The filter cannot regenerate fast enough, eventually causing limp mode.",[["h","Repeated failed regeneration cycles"],["h","Heavily clogged DPF"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[300,3000]],"c"],"P2463":["Diesel Particulate Filter Restriction — Soot Accumulation","The estimated soot mass in the DPF has crossed the upper limit and the ECU could not complete a regeneration to bring it back down. Very common on cars used on short trips.",[["h","DPF heavily loaded after multiple aborted regenerations"],["h","Predominantly short-trip operation"],["l","Differential pressure sensor reading drifted high"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[150,3500]],"c"],"P2464":["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Too High","The differential pressure across the DPF exceeds the calibrated upper threshold during operation. Indicates severe blockage of the filter element.",[["h","DPF heavily clogged"],["l","Blocked pressure sensing line"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P2465":["Diesel Particulate Filter Differential Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","The DPF differential pressure sensor signal is implausible compared to engine load and exhaust flow. Either the sensor or the pressure tubes leading to it are at fault.",[["h","Soot/water clogged pressure tubes"],["m","Sensor drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2466":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 2 Sensor 3","A general circuit fault is detected on the EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 3 (typically just downstream of the turbo or before the catalyst). The ECU loses thermal protection feedback for the catalyst and DPF.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2467":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 2 Sensor 3","Same as P242B on bank 2 sensor 3.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2468":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2 Sensor 3","Same as P242C on bank 2 sensor 3. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2469":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 2 Sensor 3","Same as P242D on bank 2 sensor 3. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P246A":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 2 Sensor 3","Same as P242E on bank 2 sensor 3. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P246B":["Vehicle Conditions Incorrect for Particulate Filter Regeneration","The driving pattern (short trips, low speed, frequent stops) does not provide the load and EGT needed for passive or active DPF regeneration. Filter loading rises until limit reached.",[["h","Short-trip operation"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P246C":["Particulate Filter Restriction Forced Limited Power Bank 1","Particulate Filter Restriction Forced Limited Power Bank 1: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","DPF heavily clogged"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,3500]],"c"],"P246D":["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor A and B Correlation","The two DPF differential pressure sensors A and B disagree by more than the diagnostic tolerance - one of them has drifted.",[["h","One sensor has drifted"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P246E":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 1 Sensor 4","A general circuit fault is detected on the EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 4 (typically just downstream of the turbo or before the catalyst). The ECU loses thermal protection feedback for the catalyst and DPF.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2474":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 2 Sensor 4","Same as P242B on bank 2 sensor 4.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2475":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2 Sensor 4","Same as P242C on bank 2 sensor 4. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2476":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 2 Sensor 4","Same as P242D on bank 2 sensor 4. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2477":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 2 Sensor 4","Same as P242E on bank 2 sensor 4. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2478":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 1 Sensor 1","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 1 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2479":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 1 Sensor 2","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 2 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247A":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 1 Sensor 3","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 3 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247B":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 1 Sensor 4","The EGT sensor at bank 1 sensor 4 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247C":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 2 Sensor 1","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 1 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247D":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 2 Sensor 2","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 2 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247E":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 2 Sensor 3","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 3 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P247F":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Out of Range Bank 2 Sensor 4","The EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 4 reports a value outside its plausible operating range over time - typically a degraded element giving an offset that the substitute logic flags as implausible.",[["h","Sensor element aged"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2481":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 5","Same as P242C on bank 1 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2482":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 5","Same as P242D on bank 1 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2483":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 1 Sensor 5","Same as P242B on bank 1 sensor 5.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2484":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 1 Sensor 5","Same as P242E on bank 1 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2485":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Open Bank 2 Sensor 5","A general circuit fault is detected on the EGT sensor at bank 2 sensor 5 (typically just downstream of the turbo or before the catalyst). The ECU loses thermal protection feedback for the catalyst and DPF.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2486":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2 Sensor 5","Same as P242C on bank 2 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2487":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 2 Sensor 5","Same as P242D on bank 2 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2488":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range or Performance Bank 2 Sensor 5","Same as P242B on bank 2 sensor 5.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2489":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 2 Sensor 5","Same as P242E on bank 2 sensor 5. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P248A":["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit Low","Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit Low: the signal voltage is below the expected range. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Sense line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P248B":["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit High","Same as P248A with the sense voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sense line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P248C":["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit Low","Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit Low: the signal voltage is below the expected range. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Sense line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P248D":["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit High","Same as P248B on heater B. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sense line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P248E":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Open Bank 2","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 2 - routes EGR around the cooler during cold-start to keep cabin and engine warm-up fast - has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P248F":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Range or Performance Bank 2","Same as P245B on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Bypass valve sticking due to soot"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2490":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Low Bank 2","Same as P245C on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2491":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit High Bank 2","Same as P245D on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P2492":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Bank 1","A general circuit fault on the position feedback sensor of the EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 1. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2493":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Range or Performance Bank 1","Same as P2492 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the actuator command. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Sensor signal offset"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2494":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1","Same as P2492 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2495":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","Same as P2492 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2496":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 1","Same as P2492 with intermittent or erratic signal. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2497":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Bank 2","A general circuit fault on the position feedback sensor of the EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2498":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Range or Performance Bank 2","Same as P2493 on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Sensor signal offset"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P2499":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2","Same as P2494 on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P249A":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit High Bank 2","Same as P2495 on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P249B":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent or Erratic Bank 2","Same as P2496 on bank 2. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[150,500]],"u"],"P249C":["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control","After cold start the AdBlue injection runs open-loop until SCR temperature is reached. The transition into closed-loop is taking longer than calibrated.",[["h","SCR warm-up slow"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P249D":["Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control At Limit Flow Too Low","With reductant injection running closed-loop the controller drives the dosing valve to maximum opening but cannot reach the required AdBlue flow.",[["h","Reductant pump pressure low"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P249E":["Closed Loop Reductant Injection Control At Limit Flow Too High","Same as P249D with the controller fully closing the dosing valve yet still measuring more flow than needed - the valve does not seat fully.",[["h","Dosing valve does not seat fully"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[300,1500]],"u"],"P249F":["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control","The DPF regeneration controller cannot transition into its closed-loop temperature control quickly enough - typically because EGT does not rise to setpoint within the calibrated window.",[["h","EGT rise too slow"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P24A0":["Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control At Limit Temperature Too Low","With regeneration running closed-loop the controller is at maximum heat-input demand yet cannot raise EGT to setpoint - typical for a load-poor drive cycle.",[["h","Drive cycle load too low"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[20,200]],"u"],"P24A1":["Closed Loop Particulate Filter Regeneration Control At Limit Temperature Too High","Same as P24A0 with the controller fully reducing heat input yet EGT still rising - typical for a runaway exotherm in the DPF (oil contamination).",[["h","DPF runaway exotherm"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,3500]],"u"],"P24A2":["Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete Bank 1","Particulate Filter Regeneration Incomplete Bank 1: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Regeneration aborted before completion"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[50,500]],"u"],"P24A3":["Particulate Filter Restriction Soot Accumulation Bank 2","The DPF on bank 2 has accumulated soot beyond the normal operating window. Active regeneration will be requested.",[["h","Soot loading high"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[50,800]],"u"],"P24A4":["Particulate Filter Restriction Soot Accumulation Too High Bank 1","Particulate Filter Restriction Soot Accumulation Too High Bank 1: the control module has detected this fault condition.",[["h","Soot loading critical"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P24A5":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Open Bank 1","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 1 is mechanically stuck in the open (bypassing) position - EGR always bypasses the cooler, gas reaches the intake hotter than designed.",[["h","Valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24A6":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Open Bank 2","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 2 is mechanically stuck in the open (bypassing) position - EGR always bypasses the cooler, gas reaches the intake hotter than designed.",[["h","Valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24A7":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit Open","The dedicated coolant pump for the EGR cooler has an open control circuit - the pump cannot run, EGR cooler temperature rises beyond the safety threshold.",[["h","Open in pump or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24A8":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Performance Stuck Off","The pump is electrically intact but does not deliver flow when commanded - typically a worn impeller or seized rotor.",[["h","Pump impeller worn or rotor seized"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24A9":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit Low","Same as P24A7 with the control line shorted to ground. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24AA":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Control Circuit High","Same as P24A7 with the control line shorted to supply. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24AB":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Stuck On","The pump or its driver is stuck on - the pump runs continuously, even with the engine off, draining battery and bleeding heat from the engine.",[["h","Driver stage stuck on"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24AC":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit Low","The feedback line that confirms pump speed reads below the plausible range - either pump not turning or feedback line shorted to ground.",[["h","Feedback line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24AD":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit High","Same as P24AC with the feedback line shorted to supply. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Feedback line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24AE":["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit","A general circuit fault on the particulate matter (PM) sensor - measures soot in the exhaust downstream of the DPF to verify regeneration.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24AF":["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24AE with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B0":["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Low","Same as P24AE with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B1":["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit High","Same as P24AE with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B2":["Particulate Matter Sensor Circuit Intermittent","Same as P24AE with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B3":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Open","The PM sensor heater (regenerates the sensor by burning off accumulated soot) has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in heater or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B4":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24B3 with the heater control loop in plausible range yet not matching the heater model. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B5":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low","Same as P24B3 with the control line shorted to ground. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B6":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit High","Same as P24B3 with the control line shorted to supply. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B7":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Resistance","The resistance of the PM sensor heater is outside the calibrated band.",[["h","Heater element aged"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24B8":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit","A general circuit fault on the LDP internal pressure sensor. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24B9":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24B8 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the pump operating curve. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BA":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Same as P24B8 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BB":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Same as P24B8 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BC":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","Same as P24B8 with intermittent or erratic signal. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BD":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit Open","The switching valve in the LDP - directs pump output between EVAP test path and reference orifice - has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BE":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit Low","Same as P24BD with the control line shorted to ground. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24BF":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Control Circuit High","Same as P24BD with the control line shorted to supply. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24C0":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Stuck On","The LDP switching valve is stuck in the activated position. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Valve stuck on"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24C1":["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Switching Valve Performance Stuck Off","Same as P24C0 with the valve stuck off. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Valve stuck off"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["medium",[120,400]],"u"],"P24C2":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Measurement System Multiple Sensor Correlation Bank 1","The multiple EGT sensors on bank 1 disagree by more than the diagnostic tolerance under stable conditions - one of them has drifted relative to the others.",[["h","One sensor has drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24C3":["Exhaust Gas Temperature Measurement System Multiple Sensor Correlation Bank 2","The multiple EGT sensors on bank 2 disagree by more than the diagnostic tolerance under stable conditions - one of them has drifted relative to the others.",[["h","One sensor has drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24C4":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit Bank 1","The bypass valve position sensor learning has reached its software-side limit on bank 1 - typically heavy soot deposits have shifted the mechanical zero beyond the design adaptation range.",[["h","Heavy carbon build-up on valve seat"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P24C5":["EGR Cooler Bypass Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit Bank 2","The bypass valve position sensor learning has reached its software-side limit on bank 2 - typically heavy soot deposits have shifted the mechanical zero beyond the design adaptation range.",[["h","Heavy carbon build-up on valve seat"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P24C6":["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit","A general circuit fault on the temperature element of the PM sensor - used to verify that the sensor is hot enough for measurement after regeneration.",[["h","Open in temperature element"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24C7":["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24C6 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Temperature element drifted"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24C8":["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Low","Same as P24C6 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24C9":["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit High","Same as P24C6 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24CA":["Particulate Matter Sensor Temperature Circuit Intermittent","Same as P24C6 with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24CB":["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit","A general circuit fault on the AdBlue tank cap switch - reports whether the cap is properly closed.",[["h","Open in switch or wiring"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P24CC":["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24CB with input in plausible range yet not matching driver action.",[["h","Contact drifted"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P24CD":["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Low","Same as P24CB with the signal shorted to ground. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P24CE":["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit High","Same as P24CB with the signal shorted to supply. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P24CF":["Reductant Tank Cap Switch Circuit Intermittent or Erratic","Same as P24CB with intermittent or erratic signal. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["easy",[40,200]],"u"],"P24D0":["Particulate Matter Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The PM sensor supply voltage is below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Supply voltage low"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24D1":["Particulate Matter Sensor Regeneration Incomplete","A sensor regeneration cycle (heating to burn off accumulated soot) did not complete - sensor cannot return to measurement mode.",[["h","Regeneration aborted before completion"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24D2":["Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit","Reductant Heater A Sense Circuit: an electrical fault is present in the circuit. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Open in sense wiring"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P24D3":["Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit","Reductant Heater B Sense Circuit: an electrical fault is present in the circuit. The reductant (DEF/AdBlue) heater keeps the urea fluid from freezing; a fault can impair SCR dosing in cold conditions.",[["h","Open in sense wiring"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,700]],"u"],"P24D4":["EGR Cooler Coolant Pump Feedback Circuit","A general circuit fault on the feedback line that the EGR cooler coolant pump reports speed on. EGR mixes inert exhaust into intake to lower combustion peak temperature — too little raises NOx, too much causes misfires and rough running.",[["h","Open in feedback wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24D5":["EVAP System Pressure Sensor or Switch B Circuit","A general circuit fault on the secondary EVAP system pressure sensor or switch B. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P24D6":["EVAP System Pressure Sensor or Switch B Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24D5 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P24D7":["EVAP System Pressure Sensor or Switch B Circuit Low","Same as P24D5 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P24D8":["EVAP System Pressure Sensor or Switch B Circuit High","Same as P24D5 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P24D9":["EVAP System Pressure Sensor or Switch B Circuit Intermittent","Same as P24D5 with intermittent or erratic signal. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Intermittent contact at connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["easy",[80,280]],"u"],"P24DA":["Particulate Matter Sensor Exhaust Sample Error Bank 1","The PM sensor on bank 1 cannot acquire a valid exhaust sample - probe fouled, exhaust path obstructed at sensor, or sensor seal leaking.",[["h","Sensing element fouled"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24DB":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit Open","The secondary reductant purge valve B - which clears AdBlue from injector and lines at shutdown to prevent crystallisation - has an open control circuit.",[["h","Open in valve or wiring"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24DC":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Performance","Same as P24DB with the actuator electrically intact yet not delivering the commanded purge flow. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Purge valve sticking"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24DD":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit Low","Same as P24DB with the control line shorted to ground. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Control line shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24DE":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Circuit High","Same as P24DB with the control line shorted to supply. The evaporative system captures fuel vapor from the tank and purges it into intake; leaks or stuck purge valves leak hydrocarbons and cause emissions failures.",[["h","Control line shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24DF":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Stuck Open","Purge valve B is mechanically stuck open - AdBlue lines drain continuously, dosing pressure cannot build.",[["h","Valve stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24E0":["Reductant Purge Control Valve B Stuck Closed","Same as P24DF with valve B stuck closed - AdBlue cannot be cleared at shutdown, risk of crystallisation in injector and lines.",[["h","Valve stuck closed"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P24E1":["NH3 Sensor Circuit","A general circuit fault on the NH3 (ammonia) sensor - measures ammonia slip downstream of the SCR catalyst to detect AdBlue overdose.",[["h","Open in sensor or wiring"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24E2":["NH3 Sensor Circuit Range or Performance","Same as P24E1 with the signal in plausible range yet not matching the engine model.",[["h","Sensor element drifted"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24E3":["NH3 Sensor Circuit Low","Same as P24E1 with the signal voltage below the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24E4":["NH3 Sensor Circuit High","Same as P24E1 with the signal voltage above the plausible range. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal shorted to supply"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[400,1200]],"u"],"P24E5":["NH3 Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The ammonia (NH3) slip sensor downstream of the SCR catalyst delivers an intermittent or erratic signal. The ECM expects a smooth voltage proportional to ammonia concentration in the tailpipe — sudden jumps, dropouts or noise mean the wiring, connector or sensing element is failing.",[["h","Corroded or loose sensor connector"],["m","Chafed or vibrating harness near the exhaust"],["m","Aged ceramic sensor element drifting under heat cycles"]],[],["medium",[180,900]],"u"],"P24E6":["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit/Open","The heater inside the ammonia (NH3) slip sensor warms the sensing cell to operating temperature so it can read tailpipe ammonia. The ECM detects an open in the heater control circuit — no current flows when the heater should be active, so the sensor never reaches its working point and SCR closed-loop control is suspended.",[["h","Burnt-out heater winding inside the sensor"],["m","Broken wire or unplugged connector"],["l","Failed heater driver stage in the dosing module"]],[],["medium",[200,950]],"u"],"P24E7":["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit Low","The heater control circuit of the ammonia (NH3) slip sensor reads below the expected voltage range. Either the wiring is shorted to ground or the heater driver in the SCR/dosing module is stuck low.",[["h","Heater control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short across the heater element"],["l","Low-side driver pulled down in the control module"]],[],["medium",[180,900]],"u"],"P24E8":["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit High","The heater control circuit of the NH3 slip sensor reads above the expected voltage range. Typically a short to battery voltage or a heater driver stuck high — duty-cycle control is lost, the heater either runs continuously or not at all, and the sensor element risks overheating before the ECM disables it.",[["h","Heater control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["m","High-side driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[180,900]],"u"],"P24E9":["NH3 Sensor Heater Circuit Performance","The heater of the NH3 slip sensor is electrically intact, but the warm-up profile or steady-state temperature feedback does not match the ECM model. The sensor takes too long to reach operating temperature or drifts away from setpoint, so SCR closed-loop control is delayed or held off.",[["h","Aged heater with increased resistance"],["m","Poor thermal contact between heater and sensing cell"]],[],["medium",[200,950]],"u"],"P24EA":["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit","The supply rail that powers the NH3 slip sensor electronics (typically 5 V or 12 V from the dosing/SCR module) is out of tolerance. Without a stable supply the sensor cannot deliver a valid ammonia reading, and the ECM disables the closed-loop SCR strategy.",[["h","Open or shorted supply wire"],["m","Failing supply rail inside the dosing module"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P24EB":["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit Low","The NH3 slip sensor supply voltage drops below the lower limit. Usually a partial short to ground in the supply line, an undersized ground path with high resistance, or an internal supply collapse in the SCR/dosing module.",[["h","Supply line shorted to ground"],["m","High-resistance ground at the SCR module"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P24EC":["NH3 Sensor Supply Voltage Circuit High","The NH3 slip sensor supply voltage rises above the upper limit. Either the supply is shorted to battery voltage or an internal regulator in the dosing module has failed open.",[["h","Supply line shorted to battery voltage"],["m","Failed voltage regulator in the dosing module"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P24ED":["NH3 Sensor Calibration Memory","The NH3 slip sensor stores its individual calibration coefficients in non-volatile memory (EEPROM/flash). The ECM cannot read valid calibration values — either checksum fails, the memory is empty after replacement, or communication with the sensor electronics is broken.",[["h","New sensor installed but not coded/learned to the ECM"],["m","Corrupted calibration memory after voltage drop"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P24EE":["NH3 Sensor Processor Performance","The microcontroller inside the smart NH3 slip sensor reports an internal performance fault — failed self-test, watchdog reset, or out-of-range plausibility checks. The sensor cannot guarantee its output value, the ECM marks the channel invalid and disables SCR closed-loop control on this branch.",[["h","Internal processor or firmware fault"],["m","Brown-out from supply voltage dips"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],[],["medium",[200,900]],"u"],"P24EF":["Control Module Wake-up Circuit/Open","The wake-up line that brings a sleeping ECU back from low-power mode is open. Many networks use a dedicated hardware wake-up wire (door-latch trigger, terminal 15, CAN wake-up) so modules can stay asleep with the ignition off.",[["h","Broken wake-up wire or unplugged connector"],["m","Failed wake-up input stage in the module"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P24F0":["Control Module Wake-up Circuit Low","The wake-up input on the control module reads stuck low — usually a short to ground or a permanently asserted wake signal. The module either keeps waking up unnecessarily and drains the battery, or it cannot distinguish a real wake event from the stuck low level.",[["h","Wake-up wire shorted to ground"],["m","Door, hood or terminal switch stuck closed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P24F1":["Control Module Wake-up Circuit High","The wake-up input reads above the expected range — typically a short to battery voltage. The module sees a permanent wake-up request, never enters sleep mode and drains the battery while parked.",[["h","Wake-up wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"u"],"P24F2":["EGR Temperature/Charge Air Cooler Temperature Correlation","After a long key-off soak both the EGR temperature sensor and the charge-air cooler outlet temperature sensor must read approximately the same ambient temperature. The ECM compares them and detects an implausible delta.",[["h","One sensor drifting outside tolerance"],["m","Residual heat in the charge-air cooler after a hot soak"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P24F3":["Reductant Tank Temperature/Fuel Temperature Correlation","After a long key-off soak the AdBlue/DEF tank temperature and the fuel tank temperature should read close to each other (both at ambient). The ECM detects an implausible spread, which usually means one of the two sensors drifts, is wired wrong, or has a heat source nearby that the plausibility model does not account for.",[["h","One temperature sensor drifting outside tolerance"],["m","Recently active reductant tank heater warming the tank above ambient"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P24F4":["NOx Sensor Delayed Response - High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 1","The pre-catalyst NOx sensor on bank 1 (sensor 1) reacts too slowly when NOx in the exhaust drops from a high to a low level — for example after a fuel cut or transition into low-load. Aged ceramic cells, soot deposits or condensation inside the sensor protective tube slow the diffusion of NOx to the measuring element.",[["h","Aged sensor element with reduced response speed"],["m","Soot clogging the protective tube"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[300,1200]],"u"],"P24F5":["NOx Sensor Delayed Response - High to Low Bank 1 Sensor 2","The post-catalyst NOx sensor on bank 1 (sensor 2) reacts too slowly when NOx in the exhaust drops from a high to a low level. Same failure mechanism as the upstream sensor — aged element, soot or condensate — but post-catalyst the consequence is a degraded SCR conversion-efficiency monitor.",[["h","Aged sensor element with reduced response speed"],["m","Soot clogging the protective tube"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[300,1200]],"u"],"P24F6":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Stuck Open","On systems that inject HC dosing fuel or AIR-assisted reductant into the aftertreatment, a purge valve clears the line after each dosing event. The ECM detects the valve stuck open — pressure or flow does not build up against a closed valve, so the dosing line cannot be charged.",[["h","Mechanically stuck open valve from soot or coking"],["m","Broken return spring"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[200,900]],"u"],"P24F7":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Stuck Closed","The aftertreatment HC dosing or reductant purge valve is stuck closed. The ECM commands purge but the line is not cleared, leaving residual fluid that can foul nozzles or freeze in cold weather.",[["h","Stuck closed by deposits or seized armature"],["m","Open coil — valve never opens"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[200,900]],"u"],"P24F8":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit","General electrical fault in the control circuit of the aftertreatment fuel/air purge valve. The ECM cannot drive the valve coil according to plausibility checks — open, short or unexpected feedback voltage.",[["h","Open or shorted control wire"],["m","Failed driver stage in the dosing module"]],[],["medium",[150,700]],"u"],"P24F9":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","The valve coil is electrically intact, but the response (current rise time, return-current decay, position feedback) does not match the ECM model. Typical for solenoids losing magnetic strength after long thermal cycling, or armatures with increased friction from coking.",[["h","Aged solenoid with weakened magnetic force"],["m","Coked armature with increased friction"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P24FA":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit Low","The control circuit of the aftertreatment purge valve reads stuck low — usually a short to ground or a failed low-side driver. The valve is energised continuously when it should be off, or the diagnostic feedback voltage is pulled below threshold.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Failed low-side driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,700]],"u"],"P24FB":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Air Purge Valve Control Circuit High","The control circuit of the aftertreatment purge valve reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage or an open ground/return path. The driver cannot pull the line low to actuate the valve.",[["h","Control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["m","Open ground or open coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,700]],"u"],"P24FC":["Particulate Matter Sensor Heater Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","The PM (soot) sensor heater is driven by a current-limited stage so it can burn off accumulated soot before each measurement. The driver reports current or junction temperature above the safe limit and disables itself.",[["h","Partial short across the heater element"],["m","Driver overheating due to poor cooling on the module"]],[],["medium",[250,1100]],"u"],"P24FD":["Particulate Filter A Incorrect","The ECM identifies the installed particulate filter A as the wrong part — backpressure signature, regeneration efficiency or coded part-number do not match the application. Common after a non-OEM aftermarket DPF or a wrong-application replacement.",[["h","Incorrect or non-OEM DPF installed"],["m","Coding mismatch after part replacement"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,3000]],"u"],"P24FE":["SCR Catalyst Incorrect","The ECM identifies the installed SCR catalyst as the wrong part — NOx conversion efficiency, NH3 storage capacity or coded part-number do not match the expected application. Typical after fitting a non-OEM SCR brick or after a coding error following replacement.",[["h","Incorrect or non-OEM SCR catalyst installed"],["m","Coding mismatch after part replacement"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[500,3500]],"u"],"P24FF":["Reductant Temperature Too High","The temperature of the AdBlue/DEF in the dosing system exceeds the safe limit — risk of thermal decomposition (NH3/biuret formation) and clogged dosing nozzles. Often caused by a stuck-on tank heater, a stalled coolant return or proximity to a hot exhaust component.",[["h","Tank heater stuck on"],["m","Heat soak from exhaust or engine bay"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P2500":["Generator Lamp/L-Terminal Circuit Low","The L-terminal feedback line from the alternator (charging warning lamp circuit) reads below the lower limit. The lamp may stay on, and battery voltage may drift if regulation feedback is also affected.",[["h","L-terminal shorted to ground"],["m","Alternator regulator failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2501":["Generator Lamp/L-Terminal Circuit High","The L-terminal feedback from the alternator reads above the upper limit — short to supply or open ground side. Charging diagnostics cannot run cleanly.",[["h","L-terminal shorted to supply"],["m","Alternator regulator failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2502":["Charging System Voltage","The ECU detects an out-of-range charging system voltage without specifying high or low. Indicates a generic charging fault that requires further sub-code investigation.",[["h","Alternator output fault"],["m","Voltage regulator fault"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P2503":["Charging System Voltage Low","The ECU detects that battery voltage during operation stays below the regulated target. The alternator output is insufficient to maintain charge under load, eventually leading to battery depletion.",[["h","Weak alternator output"],["m","Faulty voltage regulator"],["l","Slipping drive belt"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P2504":["Charging System Voltage High","The ECU detects a battery voltage above the regulated upper limit. The voltage regulator is not limiting alternator output, risking damage to electronic modules and battery overcharge.",[["h","Faulty voltage regulator"],["m","Poor alternator ground"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P2505":["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal","The ECM/PCM monitors the main switched battery feed (typically terminal 15 / ignition-switched supply via the main relay). A general fault is reported — either the input is missing entirely or it does not match the expected timing relative to ignition state.",[["h","Failed main relay"],["m","Blown fuse on the ECM power feed"],["m","Corroded connector pin at the ECM"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P2506":["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Range/Performance","The switched-battery input to the ECM/PCM is present, but the level or transient behaviour is out of plausibility — sagging during cranking, slow ramp-up after main-relay close, or noisy. Often caused by aged main relay contacts or a weak battery feed under load.",[["h","Aged main relay contacts with rising contact resistance"],["m","Weak battery sagging during crank"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2507":["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Low","The ECM/PCM switched-battery input reads below threshold while the ignition is on. Either the main relay does not close, the supply wire is broken or shorted to ground, or the battery is too low.",[["h","Main relay does not pull in"],["m","Open supply wire"],["m","Severely discharged battery"]],[],["medium",[60,500]],"c"],"P2508":["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal High","The ECM/PCM switched-battery input reads above the upper threshold. Most often caused by a charging system overvoltage (failed alternator regulator) or wrong jump-start procedure.",[["h","Alternator regulator overvoltage"],["m","Improper external power source or jump-start"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2509":["ECM/PCM Power Input Signal Intermittent","The ECU detects sporadic interruptions of its supply voltage. The fault is set when supply drops below a threshold for short periods, often during cranking or due to a poor connection.",[["h","Poor battery cable connection"],["m","Intermittent main relay"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[50,400]],"c"],"P250A":["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault on the engine oil level sensor circuit. The ECM cannot read a plausible level signal (analog level, ultrasonic or capacitive sender).",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Corroded connector at the oil pan"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P250B":["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The oil level sensor is electrically intact, but the level reading is implausible — for example a constant value across drives, jumps that cannot match real oil consumption, or readings outside the design range. Often a contaminated or aged float/ultrasonic sender.",[["h","Aged or contaminated sender"],["m","Foaming oil under high RPM masking the level"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P250C":["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Low","The oil level sensor signal voltage reads below the lower limit, typically a short to ground or an open at the reference end of the sender. The ECM treats the input as invalid and ignores oil-low warnings until the circuit is repaired.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Sender shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P250D":["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit High","The oil level sensor signal voltage reads above the upper limit, typically a short to reference voltage or an open signal return. Pegged at maximum, the ECM cannot distinguish full from invalid and disables the level monitor.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P250E":["Engine Oil Level Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The oil level signal jumps or drops out intermittently — usually loose contacts, vibration cracks at the sender or oil sloshing on bumpy roads. The ECM filters short transients but flags the input when the noise pattern exceeds the diagnostic limits.",[["h","Loose or oil-soaked connector"],["m","Cracked sender housing"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P250F":["Engine Oil Level Too Low","The oil level monitor reports the engine oil level below the safe minimum after sensor checks pass. Continued operation risks bearing damage and oil-pump cavitation, so the ECM sets a critical warning, may reduce torque and asks the driver to add oil immediately.",[["h","High oil consumption between services"],["m","External oil leak"],["m","Missed top-up since last service"]],[],["easy",[10,80]],"c"],"P2510":["ECM/PCM Power Relay Sense Circuit Range/Performance","The voltage reported on the main power relay sense line for the engine controller does not match expectation. The ECU may shut down too early or stay awake too long, draining the battery.",[["h","Main relay contacts pitted"],["m","Sense wiring corroded"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[40,400]],"c"],"P2511":["ECM/PCM Power Relay Sense Circuit Intermittent","The sense (feedback) line that lets the ECM verify the main power relay has actually closed shows intermittent dropouts. The ECM expects to see battery voltage on this line whenever the relay is energised — short losses suggest aged contacts, vibration or chafed wiring.",[["h","Aged main relay contacts"],["m","Chafed sense wire shorting intermittently"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2512":["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit/Open","The Event Data Recorder (EDR / black box) request line — used by the ECM or restraint module to trigger the EDR to capture pre-crash data — is open. The ECM cannot trigger an event capture, so any subsequent crash event would not be recorded reliably.",[["h","Open request wire or unplugged module"],["m","Failed input stage in the EDR"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2513":["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit Low","The EDR request line reads stuck low — typically a short to ground or a permanently asserted request. The ECM either sees a constant request (which it cannot service) or cannot pulse the line high to fire a real event capture.",[["h","Request wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2514":["Event Data Recorder Request Circuit High","The EDR request line reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot pulse the line back low to release the request, so the EDR may either ignore further requests or sit in a permanent triggered state.",[["h","Request wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2515":["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit","General electrical fault in the second A/C refrigerant pressure sensor circuit. Sensor B usually monitors the low-side or compressor-suction pressure (in addition to high-side sensor A).",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Failed sensor element"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2516":["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","A/C refrigerant pressure sensor B is electrically intact, but its reading does not match the system model — for example pressures that do not fall when the compressor is off, do not change with ambient temperature, or contradict pressure sensor A. Often a refrigerant charge issue or a contaminated sensor.",[["h","Low refrigerant charge"],["m","Contaminated or aged sensor diaphragm"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2517":["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","A/C refrigerant pressure sensor B signal voltage reads below the lower limit. Either a short to ground in the signal wire, an open reference voltage at the sensor, or an internal short.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Missing 5 V reference at the sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2518":["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","A/C refrigerant pressure sensor B signal voltage reads above the upper limit. Typically a short to reference voltage in the signal line, an open signal return, or an overpressure event briefly pegging the sensor.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return at the sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2519":["A/C Request A Circuit","General electrical fault on the A/C compressor request input A. This input tells the ECM that the HVAC controller wants the A/C compressor engaged.",[["h","Open or shorted A/C request wire"],["m","HVAC module not transmitting the request"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P251A":["PTO Enable Switch Circuit/Open","The Power Take-Off (PTO) enable switch input to the ECM is open. PTO is used on trucks and work vehicles to drive auxiliary equipment from the engine — without a valid enable signal the ECM refuses to enter PTO operating mode, idle speed control changes do not apply.",[["h","Open switch wire or unplugged switch"],["m","Failed PTO enable switch"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P251B":["PTO Enable Switch Circuit Low","The PTO enable switch input reads stuck low — typically a short to ground or a permanently closed switch. The ECM either sees PTO enabled when the operator has not requested it, or cannot release the PTO mode after work.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["m","Switch stuck closed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P251C":["PTO Enable Switch Circuit High","The PTO enable switch input reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot pull the input low, so the switch state is unreadable and PTO mode is locked out for safety.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P251D":["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit/Open","The PTO engine-shutdown command line is open. This safety input lets a connected work attachment (or operator switch) request an immediate engine shutdown — for example when an interlock is opened on a stationary aerial work platform.",[["h","Broken shutdown wire or unplugged work attachment"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P251E":["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit Low","The PTO engine-shutdown command line reads stuck low — usually a short to ground or a permanently asserted shutdown request. The ECM may treat this as an active shutdown command and refuse to start or keep the engine running while in PTO mode.",[["h","Shutdown wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P251F":["PTO Engine Shutdown Circuit High","The PTO engine-shutdown command line reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot pulse the line low to acknowledge a shutdown request, so the operator-side safety chain is effectively disabled.",[["h","Shutdown wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P2520":["A/C Request A Circuit Low","The A/C compressor request input A reads stuck low — typically a short to ground or a permanently asserted request. The ECM either sees A/C demanded all the time (cannot release idle-up, raises fuel use) or cannot distinguish a real request from the stuck low level.",[["h","Request wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2521":["A/C Request A Circuit High","The A/C request input A reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot pull the line low to read switch state, so the A/C compressor request is treated as invalid and the clutch stays disengaged.",[["h","Request wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2522":["A/C Request B Circuit","General electrical fault on the second A/C request input B. Many vehicles have two HVAC zones, a rear evaporator request, or a redundant request line — input B carries that signal.",[["h","Open or shorted A/C request wire B"],["m","HVAC module not transmitting request B"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2523":["A/C Request B Circuit Low","The A/C request input B reads stuck low — short to ground or permanently asserted request. Same effect as input A stuck low, applied to the second HVAC channel.",[["h","Request wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2524":["A/C Request B Circuit High","The A/C request input B reads stuck high — typically a short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot read the switch state, request B is treated as invalid.",[["h","Request wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2525":["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault on the vacuum reservoir pressure sensor circuit. The reservoir stores manifold or pump-generated vacuum for systems like brake booster, EGR actuators or HVAC dampers.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Failed sensor element"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2526":["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The vacuum reservoir pressure sensor is electrically intact, but the reading does not match the model — vacuum that does not build up after pump activation, does not bleed off when consumers draw, or stays at one value. Often a partly clogged hose, a leaking reservoir or an aged sensor.",[["h","Leaking reservoir or vacuum line"],["m","Aged sensor with offset drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2527":["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Sensor signal voltage below the lower limit — usually a short to ground or open reference. The ECM disables vacuum pump control until the input recovers.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Missing 5 V reference at the sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2528":["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Sensor signal voltage above the upper limit — usually a short to reference voltage or open signal return. ECM disables vacuum pump control to avoid overshooting.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2529":["Vacuum Reservoir Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent","The sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently — loose connector, vibration, or chafed harness. The ECM filters short transients but flags the input when noise exceeds limits.",[["h","Loose connector"],["m","Chafed harness"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P252A":["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault on the engine oil quality sensor — typically a capacitive/dielectric sensor that estimates oil aging from permittivity, viscosity proxies and conductivity. With no valid reading the dynamic service-interval algorithm falls back to the fixed-interval default.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Failed sensor electrode after long use"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P252B":["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The oil quality sensor is electrically intact, but the readings do not match the model — for example permittivity that does not change after an oil change, or shifts inconsistent with km/h driven. Often a contaminated electrode or oil that does not fit the sensor calibration.",[["h","Contaminated sensor electrode"],["m","Oil grade outside the sensor calibration range"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P252C":["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Low","Sensor signal voltage below the lower limit — typically a short to ground in the signal line or an internal short across the sensor electrode.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P252D":["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit High","Sensor signal voltage above the upper limit — typically a short to reference voltage or an open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P252E":["Engine Oil Quality Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The oil quality sensor signal jumps or drops out — usually a loose connector at the oil pan, an oil-soaked harness or vibration cracks at the sensor housing.",[["h","Loose oil-soaked connector"],["m","Cracked sensor housing"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P252F":["Engine Oil Level Too High","The oil level monitor reports the engine oil level above the safe maximum after sensor checks pass. Overfilling raises foaming, blow-by and crankcase pressure — and on diesels with regen-by-injection, fuel dilution can drive the level up by itself.",[["h","Overfilled at last service"],["m","Fuel dilution from incomplete DPF regeneration"],["l","Coolant intrusion (head gasket / cooler)"]],[],["easy",[10,200]],"c"],"P2530":["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit","The ECU detects an electrical fault on the ignition switch run position input. The signal indicating that the ignition is in the run position is missing or implausible.",[["h","Faulty ignition switch contacts"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P2531":["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit Low","The ignition switch Run-position input reads stuck low — short to ground or a permanently closed contact. The ECM cannot tell when the operator releases the switch from Run, so accessory and crank logic gets confused.",[["h","Run input wire shorted to ground"],["m","Switch contact stuck closed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2532":["Ignition Switch Run Position Circuit High","The ignition switch Run-position input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or open switch return. The ECM cannot detect when the operator turns the switch back to off/accessory, so module sleep and accessory power timeouts do not work correctly.",[["h","Run input wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2533":["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit","General electrical fault on the ignition switch On/Start (terminal 50 / crank) input. The ECM uses this signal to know when the starter is energised — without it the ECM cannot raise fuel and timing for cranking, the engine struggles to start or stalls right after.",[["h","Open or shorted On/Start wire"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2534":["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit Low","The On/Start input reads stuck low — short to ground or permanently closed contact. The ECM may see crank request when the key is at rest, blocking accessory functions or causing unexpected starter cut-off logic.",[["h","On/Start wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2535":["Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit High","The On/Start input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot read the crank state, modules dependent on this signal are unable to time their wake-up correctly.",[["h","On/Start wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2536":["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit","General electrical fault on the ignition switch accessory (terminal 75 / ACC) input. ACC tells the ECM that radio, fans, accessory loads should be powered without the engine running.",[["h","Open or shorted ACC wire"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2537":["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit Low","The ACC input reads stuck low — short to ground or permanently closed contact. The ECM may see ACC active continuously and refuse to enter sleep, draining the battery.",[["h","ACC wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2538":["Ignition Switch Accessory Position Circuit High","The ACC input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. The ECM cannot detect when the operator releases the switch from ACC, accessory power timeouts do not work.",[["h","ACC wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2539":["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault on the low-pressure fuel system sensor — typically the lift-pump or pre-supply pressure sensor that monitors the rail feeding the high-pressure pump. With no valid reading, the ECM cannot verify that lift pressure is sufficient for HP-pump intake.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Failed sensor element"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P253A":["PTO Sense Circuit/Open","The PTO sense (engagement feedback) line is open. This input tells the ECM whether the PTO clutch or driveline is actually engaged after a request — it closes the loop on the PTO enable command.",[["h","Open sense wire"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P253B":["PTO Sense Circuit Range/Performance","The PTO sense circuit is electrically intact, but the engagement feedback does not match the command. The ECM requests engage and sees no engaged feedback (or vice versa) within the expected time window — drive-line slip, sticky clutch, or a mis-adjusted limit switch.",[["h","Sticky or worn PTO clutch"],["m","Mis-adjusted limit switch"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"c"],"P253C":["PTO Sense Circuit Low","The PTO sense input reads stuck low — short to ground or limit switch stuck closed. The ECM may see PTO continuously engaged.",[["h","Sense wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P253D":["PTO Sense Circuit High","The PTO sense input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or open switch return. The ECM cannot detect engagement.",[["h","Sense wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P253E":["PTO Sense Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The PTO sense signal jumps or drops out — usually loose connectors, a chattering limit switch, or vibration on the work attachment.",[["h","Loose connector"],["m","Chattering limit switch"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P253F":["Engine Oil Deteriorated","The oil quality monitor concludes that the engine oil has reached the end of its useful life — based on permittivity, soot content, fuel dilution and total operating hours. The ECM requests an oil change before the next regen cycle to prevent accelerated bearing wear.",[["h","Service interval exceeded"],["m","High DPF regeneration load with fuel dilution"]],[],["easy",[60,200]],"c"],"P2540":["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit","The ECU detects a general fault in the low-pressure fuel system pressure sensor circuit. Without a valid signal the ECU cannot verify lift-pump pressure or fuel rail pre-pressure.",[["h","Defective low-pressure sensor"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2541":["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The signal of the low-pressure fuel sensor does not match the expected value during operation. Pressure does not rise as expected when the lift pump is commanded.",[["h","Sensor drift"],["m","Clogged fuel filter"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[60,400]],"c"],"P2542":["Low Pressure Fuel System Sensor Circuit High","The low-pressure fuel system sensor signal voltage is above the upper limit. Either a short to reference voltage in the signal line, an open signal return, or a sensor reading pegged high after an internal failure.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2544":["Torque Management Request Input Signal A","The ECU detects an invalid torque-management request signal A from another control unit (e.g. transmission, ESP, ABS) on the CAN bus.",[["h","CAN communication error"],["m","Fault in requesting module"]],[],["hard",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2545":["Torque Management Request Input Signal A Range/Performance","The ECM receives torque-management requests from other modules (TCM during shifts, ABS/ESC during traction events, hybrid controller). Input A is electrically intact but its values do not match the system model — out-of-range steps, jumps, or persistent values that other modules cannot confirm.",[["h","Requesting module sending invalid values"],["m","Communication bus corruption between modules"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2546":["Torque Management Request Input Signal A Low","Torque management input A reads stuck low — analog short to ground or message stuck at minimum value. The ECM cannot trust the request and falls back to a safe default.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","CAN message stuck at minimum value"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2547":["Torque Management Request Input Signal A High","Torque management input A reads stuck high — analog short to reference voltage or message stuck at maximum value. The ECM rejects the request to avoid running unintended high-torque commands.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","CAN message stuck at maximum value"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2548":["Torque Management Request Input Signal B","General electrical fault on the second torque-management request input B. Used when more than one module needs to request torque adjustments — typically TCM on input A and ABS/ESC on input B, or chassis vs powertrain.",[["h","Open or shorted wire / invalid CAN message"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2549":["Torque Management Request Input Signal B Range/Performance","Input B is electrically intact but the values are implausible — same failure mode as the A-side performance fault, applied to the second torque-management channel.",[["h","Requesting module sending invalid values"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P254A":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit/Open","The PTO speed-selector switch 1 input is open. This switch lets the operator pick a preset PTO operating speed (idle, 800, 1200 rpm, etc.).",[["h","Open wire or unplugged switch"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P254B":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Range/Performance","The selector input is electrically intact but the value is implausible — multiple positions asserted at once, or a value that cannot map to any of the configured speed presets. Often a sticky multi-position switch or a contaminated rotary contact.",[["h","Contaminated rotary contact"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P254C":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit Low","PTO speed selector 1 input reads stuck low — short to ground or analog signal pegged at minimum. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P254D":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit High","PTO speed selector 1 input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or analog signal pegged at maximum.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P254E":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 1 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The PTO speed selector signal jumps or drops out — usually a worn rotary contact or vibration on the work attachment.",[["h","Worn rotary contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P254F":["Engine Hood Switch Circuit","General electrical fault on the engine hood (bonnet) switch circuit. The hood switch tells the body controller and (on hybrids) the high-voltage system that the hood is open — used for security, alarm and HV-safety interlock.",[["h","Open or shorted hood-switch wire"],["m","Aged switch with corroded contacts"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2550":["Torque Management Request Input Signal B Low","Torque management input B reads stuck low — short to ground or message at minimum. ECM rejects the request, only A-side is used.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2551":["Torque Management Request Input Signal B High","Torque management input B reads stuck high — short to reference voltage or message at maximum. ECM rejects the request to avoid unintended high-torque commands.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2552":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit","General electrical fault on the throttle/fuel inhibit input A. This input lets external safety functions (immobilizer, hybrid HV interlock, anti-theft) override the throttle or cut fuel delivery.",[["h","Open or shorted inhibit wire"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2553":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit Range/Performance","The throttle/fuel inhibit A signal is electrically intact but its value does not match the system context — for example asserted while the immobilizer reports OK, or de-asserted while a hybrid HV interlock is active. The ECM cannot trust the signal.",[["h","Requesting module sending an inconsistent value"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2554":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit Low","Throttle/fuel inhibit A reads stuck low — short to ground or permanently asserted. ECM may treat it as continuous inhibit and refuse normal operation.",[["h","Inhibit wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2555":["Throttle/Fuel Inhibit A Circuit High","Throttle/fuel inhibit A reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. ECM cannot read the inhibit state and falls back to the safe default.",[["h","Inhibit wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2556":["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit","General electrical fault on the engine coolant level sensor/switch circuit. Many vehicles use a simple float-switch in the expansion tank, others use a continuous-level analog sensor.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the sensor"],["m","Corroded connector at the expansion tank"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2557":["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit Range/Performance","The coolant level sensor is electrically intact, but the readings are implausible — for example a level that does not move at all over many drive cycles, or jumps that cannot match real coolant loss. Often a stuck float, contaminated electrode or air-locked sensor.",[["h","Stuck float"],["m","Trapped air around the sensor"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2558":["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","Coolant level sensor signal voltage below the lower limit — short to ground or internal short. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2559":["Engine Coolant Level Sensor/Switch Circuit High","Coolant level sensor signal voltage above the upper limit — short to reference voltage or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P255A":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit/Open","The second PTO speed-selector switch input is open. Switch 2 typically encodes a binary or multi-bit code together with switch 1 — together they select one of several preset PTO speeds.",[["h","Open wire or unplugged switch"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P255B":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Range/Performance","PTO speed selector switch 2 is electrically intact but its value does not match a valid bit pattern — multiple positions asserted, or values that do not map to any preset.",[["h","Contaminated rotary contact"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P255C":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit Low","PTO speed selector 2 input reads stuck low — short to ground or analog signal pegged at minimum. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P255D":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit High","PTO speed selector 2 input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or analog signal pegged at maximum.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P255E":["PTO Speed Selector Sensor/Switch 2 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","PTO speed selector 2 signal jumps or drops out — usually a worn rotary contact or vibration on the work attachment.",[["h","Worn rotary contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P255F":["A/C Request A Circuit Range/Performance","The A/C request input A is electrically intact, but its value does not match the system context — for example asserted while the HVAC controller reports off, toggling rapidly, or sustained while compressor pressures cannot support it. The ECM disables A/C clutch engagement until the input becomes plausible.",[["h","HVAC module sending inconsistent request"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2560":["Engine Coolant Level Low","The coolant level monitor reports the engine coolant below the safe minimum after sensor checks pass. Continued operation risks overheating, head warping and head-gasket failure.",[["h","External coolant leak (hose, radiator, water pump)"],["m","Missed top-up since last service"],["l","Head gasket leaking coolant into combustion"]],[],["medium",[20,1500]],"c"],"P2561":["A/C Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","The A/C / HVAC control module has requested the ECM to illuminate the malfunction indicator (MIL) because of an emissions-relevant fault on its side. The original fault is stored in the HVAC module — this code only signals that the ECM has honoured the request.",[["h","Internal fault in the HVAC module — read its DTCs"]],[],["medium",[50,800]],"c"],"P2562":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit","General electrical fault on the turbocharger boost control position sensor A — the feedback sensor on the wastegate or VGT actuator (often a contactless Hall sensor). Without valid position feedback the ECM cannot close the loop on boost control and falls back to open-loop duty cycle.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the position sensor"],["m","Failed Hall element after thermal cycling"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2563":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor Circuit","The position feedback sensor on the variable-geometry or wastegate turbocharger actuator is not communicating or is implausible. Without position feedback, boost control runs in default mode and power is reduced.",[["h","Position sensor failed"],["m","Wiring open or chafed near turbo"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2000]],"c"],"P2564":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit Low","Position sensor A signal voltage below the lower limit — short to ground in the signal line or open reference voltage at the sensor.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Missing 5 V reference at the sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2565":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Circuit High","Position sensor A signal voltage above the upper limit — short to reference voltage in the signal line or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2566":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor Range/Performance","The turbocharger actuator position sensor reports a value, but it does not track commanded vane or wastegate position within tolerance. Often a sticky VTG mechanism due to soot.",[["h","VTG vanes coked, sticky"],["m","Actuator linkage worn"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2569":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","Direct Ozone Reduction (DOR) catalysts are coated radiator surfaces or dedicated catalysts that decompose tropospheric ozone passing over the radiator — used for low-emissions vehicles. The temperature sensor monitoring the DOR brick reads stuck low — short to ground or sensor short.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor shorted internally"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P256A":["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit/Open","The idle-speed selector input is open. On commercial vehicles this switch lets the operator pick a fast-idle setpoint (for example to keep auxiliary loads supplied).",[["h","Open wire or unplugged switch"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],["Check engine light on","Idle speed too high, too low, or unstable","Possible stalling at idle or after cold start"],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P256B":["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Range/Performance","The idle-speed selector input is electrically intact but the value does not match a valid preset — multiple positions or a non-mappable value. Often a sticky multi-position switch.",[["h","Contaminated rotary contact"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Idle speed too high, too low, or unstable","Possible stalling at idle or after cold start"],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P256C":["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit Low","Idle-speed selector input reads stuck low — short to ground or analog signal at minimum. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Idle speed too high, too low, or unstable","Possible stalling at idle or after cold start"],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P256D":["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit High","Idle-speed selector input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or analog signal at maximum. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Idle speed too high, too low, or unstable","Possible stalling at idle or after cold start"],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P256E":["Engine Idle Speed Selector Sensor/Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The idle-speed selector signal jumps or drops out — usually a worn rotary contact or vibration. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Worn rotary contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Idle speed too high, too low, or unstable","Possible stalling at idle or after cold start"],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P256F":["A/C Request B Circuit Range/Performance","A/C request input B is electrically intact but its value does not match the system context — same failure mode as the input A performance fault, applied to the second HVAC channel.",[["h","HVAC module sending inconsistent request B"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2570":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit High","The DOR catalyst temperature sensor reads stuck high — short to reference voltage or open signal return. Without a valid temperature the ECM cannot enable the DOR efficiency monitor.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["m","Open signal return"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2571":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The DOR catalyst temperature sensor signal jumps or drops out — typically loose connectors or chafed wiring near the radiator pack.",[["h","Loose connector"],["m","Chafed harness"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,300]],"c"],"P2572":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit","General electrical fault on the DOR catalyst deterioration sensor circuit. This sensor estimates the remaining ozone-conversion capacity of the DOR coating — coating worn off the radiator surface, contaminated by salt or grime, or thermally aged.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2573":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The DOR deterioration sensor is electrically intact but its readings drift or do not match the model — for example a deterioration value that does not move with km/h driven, or moves implausibly fast.",[["h","Aged sensor with offset drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2574":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Low","The DOR deterioration sensor signal voltage reads below the lower limit — short to ground or internal short.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2575":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit High","The DOR deterioration sensor signal voltage reads above the upper limit — short to reference voltage or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2576":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Deterioration Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The DOR deterioration sensor signal jumps or drops out — typically loose connectors or chafed wiring near the radiator.",[["h","Loose connector"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[60,300]],"c"],"P2577":["Direct Ozone Reduction Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold","The DOR catalyst no longer reduces tropospheric ozone with the required efficiency, based on the deterioration sensor and operating-time model. Coating worn off the radiator surface, contaminated by road salt and grime, or thermally aged after many heat cycles.",[["h","DOR coating worn off the radiator"],["m","Coating contaminated by salt and grime"]],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Possibly slightly increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[400,1800]],"c"],"P2578":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit","General electrical fault on the turbocharger/supercharger shaft speed sensor A — a high-frequency Hall or eddy-current sensor on the compressor shaft. The ECM uses turbo speed for overspeed protection (typically 200,000+ rpm) and for closed-loop boost on VGT systems.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring"],["m","Aged sensor with reduced output amplitude"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2579":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","Turbo speed sensor A is electrically intact, but the speed reading does not match the model — for example a speed that does not climb when boost rises, drifts away from the air-mass-flow estimate, or jumps. Often blade-fouling, a contaminated sensor tip or aged element.",[["h","Oil-contaminated sensor tip"],["m","Aged Hall element"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P257A":["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit/Open","The control circuit that drives the vacuum reservoir control valve (or vacuum pump motor) is open. The ECM cannot energise the actuator, so vacuum is no longer maintained on demand and consumers like brake booster, EGR or HVAC dampers may run out of vacuum.",[["h","Open control wire"],["m","Failed driver in the control module"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P257B":["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit Low","The vacuum reservoir control circuit reads stuck low — short to ground or low-side driver stuck on. The actuator may be energised continuously when it should be off.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P257C":["Vacuum Reservoir Control Circuit High","The vacuum reservoir control circuit reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or open coil. The driver cannot pull the line low to actuate the valve/motor.",[["h","Control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["m","Open coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P257D":["Engine Hood Switch Circuit Range/Performance","The hood switch is electrically intact, but its state is implausible — for example reporting hood-open while vehicle speed is rising, or rapid toggles. Usually a worn switch with high contact bounce or a misaligned hood actuator.",[["h","Worn switch with contact bounce"],["m","Misaligned hood actuator"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P257E":["Engine Hood Switch Circuit Low","The hood switch input reads stuck low — short to ground or stuck-closed switch. The body controller may treat the hood as permanently open and refuse to arm the alarm or close the HV interlock.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P257F":["Engine Hood Switch Circuit High","The hood switch input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or open switch return. The body controller cannot detect when the hood is opened.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"c"],"P2580":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Low","Turbo speed sensor A signal voltage below the lower limit — short to ground in the signal line or open supply.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Open supply at the sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2581":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit High","Turbo speed sensor A signal voltage above the upper limit — short to reference voltage or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2582":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Speed Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","Turbo speed sensor A signal jumps or drops out — vibration, oil mist on the sensor tip, or chafed wiring near the hot turbo.",[["h","Oil mist on the sensor tip"],["m","Chafed harness near the turbo"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2583":["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Single Sensor or Center","General fault on the radar/lidar/camera distance-range sensor used by adaptive cruise control. On systems with a single sensor or three sensors with a center unit, this code refers to the central sensor — without it, ACC distance control is disabled and the system falls back to plain cruise.",[["h","Dirty sensor surface (radar emblem / camera lens)"],["m","Sensor misaligned after a frontal impact"],["l","Failed sensor module"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2584":["Fuel Additive Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","The fuel additive control module — typical for diesel cars with a separate Eolys/Cerine additive tank that aids DPF regeneration — has requested the ECM to illuminate the MIL because of an emissions-relevant fault on its side. The original fault is in the additive module itself.",[["h","Internal fault in the fuel additive module — read its DTCs"]],[],["medium",[50,800]],"c"],"P2585":["Fuel Additive Control Module Warning Lamp Request","The fuel additive control module asks for the additive-low warning lamp to be illuminated — the additive tank (Eolys/Cerine, used to lower DPF regen temperature) is approaching empty or has reached a service threshold. Continued driving without refilling will eventually disable DPF regeneration.",[["h","Additive tank low — service refill required"]],[],["medium",[80,350]],"c"],"P2586":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit","General electrical fault on the turbocharger boost control position sensor B — second position sensor on the same actuator (redundant Hall) or on a second turbo (twin-turbo, sequential or two-stage). With B invalid the ECM cannot cross-check actuator A and falls back to limited boost control.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring to the position sensor"],["m","Failed Hall element"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2587":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Position sensor B is electrically intact, but the reading does not track sensor A or the actuator-command model. Often a misaligned redundant sensor or aged element on a second turbo.",[["h","Sensor mounting misaligned after service"],["m","Aged Hall element"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2588":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Low","Position sensor B signal voltage below the lower limit — short to ground or open reference. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2589":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit High","Position sensor B signal voltage above the upper limit — short to reference voltage or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P258A":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A/Open","The control circuit driving the electric vacuum pump (used to maintain brake-booster vacuum on direct-injection or hybrid powertrains where the engine is not always running) is open. The ECM cannot run the pump on demand — booster vacuum drops, pedal feel hardens, brake assist may be reduced.",[["h","Open control wire to the pump"],["m","Failed driver in the control module"]],[],["medium",[150,700]],"c"],"P258B":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A Range/Performance","The vacuum pump control circuit is electrically intact, but the pump response does not match the model — pump runs longer than expected to reach setpoint, current draw rises (mechanically tight) or vacuum does not build at all. Aged motor brushes, dry vanes or a leaking line are typical causes.",[["h","Aged motor brushes or dry vanes"],["m","Leaking vacuum line"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P258C":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A Low","The electric vacuum pump control circuit reads stuck low — short to ground or low-side driver stuck on. The pump may run continuously, drawing current and overheating, until the ECM disables the channel.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P258D":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit A High","The vacuum pump control circuit reads stuck high — short to battery voltage or open coil/return. The driver cannot pull the line low to start the pump.",[["h","Control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["m","Open pump motor winding"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P258E":["PTO Enable Switch Performance","The PTO enable switch is electrically intact but its state does not match operating conditions — for example asserted while the vehicle is rolling above the PTO speed limit, or asserted/de-asserted in fast succession. The ECM rejects the request to avoid unsafe PTO engagement.",[["h","Switch contact bounce"],["m","Switch operated while vehicle is moving"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"c"],"P258F":["Torque Management Request Output Signal","The ECM/PCM produces a torque-management output signal for downstream consumers (TCM during shifts, hybrid module, transfer case) and detects a fault on this output — open, short, or feedback voltage outside expected range. Without it, downstream modules cannot synchronise their behaviour with the engine.",[["h","Open or shorted output line"],["m","Downstream consumer not loading the line"]],[],["hard",[120,800]],"c"],"P2590":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Position sensor B signal jumps or drops out — vibration on the actuator, oil mist contamination or chafed wiring near the hot turbo.",[["h","Vibration-induced chafing of the harness"],["m","Oil mist on the sensor"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2591":["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Left","General fault on the left-side front distance-range sensor used by adaptive cruise. Multi-sensor radar arrays use left/center/right sensors for wider field-of-view and lane discrimination — without left, ACC may degrade to single-target tracking.",[["h","Dirty sensor surface"],["m","Sensor misaligned after a frontal impact"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2592":["Cruise Control Front Distance Range Sensor Right","General fault on the right-side front distance-range sensor used by adaptive cruise. Same role as the left sensor but covering the right field-of-view.",[["h","Dirty sensor surface"],["m","Sensor misaligned after a frontal impact"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"c"],"P2593":["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit","General electrical fault on the second turbocharger speed sensor B — used on twin-turbo, sequential or two-stage installations to read the second compressor shaft speed. Same role as sensor A on the second turbo.",[["h","Open or shorted wiring"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2594":["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Turbo speed sensor B is electrically intact, but the speed reading does not match the boost or air-mass model — same failure mode as sensor A performance fault, applied to the second turbo.",[["h","Oil-contaminated sensor tip"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2595":["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Low","Turbo speed sensor B signal voltage below the lower limit — short to ground or open supply. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2596":["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit High","Turbo speed sensor B signal voltage above the upper limit — short to reference voltage or open signal return.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to reference voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2597":["Turbocharger Speed Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","Turbo speed sensor B signal jumps or drops out — vibration, oil mist or chafed wiring at the second turbo.",[["h","Oil mist on the sensor tip"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P2598":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Performance - Stuck Low","Position sensor A reports a value stuck near the low end of its travel even when the actuator is commanded to move. Either the actuator is mechanically stuck closed (wastegate jammed shut, VGT vanes seized at minimum opening) or the sensor itself is pegged low.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck near low end"],["m","Sensor pegged low"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P2599":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor A Performance - Stuck High","Position sensor A reports a value stuck near the high end of its travel — actuator stuck open (wastegate held wide open, VGT vanes seized at maximum opening) or sensor pegged high. Boost suffers — typically underboost on VGT, overboost-protection-off on wastegate.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck near high end"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P259A":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Performance - Stuck Low","Same condition as the A-side stuck-low fault, but on the second sensor / second turbo. Position sensor B reads stuck near the low end while the actuator is commanded.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck near low end"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P259B":["Turbocharger Boost Control Position Sensor B Performance - Stuck High","Same as the A-side stuck-high fault, applied to sensor B / turbo B. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck near high end"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P259C":["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Turbocharger A Boost Control","After start-up the boost-control loop on turbo A takes longer than the calibration limit to transition from open-loop to closed-loop control. Typically a slow-warming actuator (VGT vanes carbonised), a sluggish position sensor or a leaky pneumatic actuator that cannot follow setpoints quickly enough.",[["h","Carbonised VGT vanes"],["m","Leaky pneumatic actuator"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[300,2200]],"u"],"P259D":["Excessive Time To Enter Closed Loop Turbocharger B Boost Control","Same condition as the turbo A excessive-warm-up fault, applied to the second turbo. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Carbonised VGT vanes"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[300,2200]],"u"],"P259E":["Turbocharger A Boost Control Position At Low Limit","The boost-control actuator on turbo A has been operating at the low end of its travel for too long — the closed-loop controller is saturated against the lower stop trying to reach the boost setpoint. Indicates either a leak (wastegate held closed but boost still escapes) or commanded boost above what the engine can produce.",[["h","Boost leak in the charge-air path"],["m","Failing turbocharger that cannot produce target boost"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P259F":["Turbocharger A Boost Control Position At High Limit","The boost-control actuator on turbo A has been operating at the high end of its travel — the controller is saturated against the upper stop trying to bleed off boost. Indicates either a wastegate stuck closed, oversized turbo for the calibration, or commanded boost limits being exceeded by ambient conditions (cold dense air).",[["h","Wastegate stuck closed"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P25A0":["Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At Low Limit","Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At Low Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects turbo/supercharger boost-pressure control.",[["h","Boost leak in the charge-air path"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P25A1":["Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At High Limit","Turbocharger B Boost Control Position At High Limit: the control module has detected this fault condition. This affects turbo/supercharger boost-pressure control.",[["h","Wastegate stuck closed"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P25A2":["Brake System Control Module A Requested MIL Illumination","The primary brake system control module (ABS/ESC/iBooster) has requested the ECM to illuminate the MIL because of an emissions-relevant fault on its side — for example a regenerative braking fault on a hybrid that affects driveline torque flow. The original fault is in the brake module.",[["h","Internal fault in the brake module — read its DTCs"]],[],["medium",[80,1500]],"u"],"P25A3":["Engine Hood Open","After plausibility checks the body controller has concluded that the engine hood is genuinely open while the vehicle is operating. Used to suspend HV operation on hybrids/EVs (HV interlock), block remote engine start, and trigger the alarm if armed.",[["h","Hood not properly latched"],["m","Failed hood latch sensor"]],[],["easy",[10,250]],"u"],"P25A4":["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit","General electrical fault on the fuel mode select switch — used on bi-fuel vehicles (CNG/LPG/H2/gasoline) so the driver can pick the active fuel. With the input invalid, the ECM falls back to the default fuel and disables operator-selectable switching.",[["h","Open or shorted switch wire"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25A5":["Fuel Mode Select Switch Performance","The fuel mode select switch is electrically intact, but its state does not match operating conditions — switched to gas while gas tank is empty, or fast toggling. The ECM rejects the request to avoid stalling.",[["h","Switch contact bounce"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25A6":["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit Low","Fuel mode switch input reads stuck low — short to ground or stuck-closed contact. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25A7":["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit High","Fuel mode switch input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25A8":["Fuel Mode Select Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Fuel mode switch signal jumps or drops out — worn contact or vibration. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Worn switch contact"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"],["l","Harness routed against vibrating component"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25A9":["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit/Open","The piston-cooling oil-jet control circuit is open. Modern engines with under-piston oil jets switch them on under high load to cool the piston crown — controlled by a solenoid valve in the oil gallery.",[["h","Open control wire to the solenoid"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25AA":["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Low","The piston-cooling oil-jet control circuit reads stuck low — short to ground or low-side driver stuck on. The jets may be enabled continuously, raising oil pump load and lowering oil pressure to other consumers.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25AB":["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit High","Control circuit stuck high — short to battery voltage or open coil/return. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25AC":["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","The control circuit is electrically intact, but the solenoid valve does not open when commanded — confirmed by oil-pressure or oil-temperature feedback that does not change after the activation pulse. Piston cooling does not engage under high load — risk of piston-crown overheating and ring-land cracks.",[["h","Solenoid stuck closed by oil sludge"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["hard",[300,1500]],"u"],"P25AD":["Piston Cooling Oil Control Circuit Stuck On","The piston cooling solenoid does not close when commanded off — jets remain active when not needed. Oil pressure to top-end consumers may sag, and warm-up takes longer because the cooling jets remove heat from the pistons during cold start.",[["h","Solenoid stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],[],["hard",[300,1500]],"u"],"P25AE":["Piston Cooling Oil Pressure Too Low","With the piston-cooling jets commanded on, the dedicated oil-pressure sensor in that gallery reads below the safe threshold. Insufficient flow to the jets means real piston cooling is not happening — the ECM warns the driver and may reduce torque to protect the pistons.",[["h","Low engine oil level"],["m","Sludge-clogged oil gallery"],["l","Worn oil pump"]],[],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P25AF":["Coolant Temperature Control Module Requested MIL Illumination","A dedicated coolant-temperature control module (used on engines with electric coolant pumps and electronic thermostats to keep the cylinder head and block at independent setpoints) has requested the ECM to illuminate the MIL because of an emissions-relevant fault on its side. Original fault is in that module.",[["h","Internal fault — read the module DTCs"]],[],["medium",[80,1200]],"u"],"P25B0":["Fuel Level Sensor A Stuck","Fuel level sensor A (typically the float in the main fuel tank section) reports a value that does not change over a long driving distance — the float is mechanically stuck against the tank wall, baffle or pump module. Without level changes the EVAP monitor cannot run and remaining-range estimates are wrong.",[["h","Stuck float"],["m","Bent float arm catching the tank wall"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P25B1":["Fuel Level Sensor B Stuck","Same condition as sensor A stuck, applied to the second fuel level sensor B. Saddle tanks (often AWD vehicles) and large trucks use two sensors — one per tank chamber — averaged for total level.",[["h","Stuck float"]],[],["medium",[200,800]],"u"],"P25B2":["Fuel Level Sensor A or B Stuck","The ECM detects that one of the two level sensors is stuck but cannot identify which from the available signals — for example because the saddle-tank algorithm sees implausible delta only intermittently. Both sensors should be inspected.",[["h","One stuck float — inspect both"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"u"],"P25B3":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate A Stuck Open","Wastegate A is mechanically stuck open. Exhaust gas bypasses the turbine even at low load — turbo cannot reach target speed, boost is permanently low and the engine feels asthmatic.",[["h","Seized wastegate linkage"],["m","Broken return spring"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25B4":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate A Stuck Closed","Wastegate A is mechanically stuck closed. The turbo cannot bleed off exhaust at high load — boost overshoots the setpoint, risking overboost cut-off and damage to the turbo bearing.",[["h","Carbon-locked wastegate flap"],["m","Seized linkage"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25B5":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate B Stuck Open","Same as wastegate A stuck open, applied to the second wastegate (twin-turbo, sequential or two-stage). Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Seized wastegate linkage"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25B6":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate B Stuck Closed","Same as wastegate A stuck closed, applied to the second wastegate. Boost control tracks commanded vs.",[["h","Carbon-locked wastegate flap"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"],["l","Component wear with age - mechanical play"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25B7":["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit","General electrical fault on the auxiliary ignition switch On/Start input. Used on commercial vehicles or upfit applications where a second ignition switch (in a sleeper cab, work platform or crew compartment) can crank the engine.",[["h","Open or shorted wire"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P25B8":["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit Low","Auxiliary ignition switch On/Start input reads stuck low — short to ground or stuck-closed contact. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P25B9":["Auxiliary Ignition Switch On/Start Position Circuit High","Auxiliary ignition switch On/Start input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P25BA":["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit/Open","The DPF/SCR forced-regeneration request switch — used on commercial vehicles to let the operator force a parked regeneration when the automatic regen has been postponed too often — is open. The ECM cannot honour an operator request for forced regen.",[["h","Open switch wire"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"],["l","Cracked solder joint inside the module or sensor"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25BB":["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit Low","Regeneration control switch input reads stuck low — short to ground or stuck-closed contact. The ECM may see a constant regen request which it cannot service while the vehicle is moving.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Harness chafing through insulation"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25BC":["Regeneration Control Switch Circuit High","Regeneration control switch input reads stuck high — short to battery voltage. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Switch wire shorted to battery voltage"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25BD":["Unmetered Fuel - Forced Engine Shutdown","The engine controller commanded a forced shutdown after detecting unmetered fuel reaching the combustion chambers. Common on diesels with leaking turbo seals or cracked intercoolers that drip oil into the intake — the engine then runs on the oil and can overspeed.",[["h","Turbocharger oil seal leak feeds engine oil into the intake"],["m","Oil collected in the intercooler is sucked into the engine on load"],["m","Failed PCV / crankcase breather floods intake with oil mist"]],[],["hard",[400,4000]],"u"],"P25BE":["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the alternative-fuel disable line that switches a bi-fuel vehicle (CNG, LPG, hydrogen) back to gasoline. An open detected on the control side blocks the safety shutoff for the gas system.",[["h","Broken wire or corroded connector on the disable control line"],["m","Open coil in the alt-fuel disable relay"],["l","Output driver in the alt-fuel control module faulty"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P25BF":["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit High","Voltage on the alternative-fuel disable control line is above the expected window. Often a short to battery upstream of the relay or a stuck-on driver in the control module.",[["h","Disable control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Output driver stuck on inside the control module"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P25C0":["Alternative Fuel Disable Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the alternative-fuel disable control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a failed driver pulling the line low.",[["h","Disable control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Low-side driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P25C1":["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit","The feedback signal that confirms the alt-fuel disable command was carried out is missing or out of range. The fuel system cannot verify that the gas circuit is shut.",[["h","Open feedback wire between relay and control module"],["m","Feedback contact in the disable relay corroded or stuck"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"u"],"P25C2":["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit High","The disable feedback signal sits above its valid window. Typical cause is a short to battery on the feedback wire or a failed pull-up in the input stage.",[["h","Feedback wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["l","Pull-up resistor in the input stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P25C3":["Alternative Fuel Disable Signal Circuit Low","The disable feedback signal sits below its valid window. Usually a short to ground or an open pull-up that lets the input float low.",[["h","Feedback wire shorted to ground"],["l","Open pull-up resistor in the controller input"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,500]],"u"],"P25C4":["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit","The temperature sensor monitoring the electric brake booster (iBooster, eBooster) returns no usable signal. Without temperature feedback the controller derates booster assist to protect the motor.",[["h","Open sensor element or broken sensor wire"],["m","Corroded connector on the booster sensor pigtail"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25C5":["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","The booster temperature sensor reading is implausible relative to commanded assist or coolant temperature. The signal moves too slowly, sticks, or never reaches expected values during operation.",[["m","Sensor drift or contamination on the temperature element"],["m","Sensor not seated properly against the booster motor housing"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25C6":["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Low","The booster temperature signal is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Typical causes are a shorted sensor element or a short to ground in the harness.",[["h","Internal short in the sensor element"],["m","Sensor signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25C7":["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit High","The booster temperature signal is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Common causes are an open sensor or a short to a 5 V reference in the harness.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Sensor signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1200]],"u"],"P25C8":["Brake Booster Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The booster temperature signal jumps or drops out for short moments. Usually a loose connector or a chafed wire that opens during vibration or thermal expansion.",[["h","Sensor connector not fully seated or pin tension lost"],["m","Harness chafed against booster housing or pedal bracket"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P25C9":["Brake System Control Module B Requested MIL Illumination","A second brake system control module (typically the redundant secondary unit on by-wire or AV-grade brake systems) has signalled an emissions-relevant fault and requested the engine controller to switch on the MIL.",[["h","Active DTC stored in the secondary brake module"],["l","Communication loss interpreted as MIL request"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P25CA":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit / Open Bank 1","The controller cannot drive the park-lock pin that secures the intake camshaft phaser on bank 1 in its base position at engine off. Without the lock, the next start can suffer poor combustion or rough idle until the phaser builds oil pressure.",[["h","Open coil in the park-lock solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire between ECU and solenoid"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25CB":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low Bank 1","The intake camshaft park-lock control line on bank 1 is below the expected voltage window. Usually a short to ground or a low-side driver shorted internally.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","ECU low-side driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25CC":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High Bank 1","The intake camshaft park-lock control line on bank 1 is above the expected voltage window. Typical causes are a short to battery or a stuck-on driver in the controller.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25CD":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit / Open Bank 2","The controller cannot drive the park-lock pin that secures the intake camshaft phaser on bank 2 in its base position at engine off. Without the lock, the next start can suffer poor combustion or rough idle until the phaser builds oil pressure.",[["h","Open coil in the park-lock solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire between ECU and solenoid"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25CE":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low Bank 2","The intake camshaft park-lock control line on bank 2 is below the expected voltage window. Usually a short to ground or a low-side driver shorted internally.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","ECU low-side driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25CF":["Intake Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High Bank 2","The intake camshaft park-lock control line on bank 2 is above the expected voltage window. Typical causes are a short to battery or a stuck-on driver in the controller.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25D0":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit / Open Bank 1","The controller cannot drive the park-lock pin that secures the exhaust camshaft phaser on bank 1 in its base position at engine off. Without the lock, the next start can suffer poor combustion or rough idle until the phaser builds oil pressure.",[["h","Open coil in the park-lock solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire between ECU and solenoid"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25D1":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low Bank 1","The exhaust camshaft park-lock control line on bank 1 is below the expected voltage window. Usually a short to ground or a low-side driver shorted internally.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","ECU low-side driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25D2":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High Bank 1","The exhaust camshaft park-lock control line on bank 1 is above the expected voltage window. Typical causes are a short to battery or a stuck-on driver in the controller.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25D3":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit / Open Bank 2","The controller cannot drive the park-lock pin that secures the exhaust camshaft phaser on bank 2 in its base position at engine off. Without the lock, the next start can suffer poor combustion or rough idle until the phaser builds oil pressure.",[["h","Open coil in the park-lock solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire between ECU and solenoid"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25D4":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit Low Bank 2","The exhaust camshaft park-lock control line on bank 2 is below the expected voltage window. Usually a short to ground or a low-side driver shorted internally.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","ECU low-side driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25D5":["Exhaust Camshaft Actuator Park Lock Control Circuit High Bank 2","The exhaust camshaft park-lock control line on bank 2 is above the expected voltage window. Typical causes are a short to battery or a stuck-on driver in the controller.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1200]],"u"],"P25D6":["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Stop Performance","During self-calibration of the exhaust heat exchanger bypass valve A, the position sensor never reached the expected mechanical stop. The controller cannot zero the position reference, so commanded openings will be inaccurate.",[["h","Soot or carbon deposits prevent valve from reaching the stop"],["m","Worn linkage between actuator and valve flap"],["m","Position sensor not aligned with valve shaft"]],[],["hard",[250,1500]],"u"],"P25D7":["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit","A third fuel level sensor (C) used on multi-tank trucks, dual-saddle SUVs, or auxiliary fuel systems returns no usable signal. Without it, calculated fuel level and EVAP monitor enabling will be off.",[["h","Open sender resistor or broken float"],["m","Corroded tank pump module connector"]],[],["hard",[150,700]],"u"],"P25D8":["Fuel Level Sensor C Performance","The third fuel level sensor reading does not change as expected with consumption or refuelling. Float may be sticking, or the resistor track has localised wear.",[["h","Float arm stuck on baffle or fuel pump module"],["m","Worn spot on the resistor track at common fill level"]],[],["hard",[150,700]],"u"],"P25D9":["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit Low","The third fuel level sensor signal is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Usually a shorted sender or a short to ground in the harness.",[["h","Internal short in the sender resistor"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P25DA":["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit High","The third fuel level sensor signal is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Common causes are an open sender or a short to the 5 V reference.",[["h","Open sender resistor"],["m","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"u"],"P25DB":["Fuel Level Sensor C Circuit Intermittent","The third fuel level sensor signal jumps or drops out for short moments. Usually a loose connector or a chafed wire that opens during driving vibration.",[["h","Tank module connector not fully seated"],["m","Harness chafed near tank straps"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[60,350]],"u"],"P25DC":["Fuel Level Sensor C Stuck","The third fuel level sensor reads a constant value across known consumption or refuelling events. Float arm or resistor wiper is mechanically stuck.",[["h","Float arm jammed against tank wall, baffle or pump module"],["m","Resistor wiper seized by varnish from old fuel"]],[],["hard",[150,700]],"u"],"P25DD":["A Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position Bank 1","Camshaft phaser A on bank 1 will not unlock from its base position. The phaser stays at the park-lock angle and cannot be advanced or retarded as commanded.",[["h","Park-lock pin stuck in the locked groove"],["m","Low oil pressure cannot push the lock pin out"],["m","Oil control valve blocked by debris"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25DE":["A Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position Bank 1","Camshaft phaser A on bank 1 cannot reach its base position at engine shutdown so the lock pin never engages. Next cold start may run rough until oil pressure builds.",[["h","Worn vanes or housing inside the phaser"],["m","Sludge or contaminated oil prevents return to base"],["m","Oil control valve leaks internally"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25DF":["A Camshaft Position Control Performance Bank 1","Camshaft phaser A on bank 1 follows the commanded angle too slowly, oscillates, or shows steady-state error outside tolerance. Closed-loop control of cam timing is degraded.",[["h","Oil control valve spool sticks under varnish"],["m","Stretched timing chain shifts cam reference"],["m","Wrong oil viscosity slows phaser response"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P25E0":["A Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position Bank 2","Camshaft phaser A on bank 2 will not unlock from its base position. The phaser stays at the park-lock angle and cannot be advanced or retarded as commanded.",[["h","Park-lock pin stuck in the locked groove"],["m","Low oil pressure cannot push the lock pin out"],["m","Oil control valve blocked by debris"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E1":["A Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position Bank 2","Camshaft phaser A on bank 2 cannot reach its base position at engine shutdown so the lock pin never engages. Next cold start may run rough until oil pressure builds.",[["h","Worn vanes or housing inside the phaser"],["m","Sludge or contaminated oil prevents return to base"],["m","Oil control valve leaks internally"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E2":["A Camshaft Position Control Performance Bank 2","Camshaft phaser A on bank 2 follows the commanded angle too slowly, oscillates, or shows steady-state error outside tolerance. Closed-loop control of cam timing is degraded.",[["h","Oil control valve spool sticks under varnish"],["m","Stretched timing chain shifts cam reference"],["m","Wrong oil viscosity slows phaser response"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P25E3":["B Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position Bank 1","Camshaft phaser B on bank 1 will not unlock from its base position. The phaser stays at the park-lock angle and cannot be advanced or retarded as commanded.",[["h","Park-lock pin stuck in the locked groove"],["m","Low oil pressure cannot push the lock pin out"],["m","Oil control valve blocked by debris"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E4":["B Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position Bank 1","Camshaft phaser B on bank 1 cannot reach its base position at engine shutdown so the lock pin never engages. Next cold start may run rough until oil pressure builds.",[["h","Worn vanes or housing inside the phaser"],["m","Sludge or contaminated oil prevents return to base"],["m","Oil control valve leaks internally"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E5":["B Camshaft Position Control Performance Bank 1","Camshaft phaser B on bank 1 follows the commanded angle too slowly, oscillates, or shows steady-state error outside tolerance. Closed-loop control of cam timing is degraded.",[["h","Oil control valve spool sticks under varnish"],["m","Stretched timing chain shifts cam reference"],["m","Wrong oil viscosity slows phaser response"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P25E6":["B Camshaft Position - Stuck In Locked Position Bank 2","Camshaft phaser B on bank 2 will not unlock from its base position. The phaser stays at the park-lock angle and cannot be advanced or retarded as commanded.",[["h","Park-lock pin stuck in the locked groove"],["m","Low oil pressure cannot push the lock pin out"],["m","Oil control valve blocked by debris"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E7":["B Camshaft Position - Unable to Achieve Locked Position Bank 2","Camshaft phaser B on bank 2 cannot reach its base position at engine shutdown so the lock pin never engages. Next cold start may run rough until oil pressure builds.",[["h","Worn vanes or housing inside the phaser"],["m","Sludge or contaminated oil prevents return to base"],["m","Oil control valve leaks internally"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25E8":["B Camshaft Position Control Performance Bank 2","Camshaft phaser B on bank 2 follows the commanded angle too slowly, oscillates, or shows steady-state error outside tolerance. Closed-loop control of cam timing is degraded.",[["h","Oil control valve spool sticks under varnish"],["m","Stretched timing chain shifts cam reference"],["m","Wrong oil viscosity slows phaser response"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["hard",[150,1500]],"u"],"P25E9":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Stuck Open","The clutch that engages the mechanical supercharger to the engine drive will not close. The supercharger stays disengaged so boost from this stage is unavailable, which limits torque and may also affect cooling pump drives shared with the same belt.",[["h","Open electromagnetic clutch coil"],["m","Worn friction surfaces leave the air gap too large to attract"],["l","Corroded armature plate stuck open"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25EA":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Stuck Closed","The clutch that engages the mechanical supercharger to the engine drive will not open. The supercharger remains coupled at all loads, increasing parasitic loss and fuel consumption when boost is not needed.",[["h","Armature plate seized to the pulley face"],["m","Driver stuck on keeps clutch energised"],["l","Failed pulley bearing welds clutch surfaces"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25EB":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit Range/Performance","The supercharger clutch control current does not match the commanded value within tolerance. Either coil resistance has drifted or the driver feedback is implausible.",[["m","Coil resistance increased due to thermal damage"],["m","High-resistance contact in the clutch connector"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25EC":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit Low","Voltage on the supercharger clutch control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted clutch coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in the clutch coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25ED":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch Circuit High","Voltage on the supercharger clutch control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open coil that lets the driver float high.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open clutch coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25EE":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B / Open","The controller cannot drive the secondary electric vacuum pump (B). Brake servo or HVAC actuators that depend on engine vacuum may not get enough vacuum during low-load operation or with engine off in stop-start mode.",[["h","Open pump motor winding or worn brushes"],["m","Broken control wire between ECU and pump"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"u"],"P25EF":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B Range/Performance","The secondary vacuum pump does not produce the expected vacuum within the commanded run time. Leak in the pump line or worn pump diaphragm reduces output.",[["h","Worn diaphragm or vanes inside the pump"],["m","Cracked vacuum hose or loose connection"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P25F0":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B Low","Voltage on the secondary vacuum pump control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in pump motor winding"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"u"],"P25F1":["Vacuum Pump Control Circuit B High","Voltage on the secondary vacuum pump control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open motor that lets the driver float high.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open motor winding or worn brushes"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"u"],"P25F2":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit","A third boost pressure sensor (C) used on twin-stage or sequential boost systems returns no usable signal. Without it, boost control of the third stage runs open-loop or is disabled.",[["h","Open sensor element or broken signal wire"],["m","Corroded connector at sensor pigtail"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P25F3":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","The third boost pressure sensor reading is implausible compared with manifold pressure or commanded boost. Either drift, leak in the sensing line, or contamination on the sensor diaphragm.",[["m","Sensor drift after thermal aging"],["m","Sensing hose blocked by oil residue"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P25F4":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit Low","The third boost pressure sensor signal is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Usually a shorted sensor element or a short to ground.",[["h","Internal short in the sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P25F5":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor C Circuit High","The third boost pressure sensor signal is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Common causes are an open sensor or a short to the 5 V reference.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P25F6":["AIR System B","A general fault in the second secondary air injection (AIR) circuit. Detected by the O2 sensors which expect a lean swing during cold-start AIR pump operation but do not see one.",[["h","Failed AIR pump motor or impeller"],["m","Check valve seized by exhaust soot"],["m","Corroded or cracked air injection pipe"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25F7":["AIR System B Incorrect Flow Detected","The second AIR system delivers measurably more or less air than expected. Often a partially blocked pipe, a worn pump, or a leak between pump and check valve.",[["h","Air pipe partially blocked by carbon"],["m","Worn pump impeller reduces flow"],["m","Leak between pump and check valve"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25F8":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit","A third bypass (recirculation or wastegate) valve used in three-stage charging systems is not responding to control commands. Boost balancing across stages can no longer be achieved.",[["h","Open solenoid coil"],["m","Open or shorted wiring to the valve"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P25F9":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the third bypass valve control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in the solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[120,900]],"u"],"P25FA":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit High","Voltage on the third bypass valve control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[120,900]],"u"],"P25FB":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Control Circuit Range/Performance","The third bypass valve current does not match the commanded value within tolerance. Drifted coil resistance or high-resistance contact in the connector.",[["m","Coil resistance changed by thermal stress"],["m","High-resistance contact in the valve connector"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Charge status indicator shows fault","Charging may not start or interrupts","Slower-than-expected charge rate"],["medium",[120,900]],"u"],"P25FC":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C - Mechanical","The third bypass valve is mechanically jammed. Solenoid is energised correctly but the valve flap or disc does not move as expected.",[["h","Carbon buildup blocks the valve flap"],["m","Actuator linkage seized by corrosion"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25FD":["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Temperature Too High","The third bypass valve has reached over-temperature. Either coil duty cycle is too high for too long, or cooling air flow around the valve is restricted.",[["h","Sustained high duty cycle from charge balancing strategy"],["m","Cooling air channel blocked by debris"]],["Check engine light on","Significant power loss / limp mode","Possible blue or black smoke from exhaust"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P25FE":["Supercharger Disconnect Clutch","A general performance fault in the supercharger disconnect clutch. Engagement or release is slow, sticky, or out of tolerance without a clear electrical-side cause.",[["h","Worn friction surfaces or air gap drift"],["m","Oil or debris on the clutch face"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,2500]],"u"],"P25FF":["Electrical System Voltage Stabilizer Control Module Performance","The voltage stabiliser module (DC/DC converter for stop-start engine cranking events) does not maintain the regulated 12 V output during high transient loads. Sensitive electronics may reset during cranking.",[["h","Aged smoothing capacitors lose capacitance"],["m","Battery condition causes input voltage to drop too far"],["m","Internal fault in the converter switching stage"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P2600":["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the electric coolant pump A control line. Without circulation, engine and aftertreatment can overheat or warm up incorrectly.",[["h","Open pump motor winding"],["m","Broken control wire to the pump"]],[],["medium",[180,900]],"c"],"P2601":["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","The electric coolant pump A is commanded on but does not run. Coolant temperature climbs faster than expected with no flow detected.",[["h","Pump motor seized by debris or sediment"],["m","Cracked rotor magnet decouples drive"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P2602":["Coolant Pump Control Circuit Open","The ECU detects an open circuit on the electric coolant pump control line. Without pump control the engine cannot actively manage warm-up and cool-down phases.",[["h","Pump motor open"],["m","Drive line open"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2603":["Coolant Pump Control Circuit Low","The electric coolant pump drive line reads below the lower threshold — typically a short to ground or a failed driver stage.",[["h","Drive line shorted to ground"],["m","Driver stage failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2605":["Intake Air Heater B Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the secondary intake air heater (heater grid B) used on diesel engines for cold-start support. The grid stays cold so cold-start emissions and white smoke increase.",[["h","Open heater grid element"],["m","Failed heater relay or open coil"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2606":["Intake Air Heater B Circuit Range/Performance","The secondary intake air heater current does not match expected resistance. Either the grid is partially open or the relay contacts have high resistance.",[["h","Partial element failure raises grid resistance"],["m","Burned relay contacts"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P2607":["Intake Air Heater B Circuit Low","Voltage on the secondary intake air heater control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted relay coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in relay coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,500]],"c"],"P2608":["Intake Air Heater B Circuit High","Voltage on the secondary intake air heater control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open relay coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,500]],"c"],"P2609":["Intake Air Heater System Performance","The intake air heater system did not raise intake temperature by the expected amount during cold-start support. Suggests low current draw, poor connection to the grid, or a failed temperature feedback path.",[["h","High-resistance battery feed to the heater"],["m","Intake air temperature sensor reads with offset"]],[],["medium",[100,800]],"c"],"P260A":["PTO Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the power take-off (PTO) engagement line on commercial vehicles. The PTO will not engage even when commanded by the body controller or operator switch.",[["h","Open coil in the PTO engagement solenoid"],["m","Broken wire to the PTO solenoid"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P260B":["PTO Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the PTO engagement control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in the solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P260C":["PTO Control Circuit High","Voltage on the PTO engagement control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,700]],"c"],"P260D":["PTO Engaged Lamp Control Circuit","The dashboard PTO engaged lamp control circuit is faulty. Driver may not see whether the PTO is currently driving an external accessory.",[["h","Burnt-out indicator bulb"],["m","Open or shorted wire between cluster and ECU"]],[],["easy",[20,150]],"c"],"P260E":["Particulate Filter Regeneration Lamp Control Circuit","The DPF regeneration warning lamp circuit is faulty. The driver may not be alerted to a required highway run that supports passive regeneration.",[["h","Burnt-out indicator bulb"],["m","Open or shorted wire to the cluster"]],["Check engine light or DPF warning light on","Power loss / limp mode","Increased fuel consumption"],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P260F":["EVAP System Monitoring Processor Performance","The dedicated EVAP monitoring processor (often a small auxiliary CPU inside the engine controller or a separate module) does not pass its self-test or runs out of step with the main monitor logic.",[["h","Internal fault in the monitoring processor"],["m","Software memory corruption"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],["Check engine light on","Possible smell of fuel near tank or engine bay","Failed emissions inspection"],["hard",[400,1800]],"c"],"P2610":["ECM/PCM Internal Engine Off Timer Performance","The engine controller's internal soak-time/engine-off timer fails its plausibility check — for example readings claim instant cool-down or never-cooled. Cold-start enrichment, EVAP and catalyst monitors depend on this timer; a fault freezes those readiness monitors.",[["h","ECU internal timer fault"],["m","Keep-alive memory power intermittent"]],[],["hard",[80,1500]],"c"],"P2611":["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit / Open","The A/C refrigerant distribution valve A (used to switch refrigerant flow between front and rear evaporators or between cabin and battery cooling on EVs) cannot be driven by the controller.",[["h","Open coil in the valve solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2612":["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the A/C distribution valve A control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in the valve solenoid"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,1200]],"c"],"P2613":["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit High","Voltage on the A/C distribution valve A control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,1200]],"c"],"P2614":["Camshaft Position Output Circuit/Open","The camshaft position output signal sent from the ECU to other modules is interrupted. Other systems that rely on the cam reference (e.g.",[["h","Open output wiring"],["l","Internal ECU output driver fault"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2615":["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit Low Bank 1","The buffered camshaft A position output that the engine controller sends to other modules (transmission, body, ignition module) is below the expected level on bank 1. Other modules cannot use the cam phase reference for synchronisation.",[["h","Output wire shorted to ground"],["m","Output buffer transistor failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2616":["Camshaft A Position Signal Output Circuit High Bank 1","The buffered camshaft A position output is above the expected level on bank 1. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open output stage.",[["h","Output wire shorted to B+"],["m","Output buffer open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Power loss especially in mid-rpm range","Possible rough idle or stalling"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2617":["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit / Open","The buffered crankshaft position output that the engine controller sends to ignition modules and the transmission cannot drive its line. Open detected on the output side.",[["h","Open wire between ECU and downstream module"],["m","Output buffer internally open"]],[],["medium",[120,1000]],"c"],"P2618":["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit Low","The buffered crankshaft position output is below the expected level. Usually a short to ground on the output line or a failed buffer.",[["h","Output wire shorted to ground"],["m","Buffer transistor failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,1000]],"c"],"P2619":["Crankshaft Position Signal Output Circuit High","The buffered crankshaft position output is above the expected level. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open output stage.",[["h","Output wire shorted to B+"],["m","Output buffer open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,1000]],"c"],"P261A":["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the second electric coolant pump (B). Often used for aftertreatment, turbo cool-down, or hybrid battery loops — fault stops circulation in that loop.",[["h","Open pump motor winding"],["m","Broken control wire to the pump"]],[],["medium",[180,900]],"c"],"P261B":["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","The second electric coolant pump is commanded on but does not run. Cooling demand of the connected loop is not satisfied.",[["h","Pump motor seized by sediment"],["m","Cracked rotor magnet decouples drive"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[200,1000]],"c"],"P261C":["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the second coolant pump control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Motor winding short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P261D":["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit High","Voltage on the second coolant pump control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open motor winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P261E":["Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Stuck On","The second coolant pump runs even when no command is active. Driver is stuck on or the wire is shorted to a permanent supply.",[["h","ECU output driver stuck on"],["m","Control wire shorted to a permanent B+ supply"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"u"],"P261F":["Coolant Pump A Control Circuit Stuck On","The first coolant pump runs even when no command is active. Driver is stuck on or the wire is shorted to a permanent supply.",[["h","ECU output driver stuck on"],["m","Control wire shorted to a permanent B+ supply"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"u"],"P2620":["Throttle Position Output Circuit","A general electrical fault on the ECU output that broadcasts the throttle position signal to other modules — for example to the transmission control or hybrid drive controller.",[["h","Output wire open or shorted"],["m","ECU output stage failed"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2621":["Throttle Position Output Circuit Low","The buffered throttle position output that the engine controller sends to the transmission and body modules is below the expected level. Usually a short to ground or a failed output stage.",[["h","Output wire shorted to ground"],["m","Output buffer transistor failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2622":["Throttle Position Output Circuit High","The buffered throttle position output is above the expected level. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open output stage.",[["h","Output wire shorted to B+"],["m","Output buffer open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Reduced throttle response, possible limp mode","Hesitation or surging"],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2623":["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit / Open","The Injector Control Pressure (ICP) regulator on hydraulically actuated injectors (HEUI diesel) or the high-pressure regulator on common-rail systems cannot be driven. Injection pressure cannot be controlled, engine may not start.",[["h","Open coil in the pressure regulator"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["hard",[300,2500]],"c"],"P2624":["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit Low","Voltage on the ICP regulator control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted regulator coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in regulator coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"c"],"P2625":["Injector Control Pressure Regulator Circuit High","Voltage on the ICP regulator control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open regulator coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open regulator coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[200,2000]],"c"],"P2626":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open Bank 1 Sensor 1","The ECU detects an open in the pumping current trim circuit of the wide-band oxygen sensor on bank 1 sensor 1. Without trim correction, the lambda value reported by the sensor is not accurate.",[["h","Trim wire open"],["m","Internal sensor fault"],["l","Pin pushed back out of connector body"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P2627":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 1","On a wide-band (broadband) O2 sensor, the trim resistor circuit that calibrates the pumping current is reading low on bank 1 sensor 1. Air-fuel feedback gain is wrong, causing rich or lean offsets.",[["h","Short in the calibration trim resistor"],["m","Water intrusion in the sensor connector"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P2628":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 1","The wide-band trim resistor circuit on bank 1 sensor 1 reads high. Air-fuel feedback gain is wrong, causing offsets that the controller cannot compensate.",[["h","Open calibration trim resistor"],["m","Corroded sensor connector"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P2629":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit / Open Bank 2 Sensor 1","The wide-band trim resistor circuit on bank 2 sensor 1 is open. Air-fuel feedback for bank 2 cannot be calibrated, fuel control runs degraded.",[["h","Open calibration trim resistor"],["m","Open sensor connector pin"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P262A":["Fuel Injector - Pilot Injection Not Learned","The pilot (pre) injection learning routine on a common-rail diesel did not complete successfully. Without learned pilot quantity, combustion noise increases and NOx may rise.",[["h","Injector flow drift outside learning window"],["m","Unstable rail pressure during learning cycle"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[200,2500]],"u"],"P262B":["Control Module Power Off Timer Performance","The internal power-down timer of the engine controller does not run as expected. The module either stays awake too long after key-off (battery drain) or shuts down too early (no aftertreatment cool-down or learn-write).",[["m","Intermittent main relay opens early"],["m","Software timer counter corrupted"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P262C":["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit / Open","The 5 V reference G output that the engine controller supplies to a group of sensors is open. All sensors fed from this rail will report invalid readings.",[["h","Open wire on the reference rail"],["m","Open inside the ECU reference output"]],[],["medium",[120,1200]],"u"],"P262D":["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit Low","The 5 V reference G voltage is below the expected level. Usually a short to ground or excessive load from a downstream sensor pulling the rail down.",[["h","Reference wire shorted to ground"],["m","Sensor on the rail shorted internally to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,1200]],"u"],"P262E":["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit High","The 5 V reference G voltage is above the expected level. Typical causes are a short to battery or an internal regulator failure.",[["h","Reference wire shorted to a B+ supply"],["m","Internal 5 V regulator failed"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P262F":["Sensor Reference Voltage G Circuit Range/Performance","The 5 V reference G voltage is within range but unstable or offset against expected. Loose ground or marginal regulator load.",[["m","High-resistance ground for the reference rail"],["m","One sensor draws excessive current and shifts the rail"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[120,1000]],"u"],"P2630":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low Bank 2 Sensor 1","The wide-band trim resistor circuit on bank 2 sensor 1 reads low. Air-fuel feedback gain on bank 2 is wrong, causing rich or lean offsets.",[["h","Short in the calibration trim resistor"],["m","Water intrusion in the sensor connector"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P2631":["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High Bank 2 Sensor 1","The wide-band trim resistor circuit on bank 2 sensor 1 reads high. Air-fuel feedback gain on bank 2 is wrong, the controller cannot compensate the offset.",[["h","Open calibration trim resistor"],["m","Corroded sensor connector"],["l","Supply wire pinched against B+ source"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[150,600]],"c"],"P2632":["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the secondary fuel pump (B). Common on dual-tank trucks, GDI lift-pump systems, or alt-fuel installations — fault stops fuel delivery from this stage.",[["h","Open pump motor winding"],["m","Failed pump relay"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[200,1200]],"c"],"P2633":["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the second fuel pump control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in pump motor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[180,1000]],"c"],"P2634":["Fuel Pump B Control Circuit High","Voltage on the second fuel pump control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open motor winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[180,1000]],"c"],"P2635":["Fuel Pump A Low Flow / Performance","The ECU detects insufficient fuel flow from fuel pump A. Either the pump is worn out, the supply line is restricted, or the pressure regulator does not allow proper flow.",[["h","Worn fuel pump"],["m","Clogged fuel filter"],["l","Pressure regulator fault"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[150,700]],"c"],"P2636":["Fuel Pump B Low Flow/Performance","The second fuel pump runs but does not deliver expected volume or pressure. Worn pump, restricted filter, or leaking pressure regulator.",[["h","Worn impeller reduces volumetric efficiency"],["m","Restricted in-tank or in-line fuel filter"],["m","Pressure regulator leaks back to tank"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P2637":["Torque Management Feedback Signal A","The torque feedback signal A from the transmission or other torque user is missing or invalid. The engine controller cannot reduce torque on shift requests, which can cause harsh shifts.",[["h","Required CAN message not received in time"],["m","Source module reports an internal fault"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2638":["Torque Management Feedback Signal A Range/Performance","The torque feedback signal A is present but its value is implausible against measured engine load and speed. Sender calibration or sensor offset is suspected.",[["m","Sender calibration drift"],["m","Bus value corrupted by EMI"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2639":["Torque Management Feedback Signal A Low","The torque feedback signal A reads below its valid range. Either the source reports a value below physical possibility or the bus signal is stuck low.",[["h","Source module sends invalid low value"],["m","Signal stuck low on the bus"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P263A":["MIL Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the malfunction indicator lamp control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted bulb driver.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Bulb driver internally shorted"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P263B":["MIL Control Circuit High","Voltage on the malfunction indicator lamp control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open lamp.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Burnt-out MIL bulb"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[40,250]],"u"],"P263C":["Glow Plug Control Driver Performance","The glow plug control driver does not respond to commands within tolerance. Cold-start glow function is degraded so cold starting can be delayed and white smoke increases.",[["h","Aged driver shows degraded switching behaviour"],["m","Current feedback loop noisy"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P263D":["Reductant Heater Driver Performance","The reductant (AdBlue) tank or line heater driver does not switch as expected. AdBlue may freeze in cold weather, blocking SCR dosing.",[["h","Aged driver shows degraded switching behaviour"],["m","Heater element resistance drifted out of range"]],["Check engine light or NOx warning on","AdBlue/DEF level or quality warning","Possible no-start countdown after ignore period"],["hard",[300,2000]],"u"],"P263E":["Glow Plug Control Module 1 Over Temperature","The first glow plug control module reports over-temperature. Sustained current draw or insufficient cooling has driven the module above its rated temperature.",[["h","One glow plug shorted to ground forces module overcurrent"],["m","Cooling air channel blocked by debris"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["hard",[300,1800]],"u"],"P263F":["Glow Plug Control Module 2 Over Temperature","The second glow plug control module reports over-temperature. Sustained current draw or insufficient cooling has driven the module above its rated temperature.",[["h","One glow plug shorted to ground forces module overcurrent"],["m","Cooling air channel blocked by debris"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["hard",[300,1800]],"u"],"P2640":["Torque Management Feedback Signal A High","The torque feedback signal A reads above its valid range. Source module sends an implausibly high value or the bus signal is stuck high.",[["h","Source module sends invalid high value"],["m","Signal stuck high on the bus"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2641":["Torque Management Feedback Signal B","The torque feedback signal B from a second torque user is missing or invalid. The engine controller cannot coordinate torque reduction with this user.",[["h","Required CAN message not received in time"],["m","Source module reports an internal fault"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2642":["Torque Management Feedback Signal B Range/Performance","The torque feedback signal B is present but its value is implausible against measured engine load and speed. Sender calibration or sensor offset is suspected.",[["m","Sender calibration drift"],["m","Bus value corrupted by EMI"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2643":["Torque Management Feedback Signal B Low","The torque feedback signal B reads below its valid range. Source sends a value below physical possibility or the bus signal is stuck low.",[["h","Source module sends invalid low value"],["m","Signal stuck low on the bus"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2644":["Torque Management Feedback Signal B High","The torque feedback signal B reads above its valid range. Source sends an implausibly high value or the bus signal is stuck high.",[["h","Source module sends invalid high value"],["m","Signal stuck high on the bus"]],[],["medium",[150,1500]],"c"],"P2645":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit / Open Bank 1","The controller cannot drive the rocker arm switching actuator A on bank 1 (used in cylinder deactivation systems such as VTEC, AFM, MDS). The valve lift mode cannot be switched.",[["h","Open coil in oil control valve"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2646":["A Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off Bank 1","The rocker arm actuator A on bank 1 is commanded to engage (high lift or all-cylinder mode) but does not switch. Engine stays in low-lift or deactivated mode under load, causing reduced power.",[["h","Low oil pressure cannot move the actuator"],["m","Mechanical lock pin stuck in unactivated position"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["hard",[200,1800]],"c"],"P2647":["A Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On Bank 1","On variable valve lift systems (e.g. Honda VTEC) the ECU detects that the bank 1 rocker arm actuator is stuck in the engaged (high lift) position.",[["h","Insufficient oil pressure / level"],["m","Stuck VVL solenoid"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2648":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low Bank 1","Voltage on the rocker arm actuator A control line on bank 1 is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P2649":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High Bank 1","Voltage on the rocker arm actuator A control line on bank 1 is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P264A":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Bank 1","The position sensor that confirms the A rocker arm switching state on bank 1 returns no usable signal. Closed-loop control of valve lift cannot verify the state.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Corroded sensor connector"]],[],["hard",[180,1200]],"c"],"P264B":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1","The position sensor reading does not transition cleanly between the two valve lift modes on bank 1. Sensor drift or mechanical wear leaves the signal between expected values.",[["m","Sensor signal drift after thermal aging"],["m","Worn lock pin reduces travel between modes"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P264C":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1","The position sensor signal is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Usually a shorted sensor or short to ground in the harness.",[["h","Internal short in sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P264D":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","The position sensor signal is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Common causes are an open sensor or a short to the 5 V reference.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P264E":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic Bank 1","The position sensor signal jumps or drops out intermittently. Usually a loose connector or a chafed wire in the harness.",[["h","Sensor connector not fully seated"],["m","Harness chafed against valve cover or cam carrier"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P264F":["Engine Serial Number Not Programmed or Incompatible","The engine controller cannot read a valid engine serial number from its non-volatile memory, or the stored value does not match the expected pattern. Calibration sets keyed to the serial number cannot be applied.",[["h","Replacement ECU not programmed at install"],["m","Non-volatile memory corruption"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"u"],"P2650":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit / Open Bank 1","The controller cannot drive the rocker arm switching actuator B on bank 