etween modes"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P265C":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1","The position sensor signal for actuator B on bank 1 is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Internal short in sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P265D":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High Bank 1","The position sensor signal for actuator B on bank 1 is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P265E":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic Bank 1","The position sensor signal for actuator B on bank 1 jumps or drops out intermittently. Usually a loose connector or a chafed wire.",[["h","Sensor connector not fully seated"],["m","Harness chafed against valve cover"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P265F":["Variable A/C Compressor Control Circuit Range/Performance","The variable-displacement A/C compressor control valve does not respond to commands within tolerance. Refrigerant flow regulation is degraded so cabin temperature varies or efficiency drops.",[["h","Control valve spool sticky from oil residue"],["m","Solenoid coil resistance drift"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P2660":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit / Open Bank 2","The controller cannot drive the rocker arm switching actuator B on bank 2.",[["h","Open coil in oil control valve"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2661":["B Rocker Arm Actuator System Performance/Stuck Off Bank 2","The rocker arm actuator B on bank 2 is commanded to engage but does not switch.",[["h","Low oil pressure cannot move the actuator"],["m","Mechanical lock pin stuck in unactivated position"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["hard",[200,1800]],"c"],"P2662":["B Rocker Arm Actuator System Stuck On Bank 2","The rocker arm actuator B on bank 2 stays in the activated state when commanded off.",[["h","Mechanical lock pin stuck in activated position"],["m","Oil control valve spool stuck open"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["hard",[200,1800]],"c"],"P2663":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit Low Bank 2","Voltage on the rocker arm actuator B control line on bank 2 is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P2664":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Control Circuit High Bank 2","Voltage on the rocker arm actuator B control line on bank 2 is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["hard",[150,1200]],"c"],"P2665":["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the secondary fuel shutoff valve. Engine cannot be commanded off through this path during a safety event.",[["h","Open coil in shutoff valve"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["medium",[180,1000]],"c"],"P2666":["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the secondary fuel shutoff valve control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P2667":["Fuel Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit High","Voltage on the secondary fuel shutoff valve control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"c"],"P2668":["Fuel Mode Indicator Lamp Control Circuit","The fuel mode indicator lamp circuit (showing whether a bi-fuel vehicle currently runs on gasoline or alternative fuel) is faulty. Driver may not know the active fuel.",[["h","Burnt-out indicator bulb"],["m","Open or shorted wire to the cluster"]],[],["easy",[20,200]],"c"],"P2669":["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit / Open","The second power feed used to supply actuators (relays, solenoids, motor drivers) is open. All loads on this rail are powerless and report follow-on faults.",[["h","Blown fuse on the supply rail"],["m","Broken supply wire from main relay"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P266A":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Bank 2","The position sensor that confirms the A rocker arm switching state on bank 2 returns no usable signal.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Corroded sensor connector"]],[],["hard",[180,1200]],"c"],"P266B":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2","The position sensor reading does not transition cleanly between the two valve lift modes for actuator A on bank 2.",[["m","Sensor signal drift after thermal aging"],["m","Worn lock pin reduces travel between modes"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P266C":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low Bank 2","The position sensor signal for actuator A on bank 2 is below the lower diagnostic threshold. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Internal short in sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P266D":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High Bank 2","The position sensor signal for actuator A on bank 2 is above the upper diagnostic threshold. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P266E":["A Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic Bank 2","The position sensor signal for actuator A on bank 2 jumps or drops out intermittently. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Sensor connector not fully seated"],["m","Harness chafed against valve cover"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P266F":["A/C Refrigerant Distribution Valve A Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","The driver stage for the A/C refrigerant distribution valve A is in current limit or over-temperature. Sustained overload from a partially shorted load or excessive switching frequency.",[["h","Partial short in valve coil"],["m","Module overheating from poor cooling"]],[],["medium",[200,1500]],"u"],"P2670":["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit Low","The supply voltage to actuator group B (e.g. solenoids, valves driven by ECU) is below the calibrated threshold.",[["h","Faulty supply relay"],["m","Wire shorted to ground"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2671":["Actuator Supply Voltage B Circuit High","The second actuator supply rail is above the expected voltage. Likely a charging system overvoltage or a short to a higher-voltage source.",[["m","Alternator regulator failure"],["l","Wiring shorted to a higher-voltage circuit"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P2672":["Injection Pump Timing Offset","The high-pressure injection pump timing is offset from the expected reference. On distributor pumps with a timing solenoid, the actuator does not match the commanded position.",[["h","Worn timing actuator piston or seal"],["m","Stretched pump drive chain or belt"]],[],["hard",[400,3000]],"c"],"P2673":["Injection Pump Timing Calibration Not Learned","The injection pump timing learning routine did not complete successfully. Without learned values, injection timing runs from default tables and combustion is suboptimal.",[["h","Learning routine aborted by other DTC or unstable conditions"],["m","Timing actuator drift outside learning window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2674":["Injection Pump Fuel Calibration Not Learned","The injection pump fuel quantity calibration did not complete successfully. Without learned fuel calibration, AFR runs from default tables and emissions or smoke can rise.",[["h","Learning routine aborted by other DTC or unstable conditions"],["m","Fuel quantity solenoid drift outside learning window"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P2675":["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the air cleaner inlet control valve (warm-air or snorkel switching for cold-start emissions). Stuck in default position so cold-start fueling is sub-optimal.",[["h","Open coil in inlet valve solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["easy",[60,400]],"c"],"P2676":["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the air cleaner inlet valve control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,400]],"c"],"P2677":["Air Cleaner Inlet Control Circuit High","Voltage on the air cleaner inlet valve control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["easy",[60,400]],"c"],"P2678":["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the coolant degassing valve. Air pockets in the cooling system can form and cause local overheating.",[["h","Open coil in degassing valve"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P2679":["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the coolant degassing valve control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,600]],"c"],"P267A":["B Rocker Arm Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Bank 2","The position sensor that confirms the B rocker arm switching state on bank 2 returns no usable signal.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Corroded s