[80,400]],"c"],"P267F":["Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The internal temperature sensor of the control module shows intermittent jumps or dropouts. Module thermal protection may falsely activate or fail to activate when needed.",[["h","Cracked solder joint at internal sensor"],["l","Electromagnetic interference on sensor trace"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],[],["hard",[400,1500]],"u"],"P2680":["Coolant Degassing Valve Control Circuit High","Voltage on the coolant degassing valve control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[100,600]],"c"],"P2681":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the engine coolant bypass valve A. The valve usually routes coolant around the radiator during warm-up; without it warm-up takes longer and emissions during the warm-up phase rise.",[["h","Open coil in bypass valve solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["medium",[150,900]],"c"],"P2682":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the coolant bypass valve A control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2683":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Control Circuit High","Voltage on the coolant bypass valve A control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"c"],"P2684":["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit / Open","The third actuator supply rail is open. All loads on this rail are powerless and report follow-on faults.",[["h","Blown fuse on the supply rail"],["m","Broken supply wire from main relay"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"c"],"P2685":["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit Low","The third actuator supply rail is below the expected voltage. Battery weakness, blown fuse, or excessive current draw collapses the supply.",[["h","Load on the rail shorted to ground"],["m","Battery condition causes voltage to drop"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"c"],"P2686":["Actuator Supply Voltage C Circuit High","The third actuator supply rail is above the expected voltage. Likely a charging system overvoltage or a short to a higher-voltage source.",[["m","Alternator regulator failure"],["l","Wiring shorted to a higher-voltage circuit"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"c"],"P2687":["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the diesel fuel filter or supply line heater. In cold weather diesel waxing can clog the filter.",[["h","Open heater element"],["m","Failed heater relay"]],[],["medium",[80,500]],"c"],"P2688":["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the fuel supply heater control line is below the expected window. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Relay coil short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P2689":["Fuel Supply Heater Control Circuit High","Voltage on the fuel supply heater control line is above the expected window. The sensor heater warms the element to operating temperature (~600 °C); without it the lambda sensor stays inactive in closed loop and the ECM cannot trim mixture.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[80,400]],"c"],"P268A":["Fuel Injector Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","After injector replacement the engine controller did not receive the per-injector flow calibration codes (IMA, ISA, IMV). Cylinder balance and emissions are out of tolerance.",[["h","Injector calibration codes not entered after replacement"],["m","Wrong codes entered for the wrong cylinder positions"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[80,300]],"c"],"P268B":["High Pressure Fuel Pump Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","After high-pressure pump replacement the engine controller did not receive the pump-specific calibration data. Rail pressure regulation runs from default values.",[["h","Pump calibration codes not entered after replacement"],["m","Programming session aborted before completion"]],["Check engine light on","Hard start, no start, or stalling under load","Power loss especially at high load or rpm"],["medium",[80,300]],"c"],"P268C":["Cylinder 1 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 1 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software. Calibration was applied for the wrong injector type or family.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P268D":["Cylinder 2 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 2 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P268E":["Cylinder 3 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 3 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P268F":["Cylinder 4 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 4 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2690":["Cylinder 5 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 5 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2691":["Cylinder 6 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 6 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2692":["Cylinder 7 Injector Data Incompatible","The flow calibration data programmed for cylinder 7 injector does not match the format expected by the controller software.",[["h","Replacement injector has different part number than software expects"],["m","Calibration code format does not match controller version"]],[],["medium",[80,800]],"c"],"P2693":["Cylinder 8 Injector Data 