uces flow.",[["h","Coked nozzle restricts fuel delivery"],["m","Fuel pressure to the dosing line out of tolerance"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["hard",[300,2000]],"c"],"P2699":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Circuit Low","Voltage on the 7th injector control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in injector coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,1500]],"c"],"P269A":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Fuel Injector A Circuit High","Voltage on the 7th injector control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open solenoid coil.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open injector coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine light on","Misfire or rough idle on the affected cylinder","Increased fuel consumption"],["medium",[200,1500]],"c"],"P269B":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit / Open","The control line for the aftertreatment glow plug (used on some diesels to ignite injected HC during DPF regeneration) is open. Active regeneration cannot start.",[["h","Open coil in glow plug control relay"],["m","Broken control wire"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P269C":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Performance","The aftertreatment glow plug control responds to commands but the resulting current draw is out of tolerance. Worn glow plug or high-resistance contact.",[["h","Worn glow plug element raises resistance"],["m","Corroded connector at glow plug"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P269D":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the aftertreatment glow plug control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Relay coil short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[100,600]],"c"],"P269E":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Control Circuit High","Voltage on the aftertreatment glow plug control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[100,600]],"c"],"P269F":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit / Open","The aftertreatment glow plug element itself is open. No current flows even with the relay closed.",[["h","Glow element burnt out from age or HC overload"],["m","Corroded terminal at the plug body"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,600]],"c"],"P26A0":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Performance","The aftertreatment glow plug heats but exhaust temperature does not rise as expected. Combustion of injected HC may not start.",[["h","Aged glow plug heats slowly or unevenly"],["m","HC supply from 7th injector below required"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["hard",[200,1500]],"c"],"P26A1":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit Low","The aftertreatment glow plug current is below expected. Either the element is partially open or supply is undersized.",[["h","Partial element failure raises resistance"],["m","Supply voltage drops under load"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P26A2":["Exhaust Aftertreatment Glow Plug Circuit High","The aftertreatment glow plug current is above expected. Internal short reduces resistance.",[["h","Internal short in the glow plug element"],["l","Supply voltage above specification"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Glow plug warning light on (often orange coil symbol)","Hard cold start or no start in cold weather","White smoke from exhaust during warm-up"],["medium",[120,700]],"c"],"P26A3":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Range/Performance","The coolant bypass valve A responds to commands but the resulting coolant temperature behaviour is not as expected. Possibly stuck partially open or contaminated bore.",[["h","Valve partially stuck by sediment"],["m","Weak return spring fails to close fully"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P26A4":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit","The position sensor on the coolant bypass valve A returns no usable signal. Closed-loop control of bypass position is lost.",[["h","Open sensor element"],["m","Corroded sensor connector"]],[],["medium",[120,700]],"u"],"P26A5":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit 