ss valve A position sensor never reached the minimum mechanical stop. The position reference cannot be zeroed.",[["h","Sediment prevents valve from reaching minimum stop"],["m","Sensor not aligned with valve shaft"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P26AA":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Maximum Stop Performance","During self-calibration the bypass valve A position sensor never reached the maximum mechanical stop.",[["h","Sediment prevents valve from reaching maximum stop"],["m","Sensor not aligned with valve shaft"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P26AB":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve A Stuck/Open","The coolant bypass valve A is stuck in the open position. Coolant always bypasses the radiator, leading to overheating under load.",[["h","Valve seized open by sediment or wax"],["m","Broken return spring"]],[],["medium",[80,600]],"u"],"P26AC":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the second coolant bypass valve. The associated cooling sub-loop cannot be regulated.",[["h","Open coil in bypass valve solenoid"],["m","Broken control wire"]],[],["medium",[150,900]],"u"],"P26AD":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the second coolant bypass valve control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in solenoid coil"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"u"],"P26AE":["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Control Circuit High","Voltage on the second coolant bypass valve control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Con