e disabled until voltage is in spec.",[["m","Weak battery sags voltage under load"],["m","Alternator output out of regulation"]],[],["medium",[120,1000]],"u"],"P26EC":["Engine Sound Control B Circuit / Open","The second active sound generator (B) cannot be driven.",[["h","Open output stage in the sound amplifier"],["m","Broken control wire to amplifier"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P26ED":["Engine Sound Control B Circuit Low","Voltage on the sound generator B control line is below the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Amplifier input stage short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"u"],"P26EE":["Engine Sound Control B Circuit High","Voltage on the sound generator B control line is above the expected window. Wiring faults of this kind typically come from chafing, water ingress at connector seals, or pin push-back — a wiggle test on the harness while the code is active often confirms the location.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Amplifier input stage open"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[150,800]],"u"],"P26EF":["Engine Sound Control B Circuit Performance","The sound generator B circuit responds but the resulting acoustic feedback is not as expected.",[["h","Speaker cone damaged or coil shorted"],["m","Feedback microphone drifts"]],[],["medium",[150,1000]],"u"],"P26F0":["Starter Relay A Stuck On","The first starter relay stays closed when commanded off. Starter motor remains engaged after the engine is running, which can destroy the starter pinion or ring gear.",[["h","Relay contacts welded shut by inrush current"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["easy",[50,400]],"u"],"P26F1":["Starter Relay A Stuck Off","The first starter relay does not close when commanded on. Starter motor cannot crank, the engine will not start.",[["h","Burned relay contacts no longer make contact"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["easy",[50,400]],"u"],"P26F2":["Starter Relay B Stuck On","The second starter relay stays closed when commanded off. Starter motor B remains engaged after the engine is running, which can destroy the starter pinion or ring gear.",[["h","Relay contacts welded shut by inrush current"],["m","ECU output driver stuck on"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["easy",[50,400]],"u"],"P26F3":["Starter Relay B Stuck Off","The second starter relay does not close when commanded on. The associated starter motor cannot crank.",[["h","Burned relay contacts no longer make contact"],["m","Open relay coil"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],[],["easy",[50,400]],"u"],"P26F4":["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit / Open","The controller cannot drive the third electric coolant pump. Cooling demand of the connected loop (often hybrid power electronics or battery cooling) is not satisfied.",[["h","Open pump motor winding"],["m","Broken control wire to the pump"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P26F5":["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit Low","Voltage on the third coolant pump control line is below the expected window. Usually a short to ground or a shorted motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal short in pump motor winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[180,1000]],"u"],"P26F6":["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit High","Voltage on the third coolant pump control line is above the expected window. Typical causes are a short to battery or an open motor winding.",[["h","Control wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open motor winding"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],[],["medium",[180,1000]],"u"],"P26F7":["Coolant Pump C Supply Voltage Circuit","The dedicated supply voltage line to the third coolant pump module is faulty. Pump cannot operate without battery feed.",[["h","Blown fuse on supply line"],["m","High-resistance contact in supply harness"]],[],["medium",[60,600]],"u"],"P26F8":["Coolant Pump C Stuck/Stalled","The third coolant pump is commanded on but the rotor does not turn. Sediment, frozen coolant, or a foreign object jams the impeller.",[["h","Impeller jammed by sediment or debris"],["m","Pump motor seized by bearing failure"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P26F9":["Coolant Pump C Control Module Overtemperature","The smart controller of the third coolant pump has reached over-temperature. Sustained high duty or insufficient cooling air flow around the pump electronics.",[["h","Sustained high duty cycle from cooling demand"],["m","Cooling air channel around pump blocked by debris"]],[],["medium",[200,1200]],"u"],"P26FA":["Coolant Pump C Overspeed/Air in System","The third coolant pump speed feedback is higher than commanded with no resistance from coolant. Indicates air in the cooling loop or low coolant level so the pump spins free.",[["h","Low coolant level due to leak or improper fill"],["m","Air pocket trapped in the cooling loop"]],[],["easy",[30,300]],"u"],"P26FB":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Closed Bank 1","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 1 is stuck in the closed position. EGR gas always passes through the cooler, which slows engine warm-up and can degrade cold-start emissions.",[["h","Valve flap seized closed by soot"],["m","Actuator linkage jammed in closed position"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["hard",[250,1800]],"u"],"P26FC":["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Stuck Closed Bank 2","The EGR cooler bypass valve on bank 2 is stuck in the closed position. EGR gas always passes through the cooler, slowing engine warm-up and degrading cold-start emissions.",[["h","Valve flap seized closed by soot"],["m","Actuator linkage jammed in closed position"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine light on","Pinging or knocking under load","Power loss and hesitation"],["hard",[250,1800]],"u"],"P26FD":["A/C Compressor Internal Control Module Performance","The internal control module of an electrically driven A/C compressor (typical on hybrid and BEV vehicles) reports an internal performance fault. Compressor capacity may be reduced or shut down.",[["h","Internal fault in compressor inverter electronics"],["m","Software error in compressor control logic"],["l","Module software outdated, reflash may resolve"]],["Check engine light on","Possible limp mode or no-start","Multiple follow-up faults across modules"],["hard",[800,3500]],"u"],"P26FE":["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Control Performance","The exhaust flow control valve A responds to commands but the resulting flow or back-pressure does not match expectations. Worn flap or carbon coking on the bore.",[["h","Worn valve flap loses sealing"],["m","Carbon coking restricts valve travel"]],[],["hard",[200,1500]],"u"],"P26FF":["Auto Configuration Throttle Input Not Present Bank 2","During controller auto-configuration the expected throttle input on bank 2 was not detected. Configuration cannot complete and the second throttle path cannot be used.",[["h","Broken signal wire from throttle B2"],["m","Hardware variant mismatch — sensor not installed"]],[],["medium",[120,800]],"u"],"P2700":["Transmission Friction Element A Apply Time Range/Performance","The transmission control module measured an apply time for friction element A (clutch or band) outside the calibrated window. Indicates worn clutch material, low line pressure, or a degrading shift solenoid.",[["h","Clutch pack worn"],["m","Shift solenoid response degraded"],["m","Line pressure too low"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,4500]],"c"],"P2701":["Transmission Friction Element B Apply Time Range/Performance","The time required to apply friction element B (a clutch or band inside the automatic transmission) is outside the expected window. Either too long (worn clutch, low pressure) or too short (sticky valve, mis-calibration).",[["h","Worn clutch friction plates"],["m","Pressure control solenoid drift"],["m","Internal hydraulic leak in apply circuit"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2702":["Transmission Friction Element C Apply Time Range/Performance","The time required to apply friction element C is outside the expected window. Worn clutch, low pressure, or sticky valve.",[["h","Worn clutch friction plates"],["m","Pressure control solenoid drift"],["m","Internal hydraulic leak in apply circuit"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2703":["Transmission Friction Element D Apply Time Range/Performance","The time required to apply friction element D is outside the expected window.",[["h","Worn clutch friction plates"],["m","Pressure control solenoid drift"],["m","Internal hydraulic leak in apply circuit"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,4000]],"c"],"P2704":["Transmission Friction Element E Apply Time Range/Performance","The time required to apply friction element E is outside the expected window.",[["h","Worn clutch friction plates"],["m","Pressure control solenoid drift"],["m","Internal hydraulic leak in apply circuit"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,4000]],