ne or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[400,1800]],"u"],"P28EF":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Performance/Stuck Off","The engine disconnect clutch actuator is commanded to engage but does not produce the expected motion. Actuator stuck in disengaged position.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck off"],["m","Hydraulic engagement pressure lost"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F0":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Stuck On","The engine disconnect clutch actuator stays in the engaged state when release is commanded. Pure electric driving is not available.",[["h","Actuator mechanically stuck on"],["m","Release pressure path blocked"],["l","Carbon or debris buildup preventing free movement"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F1":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit","The hybrid control module detects a generic fault on the engine disconnect clutch pressure sensor circuit. Engagement pressure cannot be monitored reliably.",[["h","Pressure sensor failed"],["m","Wiring or connector fault"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F2":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","The engine disconnect clutch pressure signal does not match plausibility checks against actuator commands. Sensor drift or installation offset.",[["h","Sensor zero point drifted"],["m","Sensor mounting loose - bias offset"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F3":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Voltage on the engine disconnect clutch pressure sensor signal line is below the expected window. Wire shorted to ground or sensor short.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to ground"],["m","Internal sensor short"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F4":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit High","Voltage on the engine disconnect clutch pressure sensor signal line is above the expected window. Wire shorted to B+ or sensor open.",[["h","Signal wire shorted to B+"],["m","Open pressure sensor"],["l","Connector pins corroded - high contact resistance"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F5":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The engine disconnect clutch pressure sensor signal drops out or jumps intermittently. Loose connector or noisy ground reference.",[["h","Sensor connector not seated"],["m","Noisy ground reference"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F6":["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit Intermittent","The control circuit of the engine disconnect clutch actuator drops out intermittently. Loose connector or vibration-sensitive wiring.",[["h","Actuator connector not seated"],["m","Harness chafing intermittently shorts the wire"],["l","Connector with intermittent contact under vibration"]],["Check engine or transmission warning light on","Harsh, delayed, or missing shifts","Possible limp mode (locked in one gear)"],["hard",[500,2800]],"u"],"P28F7":["Exhaust Pressure Too High Bank 1","The exhaust pressure measured on bank 1 exceeds the calibrated maximum. Common causes are clogged DPF, restricted exhaust path, or stuck exhaust brake/back-pressure valve.",[["h","DPF clogged with soot or ash"],["m","Back-pressure valve stuck closed"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"u"],"P28F8":["Exhaust Pressure Too High Bank 2","The exhaust pressure measured on bank 2 exceeds the calibrated maximum. Common causes are clogged DPF, restricted exhaust path, or stuck exhaust brake/back-pressure valve.",[["h","DPF clogged with soot or ash"],["m","Back-pressure valve stuck closed"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"u"],"P28F9":["Exhaust Pressure Too Low Bank 1","The exhaust pressure measured on bank 1 falls below the calibrated minimum. Common causes are leaks upstream of the sensor, missing DPF substrate, or sensor calibration drift.",[["h","Exhaust leak upstream of sensor"],["m","Sensor zero point drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"u"],"P28FA":["Exhaust Pressure Too Low Bank 2","The exhaust pressure measured on bank 2 falls below the calibrated minimum. Common causes are leaks upstream of the sensor, missing DPF substrate, or sensor calibration drift.",[["h","Exhaust leak upstream of sensor"],["m","Sensor zero point drifted"]],[],["medium",[200,2500]],"u"],"P2A00":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 1","O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 1: the signal is implausible or outside the valid range.",[["h","Oxygen sensor aging"],["m","Sensor contamination (oil, silicone)"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2A01":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 2","The rear oxygen sensor on bank 1 does not show the expected slow steady-state behaviour after the catalyst. Either the sensor is degraded or the catalyst itself behaves abnormally.",[["h","Sensor aging"],["m","Catalyst aging"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2A02":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 3","The optional third oxygen sensor on bank 1 (typically downstream of a second catalyst) returns implausible values during long-term monitoring.",[["h","Sensor aging"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"],["l","Sensor mounting loose - signal damping"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2A03":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 1","The front oxygen sensor on bank 2 reacts too slowly or shows insufficient signal swing during closed-loop fuel control.",[["h","Sensor aging"],["m","Sensor contamination"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2A04":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 2","The rear oxygen sensor on bank 2 shows abnormal behaviour during long-term plausibility evaluation. Often a sign of an aged sensor or weakened catalyst.",[["h","Sensor aging"],["m","Catalyst aging"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,400]],"c"],"P2A05":["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 3","The third oxygen sensor on bank 2 (after a second catalyst stage on some vehicles) returns implausible values. Often related to sensor aging or mechanical exhaust leak upstream.",[["h","Sensor aging"],["m","Exhaust leak upstream"],["l","Sensor element aged beyond calibration window"]],["Check engine light on","Increased fuel consumption","Possible rough idle or hesitation"],["medium",[120,500]],"c"],"P2A08":